# Talk with a resident (Docs/Design/83-dialogue-trees.md): Talk on the wheel opens the dialogue window on the
# resident's hub. Free talk is built in: the player may say something of their own at any node marked `free`, and the
# resident replies in the window (the NPC Mind when it is connected, else the window's own understanding of the words:
# Data/Voice/understand.json, doc 84 §13.5-13.6). A choice's words are a default line the player may send as written or
# rewrite, so every choice is written as the player's own speech, the ways about and out too ("Goodbye for now.", "I was
# wondering about something else...": the user, 2026-11-20). The resident's lines are talk concepts
# (dlg.resident.<node>); a mantle's own lines there are the wearer's (doc 84 §13.4.1), the tree's the floor.
#
# The hub (doc 84 §13.4.3, Phase 13): the role's links where there are any (the wares, work or a Chapter's missions, a
# trade to learn), the news, "I want to know more about something..." (the `about` node), the player's name given or the
# resident's asked, up to two things the player has heard that they might bring up (the claim store), goodbye. Never
# more than nine choices: the loader counts them (Library::mostShown), and a wearer's grafts fill what room is left (the
# rest go under `about`). The other roles' trees go on here through `do open chat` ("I was wondering about something
# else..."), and the news and the ways are this tree's for every role (`do open news`, `do open way`).
#
# Greetings by meeting and disposition (doc 84 §13.4.4): returning (back after a long while, doc 56, 10), famous (its
# deeds heard of, doc 56, 5), hostile and wary. And the ledger's callback (§13.4.7): a way asked a while back.
#
# Facts from the world (Core/RatwGameDialogue.cpp, dialogueRoleFacts; Core/RatwGameWindowTalk.cpp, windowFacts):
# here.folk, here.shops and here.inns (the town's residents, shops and inns), here.district (the House whose district
# this is); here.gossip and topic.subject, topic.claim, topic.claim_kind (the freshest thing the resident has heard of
# someone else, a week old at most); here.places and each place (topic.place_title, place_kind, place_way); here.troubles
# and each trouble; here.opinions (the issues the resident holds a view on), here.kin (their living family),
# here.people (residents the player may ask after), here.heard (what the player might bring up), here.quirk_words,
# here.hours, here.matchmaker, here.vouched, here.letter, here.festival_won, here.records; player.named and player.met.

tree resident
entry talk hub
entry chat hub
entry news news
entry way way
entry introduce introduced

node hub
say #greet#. #talk_open# | #talk_open#
say[topic.meeting=known] #greet#, #topic.player#. #talk_open# | #topic.player#. #talk_open#
say[here.time=night] It's late. #talk_open#
say[here.came_in=yes] #greet#. Come in, come in. #talk_open# | #greet#. In you come. #talk_open#
say[topic.meeting=returning priority=6] Well, well. I've not seen you since #topic.since#. #talk_open# | Look who it is. Not since #topic.since#! #talk_open#
say[topic.meeting=famous priority=6] You #topic.deed#, didn't you? Folk talk of it still. #talk_open# | So you're the one who #topic.deed#. #talk_open#
say[topic.meeting=famous_look priority=6] You look like the one who #topic.deed#. Are you? #talk_open# | I've heard of a wolf like you, who #topic.deed#. #talk_open#
say[pair.disposition=wary priority=3] Yes? | What is it you want? | #greet#. What do you want?
say[pair.disposition=hostile priority=10] You. Say what you want and go. | What now? | I've nothing to say to you.
say[player.asked=way priority=10] You asked me the way to #here.way_asked# a while back. Find it? | Did you find #here.way_asked#, in the end?
say[player.asked=person priority=10] Did you find #here.person_asked#, that time you asked? | You were after #here.person_asked#. Find them?
# ---- The Ninth Howl: the cast's own greetings (Docs/Design/86 section 6; cast-and-talk.md section 3). Each is
# gated on talk memory the campaign writes (world.mem, self.mem, pair.mem), so none plays until a key is set.
# rmx_brenna_abbot
say[self.id=rmx_brenna_abbot world.mem.nh_stage=king priority=4] #greet#. I'll read what's to be read when I'm sure of it. Not before. A herald who guesses is just a loud wolf.
say[self.id=rmx_brenna_abbot world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called priority=4] #greet#. I read it, and I'd read it again. A Moot of the nine voices. Every Keeper's taking pledges now. I'm taking this town's.
say[self.id=rmx_brenna_abbot world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning priority=4] I've a note myself, due at the new moon. I'll pay it in coin or not at all. Not in my voice.
say[self.id=rmx_brenna_abbot world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.mem.nh_debt=freed priority=4] My note's paid. A wolf of the road worked it off and wouldn't take a penny. I'll read their deed if they let me.
say[self.id=rmx_brenna_abbot world.mem.nh_stage=signals priority=4] Every notice I pin, the grey paw-mark pins one over it. I've started carrying two hammers.
say[self.id=rmx_brenna_abbot world.mem.nh_stage=howls priority=4] A Moot needs nine howls, and half the square sang the burying one at the feast. Who remembers how?
say[self.id=rmx_brenna_abbot world.mem.nh_stage=letters priority=4] Forty letters for a lord who is never home. I'll cry the ones their senders want cried.
say[self.id=rmx_brenna_abbot world.mem.nh_stage=lights priority=4] The Houses want the Moot gone before it ever sits. They'll have to shout louder than a herald.
say[self.id=rmx_brenna_abbot world.mem.nh_stage=harvest priority=4] I read out the ford's news every hour, three nights running. My voice is going. Theirs mustn't.
say[self.id=rmx_brenna_abbot world.mem.nh_stage=bell world.mem.nh_writ=whispered priority=4] Something was read in the Rain Hall before the old King went up. I'd give my horn to know what.
say[self.id=rmx_brenna_abbot world.mem.nh_stage=bell world.mem.nh_writ=read priority=4] I read it on the square at noon. My paws shook. The writ didn't.
say[self.id=rmx_brenna_abbot world.mem.nh_stage=moot priority=4] I'll read every voice as it comes in off the Line. Make sure yours comes.
say[self.id=rmx_brenna_abbot world.mem.nh_stage=moot world.mem.nh_moot=midwinter priority=4] The Midwinter Moot. I'll read every voice as it comes in off the Line, frost or no frost. Make sure yours comes.
say[self.id=rmx_brenna_abbot world.mem.nh_crown=regency priority=5] Speaker of the Moot. It's a herald who's allowed to answer back.
say[self.id=rmx_brenna_abbot world.mem.nh_crown=ottilie|lamp|bought priority=5] I read the Moot's verdict. Now I read the new orders. Same steps, same horn.
# rm_ottilie_harrowgate
say[self.id=rm_ottilie_harrowgate world.mem.nh_stage=king priority=4] #greet#. Forgive me, I'm carrying the old King's petitions still. Nobody's told me who to give them to.
say[self.id=rm_ottilie_harrowgate world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called priority=4] A Moot. The old King would have liked that. He never trusted a room with only Houses in it.
say[self.id=rm_ottilie_harrowgate world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning priority=4] They've offered to pay every small note in the Sump. With a hook in it, I expect.
say[self.id=rm_ottilie_harrowgate world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning|signals world.mem.nh_loan=taken priority=4] The notes are paid and the Crown owes the Counting House. The old King would have hated that. So do I.
say[self.id=rm_ottilie_harrowgate world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning|signals world.mem.nh_loan=refused priority=4] I refused it. Now free them, please. I've told the whole Residence you will.
say[self.id=rm_ottilie_harrowgate world.mem.nh_stage=signals priority=4] The City Office says my petitions are mislaid. All of them. Again.
say[self.id=rm_ottilie_harrowgate world.mem.nh_stage=howls priority=4] It's only the damp. It's always only the damp.
say[self.id=rm_ottilie_harrowgate world.mem.nh_stage=howls|letters|lights world.mem.nh_cough=tended priority=4] I climbed the Hundred Steps without stopping. Someone was kind, and I noticed.
say[self.id=rm_ottilie_harrowgate world.mem.nh_stage=letters priority=4] Half my petitions went to the Grayrock lord by mistake, they say. Forty letters, and mine among them.
say[self.id=rm_ottilie_harrowgate world.mem.nh_stage=lights priority=4] The Houses are at each other, and the Council writes to me about my manners.
say[self.id=rm_ottilie_harrowgate world.mem.nh_stage=harvest priority=4] I've sent what the household can spare to the ford. It isn't much. The Queen counted it twice.
say[self.id=rm_ottilie_harrowgate world.mem.nh_stage=bell world.mem.nh_writ=whispered priority=4] Something was read in the Rain Hall before the old King went up. Nobody will tell his daughter what.
say[self.id=rm_ottilie_harrowgate world.mem.nh_stage=bell world.mem.nh_writ=read priority=4] It passes over me in plain words. Good. I'd rather be passed over by the old King than by the Houses.
say[self.id=rm_ottilie_harrowgate world.mem.nh_stage=moot priority=4] If the realm wants a Harrowgate, it shall have one who carries her own petitions.
say[self.id=rm_ottilie_harrowgate world.mem.nh_crown=ottilie priority=5] I'm told a queen may not carry her own petitions. I've told them she may.
say[self.id=rm_ottilie_harrowgate world.mem.nh_crown=lamp priority=5] He asked me to keep the petitions. I said I'd never stopped.
say[self.id=rm_ottilie_harrowgate world.mem.nh_crown=regency priority=5] The Moot will hear petitions every time it sits. I'll be first in line.
say[self.id=rm_ottilie_harrowgate world.mem.nh_crown=bought priority=5] I carry petitions to a Protector now. He reads them faster. I don't like what he writes.
# rm_oda_harrowgate
say[self.id=rm_oda_harrowgate self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_stage=king priority=4] Every penny counted twice and the wake still short. The Houses lend with one paw and take with the other.
say[self.id=rm_oda_harrowgate self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called priority=4] A Moot, and a patrolman keeping the King's lamp. What next, I wonder?
say[self.id=rm_oda_harrowgate self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning priority=4] Someone in my kitchens is too rich by half. I can smell new coin on a servant.
say[self.id=rm_oda_harrowgate self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_stage=signals|howls|letters|lights|harvest priority=4] The purse is thin and the Houses are fat. That's the realm, #address#.
say[self.id=rm_oda_harrowgate self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_stage=bell world.mem.nh_writ=whispered priority=4] The Chancellor won't meet my eye. Forty years at court, I know a wolf who's hiding a paper.
say[self.id=rm_oda_harrowgate self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_stage=bell world.mem.nh_writ=read priority=4] It passes over my girl in plain words. Well. Plain words can be argued with.
say[self.id=rm_oda_harrowgate self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_stage=moot world.mem.nh_oda=contest priority=4] I'll fight for her at the Moot. I'd fight dirty for most things. For her, I'll fight clean.
say[self.id=rm_oda_harrowgate self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_stage=moot world.mem.nh_oda=accept priority=4] I keep the roll beside the Speaker. I can count. It's what I'm for.
say[self.id=rm_oda_harrowgate self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_crown=ottilie priority=5] My girl, the Queen. I can rest at last.
say[self.id=rm_oda_harrowgate self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_crown=lamp|regency|bought priority=5] I'll go home to the lake when the roads are good. Luck to the lot of you.
say[self.id=rm_oda_harrowgate self.from=coldwater pair.mem.nh_spy=told_queen priority=5] You told me about the girl in my kitchens. I've not forgotten. I never forget.
# rm_ambrose_greatly
say[self.id=rm_ambrose_greatly world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called priority=4] #greet#. A sad season. The Counting House has sent flowers to the Residence, and an account for them.
say[self.id=rm_ambrose_greatly world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning priority=4] #greet#. A city that pays what it owes. You'd be surprised how few wolves want that.
say[self.id=rm_ambrose_greatly world.mem.nh_stage=signals priority=4] Roads closed are roads unpaid. I regret it, of course. I regret most things at a fair rate.
say[self.id=rm_ambrose_greatly world.mem.nh_stage=howls priority=4] Nine howls. I've counted them. Some of them are mine.
say[self.id=rm_ambrose_greatly world.mem.nh_stage=letters priority=4] The Grayrock lord is coming home, I hear. He'll find his ledgers in order. I've seen to several.
say[self.id=rm_ambrose_greatly world.mem.nh_stage=lights priority=4] Quarrels are expensive. I lend to both sides; it keeps them civil.
say[self.id=rm_ambrose_greatly world.mem.nh_stage=harvest priority=4] Grain at siege price is still grain at a price. Someone must buy it.
say[self.id=rm_ambrose_greatly world.mem.nh_stage=bell priority=4] The Rain Hall is shut for repairs. Repairs are expensive. I've lent for those as well.
say[self.id=rm_ambrose_greatly world.mem.nh_stage=bell world.mem.nh_oskar=confessed|exposed|fled|paid priority=4] The Chancellor has been talking. Chancellors do. It passes.
say[self.id=rm_ambrose_greatly world.mem.nh_stage=moot priority=4] Count the voices, by all means. I've already counted mine.
say[self.id=rm_ambrose_greatly world.mem.nh_stage=signals|howls|letters|lights|harvest|bell world.mem.nh_ledger=shown priority=4] My girl reads well. Too well. She sleeps at the abbey now, which is cheaper.
say[self.id=rm_ambrose_greatly world.mem.nh_stage=signals|howls|letters|lights|harvest|bell world.mem.nh_ledger=kept priority=4] We came to terms, the girl and I. I keep my terms.
say[self.id=rm_ambrose_greatly world.mem.nh_stage=howls|letters|lights|harvest|bell|moot world.mem.nh_lists=sold priority=4] The Watch is in good paws now. Mine, I mean.
say[self.id=rm_ambrose_greatly world.mem.nh_crown=bought priority=5] The realm is in good order. It owes me, and it knows it.
say[self.id=rm_ambrose_greatly world.mem.nh_crown=ottilie|lamp|regency priority=5] The Moot has spoken. I'll send it my account.
say[self.id=rm_ambrose_greatly pair.mem.nh_purse=marked priority=5] Ah. One of ours. The Counting House remembers its friends, and its rates.
# rm_rosalind_greatly
say[self.id=rm_rosalind_greatly world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning priority=4] Three sums, and none of them agree. Someone's counting twice, and I think I know whose paw it is.
say[self.id=rm_rosalind_greatly world.mem.nh_stage=signals|howls|letters|lights|harvest|bell world.mem.nh_ledger=shown priority=4] I sleep at the abbey now. The beds are hard and the books are honest.
say[self.id=rm_rosalind_greatly world.mem.nh_stage=signals|howls|letters|lights|harvest|bell world.mem.nh_ledger=kept priority=4] Father bargained. I wasn't in the room. I never am.
say[self.id=rm_rosalind_greatly world.mem.nh_stage=signals|howls|letters|lights|harvest|bell world.mem.nh_ledger=ash priority=4] Burned. Good. Some things are safer in two heads than in one ledger.
say[self.id=rm_rosalind_greatly world.mem.nh_stage=bell pair.mem.nh_ledger=ash priority=5] You burned it for me. I've written something down for you. Read it alone.
say[self.id=rm_rosalind_greatly world.mem.nh_stage=moot priority=4] If they crown me, I'll read every ledger in the realm. Father should be careful what he wishes for.
say[self.id=rm_rosalind_greatly world.mem.nh_crown=bought priority=5] Crowned for a sum I didn't add. I'll audit the crown first.
say[self.id=rm_rosalind_greatly world.mem.nh_crown=ottilie|lamp|regency priority=5] The ledgers are open now. Some of them, anyway. I'm reading the rest.
# rm_gerrit_mudhand
say[self.id=rm_gerrit_mudhand world.mem.nh_stage=king priority=4] #greet#. An old wolf's note in a lamp-book is not law. I said so on the square and I'll say it here.
say[self.id=rm_gerrit_mudhand world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called priority=4] A Moot, then. By the forge and the sea, the Council will need a bigger table.
say[self.id=rm_gerrit_mudhand world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning priority=4] I keep the Moot's roll now. A Moot needs friends who aren't Houses. Back it, and I'll write your name in.
say[self.id=rm_gerrit_mudhand world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning world.mem.nh_ledger=shown priority=4] A ledger came to the Antechamber. I've read it four times. By the forge and the sea.
say[self.id=rm_gerrit_mudhand world.mem.nh_stage=signals priority=4] Every House says the lists are forged. Every House is lying, or none is.
say[self.id=rm_gerrit_mudhand world.mem.nh_stage=howls priority=4] Nine howls, the herald says. I've a roll with nine lines on it and not one name written yet.
say[self.id=rm_gerrit_mudhand world.mem.nh_stage=letters priority=4] The Grayrock seat's been empty six years. If the lord sits, the Council's whole. I'd almost like that.
say[self.id=rm_gerrit_mudhand world.mem.nh_stage=lights priority=4] Petitions on every desk to unseat the lamp-keeper. I've put them in a drawer. A deep one.
say[self.id=rm_gerrit_mudhand world.mem.nh_stage=harvest priority=4] The Council sits every night the ford holds. Mostly it argues about who pays for the lamps.
say[self.id=rm_gerrit_mudhand world.mem.nh_stage=bell world.mem.nh_writ=whispered priority=4] I saw him weep. I've said nothing for a season. I'm tired of nothing.
say[self.id=rm_gerrit_mudhand world.mem.nh_stage=bell world.mem.nh_writ=read priority=4] It's read. I'd have read it myself, years ago, if anyone had let me near it.
say[self.id=rm_gerrit_mudhand world.mem.nh_stage=moot priority=4] I keep the roll. Every voice, as it comes. The Council will hear it whether it likes it or not.
say[self.id=rm_gerrit_mudhand world.mem.nh_crown=ottilie|lamp|regency|bought priority=5] Speaker of the Council still. Fewer shouting matches. More counting.
# cty_ulric_stonevein
say[self.id=cty_ulric_stonevein self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called|reckoning priority=4] #greet#. Nothing to say, cousin. The mine's short and the road's long.
say[self.id=cty_ulric_stonevein self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_stage=signals priority=4] Lamp-black and old snow. I know that scent. I buried it, I thought.
say[self.id=cty_ulric_stonevein self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_stage=howls priority=4] Our gathering howl goes lower than the warning one. Lower than you'd think a wolf could go.
say[self.id=cty_ulric_stonevein self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_stage=letters priority=4] Black cloaks came down the Pass. Didn't take their boots off. Deep strange.
say[self.id=cty_ulric_stonevein self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_stage=lights|harvest priority=4] The Captain's a Deepvein wolf. I'd stake my stones on it.
say[self.id=cty_ulric_stonevein self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_stage=bell priority=4] The mine captain drinks alone on Restdays now. A wolf drinks alone when he's carrying something.
say[self.id=cty_ulric_stonevein self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_stage=bell|moot world.mem.nh_fenwick=confessed priority=4] Then Frosthollow knows. If he's alive, I'll stand on the Pass with a lamp lit.
say[self.id=cty_ulric_stonevein self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_stage=moot priority=4] If he's alive, I'll stand on the Pass with a lamp lit.
say[self.id=cty_ulric_stonevein self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_captain=turned priority=5] He went back over the Pass, to bring them down when the snow goes. I believe him. Mostly.
say[self.id=cty_ulric_stonevein self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_captain=beaten priority=5] They led him to the city. I walked behind. Somebody should.
say[self.id=cty_ulric_stonevein self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_captain=dead priority=5] No quarter, they said. I said nothing. I should have.
say[self.id=cty_ulric_stonevein self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_captain=fled priority=5] Gone over the Pass with his coin, and the one I'd lost with him. Deep strange, to lose a wolf twice.
# rm_gorm_plankgate
say[self.id=rm_gorm_plankgate self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_stage=howls priority=4] Hold out your paw. No reason. An infirmarian likes to look.
say[self.id=rm_gorm_plankgate self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_stage=letters priority=4] A quiet season at the infirmary, honoured guest. I write a great many letters in a quiet season.
say[self.id=rm_gorm_plankgate self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_stage=letters world.mem.nh_wardens=coming priority=4] Yes, I wrote to them. By salt and water, someone had to.
say[self.id=rm_gorm_plankgate self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_stage=lights priority=4] I am the realm's Eye, and I'm sorry for it. Ask your question; I'll carry it.
say[self.id=rm_gorm_plankgate self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_stage=harvest priority=4] She asks whether a realm that cannot hold its own ford can keep its own pups. I've no answer for her yet, honoured guest.
say[self.id=rm_gorm_plankgate self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_stage=bell priority=4] If the pup is taught, I can say the realm keeps its own. If she is hidden, I can say nothing, carefully.
say[self.id=rm_gorm_plankgate self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_stage=moot priority=4] She is listening, honoured guest. So am I.
say[self.id=rm_gorm_plankgate self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_concord=answers priority=5] She tore up the Keeping at the Bay Light. I've a Warden House to keep at the abbey now.
say[self.id=rm_gorm_plankgate self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_concord=holds priority=5] One Warden stays at the Grey Gull a while. I'm to keep her tea hot.
say[self.id=rm_gorm_plankgate self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_concord=bends priority=5] Wardens in every silent town before long. I wrote the letter that brought them. I'll carry that.
# tn_cw_tansy_reedmere
say[self.id=tn_cw_tansy_reedmere self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called|reckoning|signals priority=4] #greet#. I'm only watching the mere. It's allowed.
say[self.id=tn_cw_tansy_reedmere self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_stage=howls priority=4] I hum when the chorus starts. The water likes it better than howling. That's silly, isn't it?
say[self.id=tn_cw_tansy_reedmere self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_stage=letters|lights|harvest priority=4] The mere's restless this year. I can feel it in my paws. Don't laugh.
say[self.id=tn_cw_tansy_reedmere self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_stage=bell priority=4] I hum when it's restless. Don't tell. Please.
say[self.id=tn_cw_tansy_reedmere self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_stage=bell|moot world.mem.nh_mere=still priority=4] The whole mere went still when I asked. Everyone saw. I'm not sorry.
say[self.id=tn_cw_tansy_reedmere self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_stage=moot priority=4] If you're at the landing on the Moot night, I'll be there too. I'm braver when somebody's there.
say[self.id=tn_cw_tansy_reedmere self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_tansy=taught priority=5] The water listens now, a little, when I ask it nicely. Not the bell. Never the bell again.
say[self.id=tn_cw_tansy_reedmere self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_tansy=pledged priority=5] They say I'm to go to the Wardens' school when the roads open. I'll write. They let you write, don't they?
say[self.id=tn_cw_tansy_reedmere self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_tansy=hidden priority=5] I hum at the landing every night. Nobody asks why.
say[self.id=tn_cw_tansy_reedmere self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_tansy=found priority=5] They found me out. I'm to go away to the Wardens. Nobody at home will say a word about it.
# tn_mb_skye_eelbank
say[self.id=tn_mb_skye_eelbank self.from=fenshore world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called|reckoning|signals priority=4] #greet#. Best eel trapper on the river, me. Ask anyone. Ask the eels.
say[self.id=tn_mb_skye_eelbank self.from=fenshore world.mem.nh_stage=howls priority=4] #greet#. Mirebridge had a howl that went round the reeds twice before it came back. I'll teach you the first turn, no?
say[self.id=tn_mb_skye_eelbank self.from=fenshore world.mem.nh_stage=letters priority=4] Black cloaks on the Pass and lights in the fens. Same weather, different water, no?
say[self.id=tn_mb_skye_eelbank self.from=fenshore world.mem.nh_stage=lights priority=4] Fen-sure I'll read them at the crossing. Somebody's got to say the names out loud.
say[self.id=tn_mb_skye_eelbank self.from=fenshore world.mem.nh_stage=lights|harvest|bell|moot world.mem.nh_lights=laid priority=4] Mirebridge's Keeper, they call me. I'm an eel-trapper with a long memory. Same thing, no?
say[self.id=tn_mb_skye_eelbank self.from=fenshore world.mem.nh_stage=harvest|bell priority=4] The fen's gone quiet. Quiet fens make me nervous, no?
say[self.id=tn_mb_skye_eelbank self.from=fenshore world.mem.nh_stage=moot priority=4] Mirebridge has a voice again, no? Carry oil to the crossing three nights, and the true lights will answer.
# rm_oskar_gullworth
say[self.id=rm_oskar_gullworth world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called|reckoning|howls|letters|lights|harvest priority=4] I've no time to talk. The City Office keeps late hours.
say[self.id=rm_oskar_gullworth world.mem.nh_stage=signals priority=4] Mislaid petitions, they say. The City Office mislays nothing. It postpones.
say[self.id=rm_oskar_gullworth world.mem.nh_stage=bell priority=4] I've no time to talk. The City Office keeps late hours. Some papers keep later.
say[self.id=rm_oskar_gullworth world.mem.nh_stage=bell world.mem.nh_writ=read priority=4] It's read, then. All of it. Don't look at me like that. Everyone looks at me like that now.
say[self.id=rm_oskar_gullworth world.mem.nh_oskar=confessed priority=5] I said it before the Council. All of it. I've not slept so well in a long while.
say[self.id=rm_oskar_gullworth world.mem.nh_oskar=exposed priority=5] Printed, on every board. I signed the order that bought that press.
say[self.id=rm_oskar_gullworth world.mem.nh_oskar=fled priority=5] Don't. I came here because nobody comes here.
say[self.id=rm_oskar_gullworth world.mem.nh_oskar=paid priority=5] There's nothing to say. Nothing at all. Leave me be.
# cty_fenwick_plankworth
say[self.id=cty_fenwick_plankworth self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning priority=4] The mine's note is the Counting House's now. I'm the mine captain. I'm told that's the same as owning nothing, eh?
say[self.id=cty_fenwick_plankworth self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_stage=howls priority=4] Silver under the ice, eh? I've heard the story. I might even know the place.
say[self.id=cty_fenwick_plankworth self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_stage=bell priority=4] Restday again. I'll drink at the Lamp and Pick, and say nothing, like every Restday. Leave it, eh?
say[self.id=cty_fenwick_plankworth self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_fenwick=confessed priority=5] I barred the door. I've said it. Now leave me the saying of it, eh?
# rm_aldric_grayrock_
say[self.id=rm_aldric_grayrock_ world.mem.nh_stage=letters priority=4] Letters, chasing me all the way out here. If one's in my girl's paw, I'd know it anywhere.
say[self.id=rm_aldric_grayrock_ world.mem.nh_stage=letters world.mem.nh_grayrock=home priority=4] Forty letters. My girl's were the heaviest. I read them all on the road.
say[self.id=rm_aldric_grayrock_ world.mem.nh_stage=letters|lights world.mem.nh_wharf=heard priority=4] I stood at the chapel while they read them. I didn't know them. I should have.
say[self.id=rm_aldric_grayrock_ world.mem.nh_stage=moot priority=4] Grayrock's seat is filled. Whether it votes as you like is another matter.
say[self.id=rm_aldric_grayrock_ pair.mem.nh_letters=ten priority=5] Ten letters, out to my road. I've not forgotten whose paws carried them.
# rm_maren_grayrock_
say[self.id=rm_maren_grayrock_ self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_stage=letters priority=4] I've not been to the gate in years. I wonder if the city's still the same out there.
say[self.id=rm_maren_grayrock_ self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_stage=letters|lights world.mem.nh_grayrock=home priority=4] I walked to the gate. Scales and silver, it's further than it looks.
say[self.id=rm_maren_grayrock_ self.from=larkfield pair.mem.nh_thyme=given priority=5] There's thyme in a jar by my window now. You did that.
# rm_ingrid_grayrock_
say[self.id=rm_ingrid_grayrock_ world.mem.nh_stage=letters priority=4] I write to my father every week. He's always somewhere on the coast road. Always somewhere.
say[self.id=rm_ingrid_grayrock_ pair.mem.nh_ingrid=truth priority=5] You told me the truth about Father. I've been less bored since. Isn't that strange?
say[self.id=rm_ingrid_grayrock_ pair.mem.nh_ingrid=kind priority=5] Father's coming home, you said. I watch the road.
# rm_tobias_grayrock_
say[self.id=rm_tobias_grayrock_ world.mem.nh_stage=letters world.mem.nh_grayrock=road priority=4] If Father doesn't come home, I'm the House. I'd rather be the forge.
# rm_gudrun_fell_
say[self.id=rm_gudrun_fell_ world.mem.nh_stage=letters priority=4] The head of my House never lets a debt go. Neither do I. Whatever errand you're on, I'll know whose before long.
say[self.id=rm_gudrun_fell_ world.mem.nh_gudrun=match priority=5] Vines and iron. It might even work. Don't tell Fellhall I said so.
say[self.id=rm_gudrun_fell_ world.mem.nh_gudrun=shown priority=5] I'm doing sums. I'm always doing sums. Go away.
say[self.id=rm_gudrun_fell_ pair.mem.nh_gudrun=ash priority=5] You burned it and told me. I owe you. I've written down how Fell will vote. Don't let the head of my House see you read it.
# rm_corwin_fell_
say[self.id=rm_corwin_fell_ world.mem.nh_stage=letters priority=4] The Rainward Hills want vines, not quarry dust. Any fool can see it.
say[self.id=rm_corwin_fell_ world.mem.nh_hills=oakhaven priority=5] The Council refused me, in front of Timberland. I'll remember the faces.
say[self.id=rm_corwin_fell_ world.mem.nh_hills=split priority=5] Half the hills. Half a victory. I'll drink to the half.
say[self.id=rm_corwin_fell_ world.mem.nh_hills=fell priority=5] Fell's hills now. Vines by the next planting. Oakhaven can cut somewhere else.
# rm_celestine_greatly
say[self.id=rm_celestine_greatly self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning priority=4] #greet#. The Counting House counts coin. I count wolves. I've counted you.
say[self.id=rm_celestine_greatly self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_stage=lights priority=4] My salon is open to every House, #address#. Especially the ones at odds.
say[self.id=rm_celestine_greatly self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_quarrel=peace priority=5] A wedding, and every House at one table. I'll sleep tonight.
say[self.id=rm_celestine_greatly self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_stage=moot world.mem.nh_ledger=shown priority=4] I cast the House's vote. The Counting House will learn what that means.
# rm_signe_mossgrave
say[self.id=rm_signe_mossgrave world.mem.nh_stage=lights priority=4] Timberland votes as its lord never bothers to. Mostly with his sense.
say[self.id=rm_signe_mossgrave world.mem.nh_stage=moot priority=4] The Council's vote is mine to cast. I'll cast it as the Line runs.
# rm_halvard_mossgrave
say[self.id=rm_halvard_mossgrave world.mem.nh_stage=letters|lights|harvest priority=4] Every smith in the Cinders would lie for me. That's a responsibility, not a boast.
say[self.id=rm_halvard_mossgrave world.mem.nh_stage=moot world.mem.nh_captain=turned priority=4] Deepvein iron was the best I ever bought. Tell them that, at the Pass.
# rm_isolde_fell_
say[self.id=rm_isolde_fell_ world.mem.nh_stage=letters priority=4] Fell never lets a debt go. Whatever you're selling, I've already priced it.
say[self.id=rm_isolde_fell_ world.mem.nh_quarrel=fell_timber priority=5] Shamed before the Council. Fell will vote against the lot of them. Mark it.
# rm_edric_kelpham
say[self.id=rm_edric_kelpham world.mem.nh_crown=bought priority=5] The Protector's steward now. Same kitchens, finer napkins.
# tn_cw_myrtle_stillford
say[self.id=tn_cw_myrtle_stillford self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called|reckoning|signals world.mem.nh_willa=home priority=4] Our carter's home and sulking about her wheel. Calm water.
say[self.id=tn_cw_myrtle_stillford self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called|reckoning|signals world.mem.nh_willa=alone priority=4] Our carter walked home alone. Nobody came. Deep and dark, I'll remember that.
# tn_cw_willa_coldwick
say[self.id=tn_cw_willa_coldwick self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called|reckoning|signals priority=4] The Oakhaven road's a fair road if nobody sits on it.
say[self.id=tn_cw_willa_coldwick self.from=coldwater pair.mem.nh_willa=walked priority=5] You walked me home from the camp. I'll not forget it, shore-friend.
# cty_ulla_rusthand
say[self.id=cty_ulla_rusthand self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called priority=4] I fell cedar, mm? Ask me about cedar. Don't ask me about wool.
say[self.id=cty_ulla_rusthand self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_logger=cleared priority=5] Shade on you. They'll let me howl for the town now, mm? Root and rain, I didn't think I'd want to.
say[self.id=cty_ulla_rusthand self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_logger=believed priority=5] Still a thief, to half the Sound Road. I count them under my breath.
# tn_oh_cairn_oakhaven
say[self.id=tn_oh_cairn_oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_logger=cleared priority=5] I carved the logger a bird. She didn't throw it at me. That's a start.
# cty_briar_cornby
say[self.id=cty_briar_cornby self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_stone=read priority=5] The stone remembered. So do I, now. I'll tell you true from here on, mostly.
# cty_nan_ashhand
say[self.id=cty_nan_ashhand world.mem.nh_hills=fell priority=5] I'll spend it on a cart to Oakhaven. They'll want cutters who know stone.
# tn_oh_ludo_beechshaw
say[self.id=tn_oh_ludo_beechshaw self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_potter=cleared priority=5] Here. A bird. I carve them and give them away. Keep this one, mm?
# cty_sloe_mistwick
say[self.id=cty_sloe_mistwick self.from=fenshore world.mem.nh_sloe=turned priority=5] My boats carry grain upriver now. Honest grain. Boggy feeling, no?
say[self.id=cty_sloe_mistwick self.from=fenshore world.mem.nh_sloe=exposed priority=5] Locked my shed and held me three days. I was late anyway.
# tn_mb_aspen_marshholm
say[self.id=tn_mb_aspen_marshholm self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_stage=harvest priority=4] I've never sold a sack I couldn't count. Count wolves for me tonight.
# rm_hilde_dripby
say[self.id=rm_hilde_dripby world.mem.nh_stage=bell priority=4] Ten pennies and I'll remember something. Twenty and I'll remember it right.
say[self.id=rm_hilde_dripby world.mem.nh_oskar=paid priority=5] The Chancellor paid better than you would have. No hard feelings.
# tn_cw_kell_greyton
say[self.id=tn_cw_kell_greyton self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_stage=bell priority=4] Something big's moving under the Upper Mere. I hear it at night through the shed floor, eh?
say[self.id=tn_cw_kell_greyton self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_bell=rung priority=5] Green as a pike and loud as a gale. Calm water, it's up!
say[self.id=tn_cw_kell_greyton self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_bell=cracked priority=5] It rang flat. Still rang, eh?
say[self.id=tn_cw_kell_greyton self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_bell=lost priority=5] It's still moving down there. I hear it at night.
# tn_fh_thistle_stonepick
say[self.id=tn_fh_thistle_stonepick self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_stage=bell priority=4] A mine collapse, they told me. Not which mine. Not who barred what. By salt and water, I'll know now.
say[self.id=tn_fh_thistle_stonepick self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_fenwick=confessed priority=5] Deepvein. Kin of mine were at that door. The well remembers. Now so do I.
# rm_mab_coalridge
say[self.id=rm_mab_coalridge self.mem.nh_spy=told_king priority=5] I keep to the kitchens. I speak to nobody. Go away.
say[self.id=rm_mab_coalridge self.mem.nh_spy=told_queen priority=5] The Queen knows. She hasn't sent me off. I don't know why.
say[self.id=rm_mab_coalridge self.mem.nh_spy=paid priority=5] You took the coin too. So we're the same.
# cty_lorn_hedgeton
say[self.id=cty_lorn_hedgeton self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_stage=signals priority=4] I watch the road. Leave it, eh?
say[self.id=cty_lorn_hedgeton self.from=coldwater self.mem.nh_lorn=shamed priority=5] The square's turned its back. Muddied, all of it.
say[self.id=cty_lorn_hedgeton self.from=coldwater self.mem.nh_lorn=turned priority=5] Two long and one short is a wagon on the road. Now you know, eh? Don't say who said.
# rm_rune_gullwell
say[self.id=rm_rune_gullwell world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning priority=4] Notes fall due at the new moon. I only carry the chalk.
# rm_corra_coalcot
say[self.id=rm_corra_coalcot world.mem.nh_stage=signals priority=4] Papers, fresh today. Don't sniff them, they're delicate.
# rmx_piet_lumley
say[self.id=rmx_piet_lumley world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning|signals|howls|letters|lights|harvest|bell|moot self.mem.nh_debt=freed priority=4] I light the city's lamps and couldn't light my own. #thanks#.
say[self.id=rmx_piet_lumley world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning|signals|howls|letters|lights|harvest|bell|moot self.mem.nh_debt=pledged priority=4] I've pledged my howl to the Counting House. I light their lamps first now.
# Debtors (any resident the campaign marks: self.mem.nh_debt, npc scope, Ch 1 to 4, read until Ch 9)
say[self.mem.nh_debt=pressed world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning|signals|howls|letters|lights|harvest|bell|moot priority=4] They want my howl for my note. A howl! As if it were a spoon to pawn.
say[self.mem.nh_debt=freed world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning|signals|howls|letters|lights|harvest|bell|moot priority=4] A wolf of the road worked off my note and asked nothing back. I'll howl how I please now.
say[self.mem.nh_debt=angry world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning|signals|howls|letters|lights|harvest|bell|moot priority=4] Chalk on my door. I'll scrub it off, and I'll remember who drew it.
say[self.mem.nh_debt=pledged world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning|signals|howls|letters|lights|harvest|bell|moot priority=4] I sold my howl. Don't look at me.
say[self.mem.nh_debt=sings world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning|signals|howls|letters|lights|harvest|bell|moot priority=4] Bought back! I'll be in the chorus at dusk. Loudest in the street.
free
choice Let me see your wares. [role=merchant here.shop=open|bare] -> do shop
choice Any work going? [role=merchant here.giver=yes] -> do open work
choice Any missions for our Chapter? [role!=merchant here.official=yes here.chapter=yes] -> do open missions
choice Could you teach me your trade? [here.teaches=yes] -> do open learn
choice Heard any news? [does ask.detail] -> news
choice I want to know more about something... -> about
choice I'm #self.name#. [player.named=no] -> do introduce ; then introduced
choice What's your name? [player.named=yes player.met=no] -> do ask_name ; then name
each heard in here.heard max 2
choice I heard #heard.words#. [does tell.news] -> told
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node about
say What about? | Ask away. | Go on, then.
say[pair.disposition=hostile|wary] If you must.
free
choice Tell me about yourself. [does ask.detail] -> job
choice They say you're one who #here.quirk_words#. [here.has_quirk=yes] -> quirk
choice What do you make of things these days? [here.opinions>0] -> opinions
choice How's your family? [here.kin>0] -> kin_list
choice What's it like around here? -> town
choice Could you tell me the way? [here.places>0] -> way
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub

node town
say #here.town#? About #here.folk# of us live here, and there are #here.shops# shops. | #here.town#'s home to #here.folk# or so. It does well enough, #address#.
say[here.district] This end of #here.town# is the #here.district# district. About #here.folk# of us in the town, #here.shops# shops. | The #here.district# district, this. #here.town# has #here.folk# souls or so.
say[here.inns=0 priority=1] #here.town#? #here.folk# of us, #here.shops# shops, and no inn, so don't count on a bed.
say[world.times=hard] Hard times in #here.town#. #here.folk# of us, and not all of us eating well. | #here.town#? Lean, these days. #here.shops# shops, and fewer customers.
say[here.folk=0 priority=3] It's quiet out here. Not many of us about.
say[world.times=good|boom] #here.town#'s doing well. #here.folk# of us, #here.shops# shops, and coin about. | Good times, here. Ask anyone.
free
choice Where would I find someone? [here.people>0] -> people
choice What day is it? -> day
choice Anyone here I ought to meet? [here.matchmaker=yes] -> match
choice Am I wanted here? -> wanted
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node job
ask player.job
say #job_busy#
free
choice And how's business? [business=thriving|steady|failing] -> business
choice When do you work? [here.has_hours=yes] -> hours
choice How are you keeping, yourself? [does ask.how] -> how
choice Heard any news? -> news
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node how
answers
say Well enough. | Getting by. | Can't complain. | Middling, thank you.
say[tired=yes] Tired. It's been a long day. | Worn through, if I'm honest.
say[injured=light] A few aches. Nothing to speak of.
say[injured=bad priority=2] Hurt. I'm hurt, and it's slow mending.
say[mourning=kin|friend priority=3] Some days are easier than others. | I manage.
free
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node business
say Steady. It pays the rent. | Steady enough, thank you.
say[business=thriving] Couldn't be better. We can't keep the shelves full. | Thriving, touch wood.
say[business=failing] Badly. I don't know how long we'll last. | Poorly. Customers are few.
free
choice Heard any news? -> news
choice I was wondering about something else... -> do open talk
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node hours
ask player.hours
say Most days, from the morning until the light goes. | The usual hours. Morning till dusk.
free
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node quirk
say So they say. They're not wrong. | Ha. Somebody's been talking. It's true enough. | Guilty. A wolf has her habits, or his.
say[pair.disposition=hostile|wary] And what's it to you?
mood pleased
free
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node opinions
say Which things? | About what, now? | Ask, and I'll tell you.
each opinion in here.opinions max 3
choice What do you make of #opinion.words#? [does ask.opinion] -> opinion
choice I'd like to ask about something else... -> about

node opinion
answers
say #topic.opinion_words.capitalize#? I couldn't say, one way or the other. | #topic.opinion_words.capitalize#? I keep my thoughts on that to myself.
free
choice What about the other things? -> opinions
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node kin_list
say Which of them? | Mine? Ask, then.
each kin in here.kin max 3
choice How's your #kin.word#? [does ask.after] -> kin_said
choice I'd like to ask about something else... -> about

node kin_said
say #topic.kin_name#? Well enough, thank you for asking. | #topic.kin_name#'s well. Busy, as ever.
say[topic.kin_state=hurt] #topic.kin_name#'s hurt, and mending slowly. Kind of you to ask. | Not so well. #topic.kin_name#'s hurt.
say[topic.kin_state=hungry] Hungry, if I'm honest. We're short this week.
say[topic.kin_state=mourning] Grieving, still. We both are.
free
choice And the others? -> kin_list
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node news
say #news_none#
# >>> Ninth Howl talk, part 2 (gossip and helpful knowledge; generated, doc 86 §6.4): news lines
# The campaign: thanks to the heroes and, after the Moot, how it ended (cast-and-talk §4).
say[self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_debts=grace] The factors gave a moon's grace. Generous of them, they say. It only means the interest runs a month longer.
say[self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_debts=grace] A moon's grace from the factors, eh? Like letting a fish run with the hook still in. Deep and dark, it comes in all the same.
say[self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_debts=grace] A moon's grace on every note, #address#. Fair price, they call it. Weigh the interest, then tell me it's fair.
say[self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_debts=grace] The factors gave the debtors a moon's grace. Chaff and promises, #address#. The note's still due, only later.
say[self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_debts=grace] A moon's grace, no? Boggy sort of grace. The water's still rising, only slower.
say[self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_debts=grace] The factors gave a moon's grace, #address#. A grace you pay interest on is not a grace. It is a longer leash.
say[self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_debts=grace] A moon's grace on the notes, mm? Bark and branch, the rot keeps working under the bark.
say[self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_debts=grace] The factors gave a moon's grace. Dead rock talk. The note weighs the same, only colder.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=ridgemere] Whoever's carrying the Summons out to the far towns, blood and bread, the whole city owes them a cup.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_alder=cleared] Whoever broke the Alder Mere camp, the carters drink to them now.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=coldwater] Whoever walks the city's word up to the lake, calm water to them. We're not often asked, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_willa=home] Our carter's home! A wolf of the road walked her in. Calm water to them.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_alder=cleared] The Alder Mere camp's broken. Full weight to whoever broke it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=southmeadow] Whoever walked the Summons all this way south, they'll have a cup of the new wine from me.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] A Moot called by a fen wolf's lamp. Dry feet to the herald who said it out loud.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=saltwell] Whoever walked the Summons to the pool, may their well never fail.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=oakhaven] Shade on whoever carries the city's word down the Sound Road, mm? Slow news, but welcome.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_logger=cleared] The logger's cleared. Somebody found the wool smelling of smoke, not sap. Good bark, that wolf.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=frosthollow] Whoever walked the Summons up the Pass Road, lamp's thanks. The valley's not used to being asked.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_alder=cleared] The Alder Mere camp's broken, the carters say. Lamp's thanks to whoever went in.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_debts=eased] The lamplighter's note is paid. A wolf of the road did it. Blood and bread, the streets are brighter.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere] Blood and bread to whoever lends a debtor a paw at her work and won't take a penny for it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_debts=eased] A wolf of the road paid off a city note with work. Calm water, there's hope in the city yet.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_handbill=up] The handbill's on every board. A debt is not a voice. Sold, to whoever wrote it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_debts=eased] The new moon came up on paid doors, they say. Ripe days.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] Whoever works the city's lamplighter free of his note, dry feet to that one.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=saltwell] May the well never fail whoever frees the city's herald from her note.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=oakhaven] A wolf who frees a debtor and asks nothing back, mm? Good bark, that one.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=frosthollow] Lamp's thanks to the road wolves hauling ore with us. The note's lighter for every load.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_seam=honest] The quota's met. A road wolf hauled ore with us. Lamp's thanks.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_lists=bettany] The sergeant took the list to the magistrate. Door open, at noon. Blood and bread.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_dark=1] No lamps on the ridges last night, the carters say. Blood and bread to whoever sat up there.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_dark=1] No lamps on the downs last night. Calm water to whoever sat on that ridge.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_glasswater=open] The Glasswater road's open. Wagons in, wagons out. Full weight.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=southmeadow] A wolf sat on a ridge all night so a wagon of ours came through. Sheaf and sickle, I'll stand them a cup.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_dark=1] Somebody put the ridge lamps out. Dry feet to them, wherever they're drying.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] A wolf of the road sat up on the ridges so the wagons could pass. Dry feet to them, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=saltwell] The road to the well runs clear this week. May the well never fail whoever cleared it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_dark=1] The knoll was dark last night. Somebody sat on it. Good bark.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=frosthollow] The Upper Mere post's going up. Cold iron, there's a light on the road that's ours.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=ridgemere] Somebody's carrying the old howl from square to square. Blood and bread, it's been years since I heard it right.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_howl=found] The square came out at dusk and howled the old one right. The Bright One heard that, I'd say.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=coldwater] Somebody sat with the old ones and caught the howl off them. Calm water, that's patience.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_howl=found] Coldwater found its howl! Calm water, it went up like a rising fish.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=larkfield] A road wolf stood in our chorus and didn't miss a turn. Full weight, that.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_howl=found] Full weight! Larkfield howled the old one right and half the Downs came to hear.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_stone=read] The stone's read, nine names, one chiselled out. Somebody went up four nights for it. Ripe days.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] Somebody's carrying the old howl from town to town. Dry feet to them. The drowned would thank them.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=saltwell] A wolf of the road sat three Restdays with the old one at the pans. The well remembers patience, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_howl=found] The pool heard its own howl again. May the well never fail whoever sat still for it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=oakhaven] A road wolf asked three old roots for the howl, slow and twice. Good bark, that one.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_relay=ran] Oakhaven answered on the relay night. Proper, it did.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_silver=crown] The silver came down the Pass Road and the Crown has it. Cold iron, the mine's got its charter.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_grayrock=home] The Grayrock lord's in the Antechamber, and the Council's whole. Blood and bread, the letters did that.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_wharf=heard] The wharf drowned were read out at the Chapel of the Tide, with the Grayrock lord standing. About time.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_hills=oakhaven] The cut's still Oakhaven's, I hear. Calm water.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=coldwater] Somebody walked the Grayrock lord's letters out to him, eh? Calm water, the wharf can sleep.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=larkfield] The Grayrock lady smiled at the gate, they say. Full weight, that wolf who brought the thyme.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_hills=oakhaven|split] The hills are settled and nobody's dead. Ripe days, that's a fair end.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=southmeadow] Somebody's walking the twelve bounds for Oakhaven. Sheaf and sickle, I'd stand them a cup.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_grayrock=home] The Grayrock lord came home. Dry feet to whoever dragged him.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] Somebody carried the drowned's names to the Chapel of the Tide. Dry feet to them, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_wharf=heard] The names of the wharf drowned were read before the Grayrock lord. May every well remember them.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=saltwell] Somebody carried forty letters to a lord who never drinks at home. May their well never fail.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=oakhaven] Shade on every wolf who walks the bounds with us. The cut remembers who stood on it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=oakhaven here.region=oakhaven world.mem.nh_cut=ours] The cut's ours for good. Good bark to every wolf who walked the bounds with us, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=frosthollow] Lamp's thanks to whoever walks the black cloaks' road with them. The Pass is long and the Captain's watching.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_envoy=walked] The black cloak walked down with an escort. Lamp's thanks to whoever kept her road.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=ridgemere] Somebody carried bread and salt to a House steward and the door stayed open. Blood and bread, the old ways.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_quarrel=peace] A wedding at the Greatly salon and every House at one table. Blood and bread, somebody kept the peace.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_lights=laid] The fen lights stopped. They say the priest said every name. Calm water.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_cache=home] Our stillmaster got her wine back from the drowned causeway. A road wolf carried it. Fair catch.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_cache=home] A wolf brought the cache from the drowned causeway home, piece by piece. Full weight, that.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_cache=home] The bee-keeper got her honey back! Some road wolf found it at the drowned causeway. Ripe days.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_potter=cleared] The carpenter's cleared. The records say what they say, and he carves birds for the pups. Dry feet.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_quarrel=peace] Bread and salt reached every House. By bread and salt, the old way still works.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_potter=cleared] The carpenter at Fenshore's cleared, they say. He carved a bird for whoever did it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_lights=laid] The fen lights are laid, they say. Lamp's thanks to whoever walked the path.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=ridgemere] Every wolf who went down to the Larkfield ford, blood and bread, the city's proud of you.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_desmond=mercy] The dismissed guard stood the granary door all the third night. Mercy paid, for once.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_ford=held] The ford held. Calm water to every wolf who stood in it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_ford=held] Three nights held! Full weight, every wolf who stood.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_ford=held] Southmeadow went to the ford. Ripe days, we'll tell it at every harvest.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] Somebody walked the river company into the shallows. Dry feet to them.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=saltwell] Salt and water went north on every caravan this week. May the well never fail those who carried it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_runner=came] The runner reached the pool before midnight. May the well never fail that wolf.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=oakhaven] Shade on every wolf at the ford. Oakhaven's sending what it can.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_ford=held] Larkfield held. Good bark, every one of them.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=frosthollow] Lamp's thanks to the wolves at the ford. The valley sent rope and lamps, what we had.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_ford=held] They held the ford in Larkfield. Cold iron, the valley's proud.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=ridgemere] Every wolf hauling on the Upper Mere ropes, blood and bread, the city's waiting to hear that bell.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_writ=read] A wolf of the road found the writ. The herald read it at noon. Blood and bread, I wept too.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_bell=rung] The bell's up and the haulers are home. Calm water to every wolf on the ropes, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_bell=rung] The bell came up out of the Upper Mere. Full weight of a bell!
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_writ=read] The writ's found and read. Ripe days for the whole realm.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_bell=rung] Our bell's out of the ice. Dry feet to every wolf on the ropes.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_fenwick=confessed] The mine captain said it aloud at last. By salt and water, the well remembers, and now so does the valley.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_writ=read] The writ's read. Shade on whoever found it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=frosthollow] Lamp's thanks to every wolf who went down the mine and was counted up again.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_fenwick=confessed] He said it, at the Lamp and Pick. Deep quiet after. Then we drank to Deepvein.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=ridgemere] Every post on the Line has a keeper now. Blood and bread, I never thought the realm could agree on a howl.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=coldwater] Every wolf standing a post on the Line, calm water to you, eh? We'll hear you from the mere.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_voice=raised] Coldwater's voice is raised. We'll answer even if no wolf of the road is here. Calm water.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=larkfield] Every wolf who held the ford, Larkfield howls for you on the Moot night.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=southmeadow] Every wolf who carried a howl south, Southmeadow sings for you. Sheaf and sickle.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_stone=read] Whoever read the stone, Southmeadow howls with Mirebridge's name back in it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] The drowned heard their names this season. Now they'll hear their howl. Dry feet to you.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=saltwell] The well's roll has your names in it now, every wolf who sat still. Peace on you.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=oakhaven] Shade on every wolf who walked the bounds. Oakhaven remembers.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=frosthollow] Every wolf who stands at the Pass, Frosthollow keeps your lamp lit.
say[self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_crown=ottilie] Bright One keep the Queen. And the lamp-keeper beside her, bless his flat feet.
say[self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_crown=lamp] A Sump wolf at the lamp, by the realm's own howl. Blood and bread, I howled for him.
say[self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_crown=regency] No crown at all, and a Moot every year. I'll believe it when it sits twice.
say[self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_crown=regency world.mem.nh_moot=midwinter] No crown at all, and a Moot every Midwinter. I'll believe it when it sits twice.
say[self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_crown=bought] The Counting House has the realm now. They call it a Protectorate. I call it a debt with a crown on.
say[self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_concord=answers] The black cloak tore the Keeping at the Bay Light. The Wardens are going home.
say[self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_concord=bends] Wardens in every silent town by spring. We were too quiet, somewhere.
say[self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_captain=turned] The Grey Captain went back over the Pass with the coin. To fetch the Deepvein families down, they say.
say[self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_captain=beaten] They held the Grey Captain a day in the Keep's cells and judged him at the Moot's end. It's on the Market Square board.
say[self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_howl=ran] We answered, eh? Glasswater answered! A howl over the water.
say[self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_crown=ottilie] A Queen who coughs in the damp. She'll want a lake wolf's soup. Calm water.
say[self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_crown=lamp] The lamp-keeper's a fen wolf. Close enough to the lake. Fair catch.
say[self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_crown=regency] A Moot every year, eh? The city asking the lake what it thinks. Deep and dark, I'll get used to it.
say[self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_crown=bought] Bought, eh? Muddied water all the way up.
say[self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_concord=holds] One black cloak at the Grey Gull till spring. Fair winds to her.
say[self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_howl=ran] Larkfield answered on the dot. Sold, to the realm.
say[self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_crown=ottilie] A Queen who carries her own petitions. That's full weight.
say[self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_crown=lamp] A patrolman king. By the market cross, the Houses are still weighing it.
say[self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_crown=regency] No crown, and a market of voices every year. Fair price.
say[self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_crown=bought] Short-weighed realm. The Counting House kept the scales.
say[self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_captain=beaten] They led the Grey Captain down the Pass Road. Weights and measures, there'll be a judging worth watching.
say[self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_howl=ran] Ripe days. We howled the burying howl by mistake and nobody minded.
say[self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_crown=ottilie] A Queen! Sheaf and sickle, I'll plant her an apple tree.
say[self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_crown=lamp] The lamp-keeper's king. Good harvest to him.
say[self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_crown=regency] A Moot every year. More talk than a harvest dance, and longer.
say[self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_crown=bought] Blight take it. Bought, like a cart of chaff.
say[self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_concord=answers] The Wardens left by the Pass. A good harvest of a night.
say[self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_bell=rung] Our bell rang the Moot in. Fen-sure, the drowned heard it.
say[self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_crown=lamp] A Mirebridge wolf with the Palace lamp. Dry feet, the drowned have a king.
say[self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_crown=ottilie] A Queen, and the lamp-keeper beside her. Fen-sure, he'll keep her feet dry.
say[self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_crown=regency] A Moot every year, and Mirebridge has a voice in every one. Mud and eels!
say[self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_crown=bought] Bought. Boggy. We'll howl louder at the next Moot, no?
say[self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_lights=faded] The Council spoke for us at the Moot. The drowned won't forgive that.
say[self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_howl=ran] The howl came out of the dark to the oasis, #address#, and we sent it on. The well remembers.
say[self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_crown=ottilie] A Queen who answers petitions. Peace on her house.
say[self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_crown=lamp] A keeper of the peace with the lamp. By salt and water, that is what the old King meant.
say[self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_crown=regency] The realm draws from the Moot each year, like a well. Good.
say[self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_crown=bought] A crown bought with debt is a brackish crown, #address#.
say[self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_concord=holds] A black cloak at the Grey Gull, they say. Let her drink, and go in peace.
say[self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_howl=ran] A Moot night to remember, mm? It came through the cedars slow and climbing.
say[self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_crown=ottilie] A Queen, mm? Root well, Majesty.
say[self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_crown=lamp] The lamp-keeper keeps it. Proper.
say[self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_crown=regency] No crown. A council of everyone. Old Oak, that's a big grove.
say[self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_crown=bought] Bought. Rotten at the root. We'll grow round it.
say[self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_concord=answers] The black cloaks went back over the Pass. Shade on the realm.
say[self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_howl=ran] Held the Pass post. Cold iron and warm hearts, the both of it.
say[self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_crown=bought] Bought, then. Black seam. At the next Moot, we howl deeper.
say[self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_captain=turned] Deepvein's coming down in spring, they say. We'll share the oil this time.
say[self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_captain=dead] No quarter at the Pass. Lamp and pick, I'd rather we'd given one.
say[self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_captain=fled] The Captain went over the Pass with his coin. He'll be back. They come back for what they're owed.
say[self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_captain=beaten] They took the Captain down to the city's cells. Lamp and pick, I hope they judged him fair.
say[self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_crown=ottilie|lamp|regency] The realm howled from the Pass to the Bay Light. Deep quiet after. Then the bell.
# The quest packs: helpful knowledge (priority 2) and the thin purse (priority 3) (quests-*.md, talk).
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The Morning Oven sends bread to the Sump Infirmary every day. The baker's always a carrier short, and she pays in cake. | Want an honest errand? The baker on the north side needs her loaves carried down to the Sump.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=sump world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Going down to the infirmary? Take the Stairs. The lanes behind the Fish Hall are the first to flood.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The abbey's healer pays for herbs. Long grass and willows give them, any season but winter. | Herbs for the House of Mending? Any green bunch from the grass outside the walls, he says.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Yarrow's the one the healer wants most. It grows on open grass, spring to autumn.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=sump world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The old wolf above the pawnshop loses his littlest twice a week. She's always on the piers, counting masts.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=wharf world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Hunting for a pup on the quay? Try the piers under the Grayrock office. That's where the small ones go to look at the ships.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=coldwater world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] That old lake wolf over the pawnshop has a pup who'd sail to the Bright One's door if a ship went there, eh?
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=sump world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] If somebody's already gone after the pawnbroker's pup, the Morning Oven always wants a carrier down the Stairs.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The smokehouse on the north wharf pays for oak bark. Never pine, she says, and you can smell why.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Oak bark peels off the broad-leaved trees in the woods past the walls. Pines give you resin, not bark.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The Ropewalk buys pine resin for the tar. The hills east of the city are thick with pines.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=works world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Every Grayrock hull leaves port in Ropewalk rope. The ropemaker pays for resin, and counts every lump.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=office world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Upstairs at the Records Office they pay for copying. You read the old count while you do it.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] If you want to know how the city was counted, sort a drawer at the Records Office. They'll even pay you for it.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The City Office never has enough paws for the Heights round. Those houses tip in thanks, not pennies.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=heights world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] A letter for this street? Bring it to the door, not the gate. The doorkeepers here don't come down for anyone.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The cathedral's sexton takes candles any day, but she wants you at the service on Restday too.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Wax or tallow, the cathedral burns it all. The chandlers on the north side sell both.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=sump world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The young almoner from the lake country sends bread down here. Some wolf carries it, and doesn't ask questions.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=coldwater world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The abbey's almoner is lake-born, eh? She'll find you work if you've a strong back and a closed mouth.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=commons world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The provisioner in the Market Hall buys whatever you've gathered, and pays honest. On Marketday she's desperate.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Stalls on the Square go for a few pennies on Marketday. Sell from one and you'll learn every trick on the Commons.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=sump world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The greens wolf from the Rainwood pays for mushrooms. She says the Sump's too damp for anything but mould.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Mushrooms come up out of rotten logs and fern banks, spring to autumn. The woods past the walls are full of both.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=oakhaven world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Mushrooms want deadwood, mm? Rotten logs and wet ferns. You'll fill a basket slow and sure.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=works world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The Nailers' Forge never has charcoal enough. The charcoal store on the Sump side of the Commons sells it by the sack.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Want honest sweat in the Cinders? Carry charcoal for the nailers. They pay in nails, and nails sell.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The Greatly stables pay for oats and straw. Don't expect the steward to thank you; the stable wolf will.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The lamplighter wants somebody to ring the morning bell. You climb the Clock Tower at first light; he can't, at his age.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=wharf world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Want work on the piers? Be there when a ship comes in. They always want paws on the lines.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The ships come in on a timetable, and the notice board tells you which is due. Bring rope and you're welcome.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The Carters' Yard pays for a crate carried when a wagon goes short. The Oakhaven road's the usual one.
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The Ridgemere carters send short loads, mm? Some kind wolf usually walks the rest along the Sound Road.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=heights world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The wolf who visits our sick swears by willow bark for stiff joints. Says it beats any physician on the Commons.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Every physic in the city sells willow bark. Steep it long and it eases an old joint, they say.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The Cinder butcher pays for pheasants out of the Rainward Woods. They run more than they fly; head them off.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Pheasants feed in the grass and scrub at the wood's edge. Two wolves, one to drive and one to wait, take them easy.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=commons world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Soundings pays wolves to walk out to the tarns and back. Easy pennies, if your paws are good.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Rainmere's up in the hills east of here, and Slate Tarn past it. Keep the city behind you and climb.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The Oakhurst pig wolf has a fox at his hens, eh? Foxes keep to the scrub and woods. Corner one and it fights.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Hunting a fox? Go quiet and downwind. They hear you coming a field away, eh?
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The baker sends bread down to the landing most days, eh? Carry it and she'll see you right.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] If you want a small job here, ask the baker. Her loaves go down to the boat crews every day.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The Boiling House always wants wood, eh? Any wood. The kettle doesn't care if it's pretty.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Fat scraps? A badger gives two. They're in the woods and scrub, and they'll run, eh? Corner one and it turns round and bites.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The Meresend pup wanders after apples. Wherever the wind smells sweet, that's where he'll be, eh?
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Mind the mere shore past the orchards. There's a camp up there that won't stay broken.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] If the Meresend pup's already being looked for, the bakehouse wants loaves carried to the landing, eh?
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The Larkdowns shepherd pays for straw for his pens. Calm sort, eh? He hums to the ewes.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The fen-born shepherd at Larkdowns loses ewes up the downs, eh? They leave wool on the thorns; a good nose follows it.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] If both his strays are being tracked, the other Larkdowns shepherd wants straw for the pens, eh?
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The carter's drag rope's given out, mm? Rope comes from the city ropewalk. The notice is on the board by the square.
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The road wolves sit at Alder Mere, on the way to the city. Go in a pair if you're carrying.
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The fellers at the cut want venison. Roe deer keep to the deep trees, mm? Downwind, and slow.
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] One of the loggers can't sleep before a storm. Chamomile helps, mm? It grows with the wildflowers in spring and summer.
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The Pass House burns through wood while the carters wait on the road. The carter on the square keeps their stack, stone.
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Wood for the Pass House? The notice is on the board, cousin. Any deadwood burns, and the slopes are full of it.
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The young collier on the Upper hearths wants her clamp sat at night. Deep cold up there; take a fur.
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] If both clamps are spoken for, the limeburner wants the goats off his scree, stone.
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The limeburner wants the goats off his scree. They fight when they're cornered, stone. Go in a pair.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The Plumtree orchard has a badger under the store. Fair warning: they're top-weight, and a cornered one bites.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] A badger's fat is worth the bite. The soap wolves at the lake pay for it, eh?
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The Southwood swineherd keeps a tally of who's helped him. Better to be on it than off it, eh?
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The press buys old linen. You'd not think a rag of it was worth anything till you see them weigh it, eh?
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Linen for the vats? The stores keep a bolt or two. Buy fair, sell to the press, and everybody's full weight.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The Longmead miller wants the reeds pulled from his race. Wet work, but he pays in flour, eh?
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The Larkholm farmhand keeps skeps by the granary. He wants herbs for his smoker; wormwood if there's any, summer and autumn.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Mind the Sunfields road past Larkholm. There's a camp up there, blight take it, and it keeps coming back.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The Larkholm miller'll wager on anything, bless him. He's got one going on the hares in his seed rows.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Hares sit tight and then go like a shot. Two of you: one to drive, one to wait in the furrow.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The Larkholm farmhand's stringing garlands round the square for the festival. Every bunch helps the rope reach, bless it.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Southmeadow's dressing its square for the festival. They'll pay in thanks, not silver, but it's a fair trade, eh?
say[here.region=fenshore self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The Dune warrener's purse-nets are worn through, no? Bring him cord. He pays in smoked rabbit and old sayings.
say[here.region=fenshore self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Firewood's scarce in the fen, no? The dry ground north of the boardwalks has scrub and willow, and that burns.
say[here.region=fenshore self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The Fenside salt worker has a grandmother story for everything, no? Ask her about Mirebridge, if you've the stomach for it.
say[here.region=fenshore self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The clay digger at the Mirebridge pits wants a second spade, no? She counts every lump, so bring four.
say[here.region=fenshore self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Nobody digs at the crossroads itself, no? That's where the village stood, before the river came over.
say[here.region=fenshore self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] There's a plank gone by the Heron. The deckhand who mends the boardwalks takes planks and nails, no?
say[here.region=saltwell self.from=saltwell world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The salt rakers at the pan need carriers. Go when the sun is low, my friend; the white burns when it is high.
say[here.region=saltwell self.from=saltwell world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The Redsand warrener cannot cure her pelts without salt. Carry some to the stores and she will remember it.
say[here.region=saltwell self.from=saltwell world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The Ochre vines are stripped by rabbits. The vine-tender pays well, and feeds better.
say[here.region=saltwell self.from=saltwell world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Rabbits hear you before they see you. Come at them slowly, downwind, and the vines will thank you.
say[here.region=saltwell self.from=saltwell world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The farm cart comes in early, most mornings, and the caravans more seldom. Wait in the shade by the pool, and you will hear them before you see them.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=saltwell world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] In Saltwell, #address#, a caravan is met at the well. Even here, so far from it, I look for someone to meet.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=estate world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] The Fellhall kitchen is always a basket short. The hall servant pays for eggs and cheese brought round the back.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Fellhall's kitchen buys eggs off the Commons most days. Go in by the kitchens; the front door's for the family.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=estate world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Grayrock Hall buys linen when the sea damp gets into the sheets. The young hall servant pays, and talks loud enough for two.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Greywool sends its finished bolts up to the big houses. The young loom hand pays a carrier, and makes a joke of it.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=estate world.mem.sq_on=yes priority=2] Looking for the Court's chamber keeper? He takes his supper below stairs, and you'll hear him humming before you see him.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called|reckoning priority=2] The Square's baker is baking double for the wake. She wants carriers to the Soup Kitchen, and no payment taken at the tables.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=sump world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called|reckoning priority=2] The Soup Kitchen's feeding the wake and the Sump both. Bread carried down from the Square goes a long way.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called|reckoning priority=2] The City Office is sending the Moot's summons to every farmstead on the roll. The clerk pays carriers who don't mind hills.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_stage=signals priority=2] The masons' yard by Northgate gives a carrier two blocks a day for the Line posts. The posts want four apiece.
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_stage=signals priority=2] The post at Alder Mere wants stone, mm? The city masons send it out, two blocks at a time.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_stage=signals priority=2] The coppice woodward cuts two poles a day for the Line posts. He wants carriers, and says so bluntly.
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_stage=signals priority=2] The Upper Mere post wants timber, stone. Poles come out from the city coppice, two at a time.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_stage=howls priority=2] The Larkholm lad's sending sorry-gifts round for the howl that went wrong at the wedding. Carry one and you'll hear the story, bless you.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_stage=howls priority=2] Practising the howl? Mind which one. We've one for the dead and one for a wedding, and the square mixed them, ripe and proper.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_stage=letters|lights priority=2] The Rainward orchard keeper sends bread up to the wolves walking the bounds. Carry some and she'll fill your waterskin.
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_stage=letters|lights priority=2] Bread comes up from the Rainward orchard for the bounds-walkers, mm? Good bark, that keeper.
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_stage=letters|lights priority=2] Green stakes in the cut, mm? Pull one and take it to the logger. The notice is up on the square.
say[here.region=fenshore self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_stage=letters|lights priority=2] The Fen Shore deckhand wants the boardwalk lamps lit at dusk, no? So a wolf can tell our lights from the ones out on the fen.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_stage=harvest|bell priority=2] The Looms send blankets down to the wolves at the ford, eh? The loom hand wants carriers, and she'll give you a hard look first.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_stage=harvest|bell world.mem.nh_ford=burned priority=2] The Longmead farmhand's giving out bread for the burned houses, eh? Find him at the granary and he'll load you up.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_stage=bell priority=2] The bakehouse sends bread up to the haulers on the mere, eh? The shop hand wants carriers who don't mind the cold.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_stage=moot priority=2] The carpenter in the Market Hall is building benches for the Moot. She wants planks and nails, and dry ones.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_stage=moot priority=2] The fen carpenter in the Market Hall wants planks for the Moot benches, no? Dry ones, or she'll cough at you.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=sump world.mem.mq_lamps=dark priority=2] Want the lamp-oil thief? Ask at the Pawn and Ledger who's been selling flasks cheap.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.mq_tally=open priority=2] The night wagons go out by the south road. You'll see the ruts below Southgate if you've a nose for axle grease.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=wharf|office world.mem.mq_wharf=open priority=2] If you want to know why a crane rope parted, ask at the Ropewalk. They remember every order they refused.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.mq_sunken=open priority=2] Pups go down the Sunken Street steps for dares. The west end's where they hide; it's darkest there.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.mq_coal=open priority=2] The farthing coal comes off a lighter at the pier foot, by the Customs House. The crier's in the Rag Market by day.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=office|commons world.mem.mq_note=open priority=2] Anything paid in this city is written twice. If the Counting House lost a line, the Records Office kept it.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=estate|sump world.mem.mq_larder=open priority=2] There's an old coal chute behind Timberland Court, round the back wall. Small enough for a pup, they say.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.mq_nets=open priority=2] Tracks off the landing go up the bank, not out on the water. Up toward the Glasswater road, where the rough lot camp.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.mq_blight=open priority=2] Black leaf at Meresend. Old folk say burn it at dusk with the wind behind you. City folk sell a wash. Pick your fool.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.mq_bolt=open priority=2] New linen smells of size. If a bolt's gone walking, follow your nose from the Linen Shed door.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.mq_axles=open priority=2] A carter's in the mud below Longmead Mill. Needs an axle, two planks, and someone to stand by her at dusk.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.mq_bear=open priority=2] A bear in the bee garth. It lies up in the wood west of the hives. Go in daylight, and go in numbers.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.mq_casks=open priority=2] Casks out of the vineyard cellar at night. The cart ruts go west toward the road, where that rough camp sits.
say[here.region=fenshore self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.mq_lights=open priority=2] The fowler on Withy Creek sees the lights closest. Ask him first. He says one stank of eel oil.
say[here.region=saltwell self.from=saltwell world.mem.mq_raker=open priority=2] In a salt wind, walk with the sun on your left and the pans will bring you home. That is what the old ones say, my friend.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.mq_salt=open priority=2] The salt wagon's due home across the Waste. If you've teeth, the dry wash is where the carter will want them.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.mq_names=open priority=2] If you're going to the Mirebridge crossroads, go at dusk. That's when the old village said its names. By the market cross, it is.
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.mq_cedar=open priority=2] A cedar windthrown across the Sound Road below the cut, mm? The loggers have the ropes and the know-how; ask them.
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.mq_props=open priority=2] Rotten props went into the low drift this week. The shop knows who bought the good cedar, if you ask it right.
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.mq_oil=open priority=2] Want to be on the lamp-oil list? Tallow from the kill, rendered at the shop. Ibex in the high valley give the best.
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.mq_logs=open priority=2] Logs off a broken raft fetch up on the south shore of the Sound. Shingle and shallows, west of the Soundside landing.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.st_wagon=open priority=2] The wagon road to Coldwater runs under the Alder Mere knoll. That's where the lamp is, and where they wait.
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.st_cloak=open priority=2] The first stage below the Pass is where the Captain's men sit by the road, stone. Go in a pair.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.st_relief=open priority=2] If the road north's watched, go round over the downs. Long, but nobody sits up there.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.st_ice=open priority=2] If you sit the ice, sit it by the Upper Mere shed, late, and keep still. It rings in the small hours.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.st_bell=open priority=2] The bell's cart stands a night west of here on the road. Somebody should keep that stage till dawn.
say[here.region=saltwell self.from=saltwell world.mem.lq_salt=raided priority=2] If you ride with the salt, carry water. The raiders wait where the flats turn to dune, and they run from a crowd, by salt and water.
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.lq_cedars=dying priority=2] Sit up in the old stand when the night's dark, mm? The night crew comes in by the ravine and goes out by the Sound.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.lq_brown=rustled priority=2] Sit the Greyteeth fold in the dark hours, eh? The rustlers come in the middle of the night, and they run from more than three of us.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.lq_silver=clipping priority=2] Weigh your pennies on the anvil scales before you take them. Light coin's coming down the High Road, and top-weight liars with it.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.lq_vines=blight priority=2] If you hunt the boar, go in by the Southwood stream. They come up the rows from there, full-bellied and slow.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=sump self.from=ridgemere world.mem.lq_runnel=fever priority=2] Boil Runnel water before the pups drink it. The cough's from the water, not the damp. The honest apothecary sells thyme syrup at cost.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=sump self.from=ridgemere world.mem.lq_runnel=fever priority=2] If the infirmary's out of syrup, the preserver at the Honey Crock can brew it. Bring her herbs; she's honey enough.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=wharf self.from=ridgemere world.mem.lq_wreck=lamp here.weather=fog priority=2] Fog like this, watch the North Headland, not the Mole. The sailors swear there's a second light down on the rocks.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=wharf self.from=ridgemere world.mem.lq_wreck=lamp priority=2] If you go out on the headland at night, go two together. Somebody lights a lamp on the rocks, and the salvage gangs come after.
say[self.from=ridgemere world.mem.lq_post=running priority=2] If you carry the Couriers' tube, hand it on at the square. Fresh legs beat proud ones, and bandits watch the long roads.
say[here.region=fenshore self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.lq_eels=weir priority=2] Go to the weir at dusk with friends and a strong back, no? The guards run when they're outnumbered, and the stakes come out easy in the mud.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=sump self.from=ridgemere world.mem.lq_thief=walking priority=2] There's an old street under the Heights, from before the walls. The Sunken Street. Folk say it runs further than anybody's walked.
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.lq_hearths=undersold priority=2] If you go after the char thieves, go at night and go below the tarn. They dry what they steal by a fire, cousin, and a fire shows.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_coin=thin priority=3] The town purse is thin this week. Errands are still paid, in bread if not in coin.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_coin=thin priority=3] Purse is thin as a holed net, eh? The errands still pay, in bread if not coin.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_coin=thin priority=3] The purse is short-weighed this week, #address#. Errands pay in bread till it's full weight again.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_coin=thin priority=3] The purse is blighted thin this week, #address#. You'll get bread, not coin, till it fills.
say[here.region=fenshore self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_coin=thin priority=3] Purse is boggy-low, no? Errands still pay, in bread if not in coin.
say[here.region=saltwell self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_coin=thin priority=3] The purse is dry this week, #address#. The work is paid in bread until it fills.
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_coin=thin priority=3] The purse is down to the bark, mm? Work's still paid, in bread if not in coin.
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_coin=thin priority=3] Purse is thin as a worked seam, #address#. You'll be paid in bread till it fills.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=sump world.mem.st_round=open priority=2] If you walk the Sump round of a night, keep to the posts and carry a light. The cutpurses wait in the dark between.
say[self.from=ridgemere world.mem.st_bounty=open priority=2] The broken camps come back where the roads cross the wild: Alder Mere, Glasswater, the Frosthollow road. The Watch pays for each one broken again.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.st_bounty=open priority=2] Camp's back by Glasswater, eh? The Watch in the city pays for it broken. Net and line, go in a pack.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.st_fair=open priority=2] Fair-goers on the north road this week. The gate guard wants it walked. Bandits know the fair days too.
say[self.from=ridgemere world.mem.st_posts=probed priority=2] Bands are testing the Line's posts of a night. Stand one from dark till first light, and take a friend.
# <<< Ninth Howl talk, part 2: news lines
say[world.event_words] It's all talk of #world.event_words#. | Have you heard? #world.event_words.capitalize#.
say[world.news] Word from #world.news_from#: #world.news#.
say[world.wagons=raided] A wagon was robbed on the road. Mind yourself out there.
say[world.death=recent] We buried one of ours this week. It's been quiet since.
say[world.wedding=recent] There was a wedding! The whole street turned out.
free
choice Any gossip going round? -> gossip
choice Is something troubling you? -> trouble
choice Did anyone speak up for me? [here.vouched=yes] -> vouch
choice I wanted to ask about your letter. [here.letter=yes] -> letters_said
choice Who won at the festival? [here.festival_won=yes] -> festival_said
choice What do the records say of this town? [here.records=yes] -> records
choice What's all this talk of the Moot? [world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called|reckoning|signals|howls|letters|lights|harvest|bell|moot] -> nh_story
choice I was wondering about something else... -> do open talk
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node gossip
say #gossip_none#
# >>> Ninth Howl talk, part 2 (gossip and helpful knowledge; generated, doc 86 §6.4): gossip lines
# The campaign: rumours, villain hints and warnings, by stage and dialect; the grace; the epilogue. No
# priority, so a fresh real claim (here.gossip=yes) still competes (cast-and-talk §5.1).
say[self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_debts=grace] The factors gave a moon's grace. Generous of them, they say. It only means the interest runs a month longer.
say[self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_debts=grace] A moon's grace from the factors, eh? Like letting a fish run with the hook still in. Deep and dark, it comes in all the same.
say[self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_debts=grace] A moon's grace on every note, #address#. Fair price, they call it. Weigh the interest, then tell me it's fair.
say[self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_debts=grace] The factors gave the debtors a moon's grace. Chaff and promises, #address#. The note's still due, only later.
say[self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_debts=grace] A moon's grace, no? Boggy sort of grace. The water's still rising, only slower.
say[self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_debts=grace] The factors gave a moon's grace, #address#. A grace you pay interest on is not a grace. It is a longer leash.
say[self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_debts=grace] A moon's grace on the notes, mm? Bark and branch, the rot keeps working under the bark.
say[self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_debts=grace] The factors gave a moon's grace. Dead rock talk. The note weighs the same, only colder.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=ridgemere] The old King's gone up to the Bright One. And they say the one keeping the Palace lamp still walks his Sump round.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=ridgemere] There's a camp on the Oakhaven road that won't starve out. Somebody's feeding it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=ridgemere] The notice on the Oakhaven board was signed with a grey paw-mark. Nobody signs like that who means well.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called self.from=ridgemere] A Moot! Blood and bread, I never thought I'd see one called.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_purse=greatly] The Counting House paid for the old King's wake. Fine wake. Long account.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_purse=household] The Queen's household paid for the wake from its own purse, they say. Bright One bless a house that pays its way.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=coldwater] A patrolman keeping the Palace lamp, eh? Still water runs strange in the city.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=coldwater] Wet ash on the wind from the Alder Mere side. That's no fisher's fire, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=coldwater] Don't take the Oakhaven road alone. Something's camped under the oaks, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_willa=alone] Our carter walked home alone. Nobody came for her. Muddied, that.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called self.from=coldwater] A Moot, eh? The old folk speak of one. Said it was the only time the city asked the lake anything.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=larkfield] A Watch guard keeping the Palace lamp? By the market cross, the Houses will have that weighed and short-weighed by Marketday.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=larkfield] Somebody's buying the Oakhaven road off the carters. Fair price? Not to the carters.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=larkfield] Wagons to the Sound Road go in pairs now. Scales and silver, I'd not send one alone.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=larkfield] The market beam weighs light, some say. Weights and measures, and the factors still want paying by the new moon.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called self.from=larkfield] A Moot! Every town a voice. That's the first fair market the city's ever held.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=southmeadow] The old King's gone up, they say. Sheaf and sickle, I hope the next one likes apples.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=southmeadow] Carters say the Oakhaven road's got a toll on it now, and no tollhouse.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=southmeadow] Don't send a cart north alone, neighbour. They wait for the lone ones.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called self.from=southmeadow] A Moot of every town? Ripe days for talkers, then.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] That lamp-keeper's got fen in his mouth, I hear. Talks like the old ones on the boardwalk, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] Mirebridge-born, they say, the wolf with the lamp. Dark One's mire, the drowned get a king at last.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] Grey paw-marks on the Oakhaven board, no? Boggy business, signing with a paw.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] Keep off the Oakhaven road alone, #address#. Something's sitting on it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=saltwell] The Summons reached the well, #address#. The well remembers who drew from it. We will see whether the city does.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=saltwell] A guard keeping the Palace lamp. In the oasis we would say: a well is kept by whoever draws the water.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=saltwell] Caravans say the north road has a keeper who is not the Watch. By salt and water, I mistrust a keeper with no face.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=saltwell] Caravans that walk the north road alone come in short, #address#. Walk in company, or wait for one.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=oakhaven] Slow news, the city. A king gone up a fortnight before the Sound Road hears it, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=oakhaven] Grey paw-mark on our board. Proper strange. Wolves who sign with a paw don't sign with a name.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=oakhaven] Don't walk the Oakhaven road alone. Bark and branch, we've lost a wagon already.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_logger=believed] Still a thief, the logger, if you ask the store. I don't ask the store, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=frosthollow] Patrolman keeping the Palace lamp. Deep strange. Keep your lamp lit, they say. Well, someone is.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=frosthollow] Somebody's paying carters for their days. In Frosthollow we call that buying a road.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=frosthollow] Don't take the Pass Road alone, #address#. Lamps where there's no house.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called self.from=frosthollow] A Moot. The city remembered the valley. Lamp and pick, it'll forget again by spring.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere] Chalk on the doors in the Sump. The Counting House wants every debtor's howl for the Moot.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_debts=eased] A wolf of the road worked off a neighbour's note and asked nothing back. That's the Sump I remember.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere] The Counting House master gives every debtor a moon's grace. Grace, he calls it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere] Don't sign anything the clerks bring round. Chalk washes off. Ink doesn't.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_debts=called] They called in every note at the new moon. Half the Sump's howl belongs to the Counting House now.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_ledger=shown] A ledger went to the Antechamber, and the Sump's doubled debts are struck. Bright One keep whoever carried it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_ledger=ash] Somebody burned a Counting House ledger, they say. Ash doesn't testify, but it doesn't lie either.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_loan=taken] The Crown took the Counting House's loan. Every small note paid, and the Crown in the book instead.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_loan=refused] The Queen's household turned down the Counting House's loan. The notes stand, but the Crown's its own.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=coldwater] Factors chalking doors in the city, eh? Out here we'd call that marking a net that isn't yours.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=coldwater] Counting House pennies at the carters' yard. Deep and dark, those coins swim upstream.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=coldwater] Don't lend your wagon days to a guard with his badge cut off, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=larkfield] Short-weighed, the lot of it. Fair price to you, they say, and the scale's got a thumb on it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=larkfield] The Counting House lends with one paw and weighs with the other. Weights and measures, I know a cheat's scale.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=larkfield] If a clerk asks you to sign for a neighbour, read it twice and sign nothing.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=southmeadow] Notes due at the new moon? Chaff and promises, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=southmeadow] The Counting House master wants every howl in the realm. Blight take him, he can't carry a tune.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=southmeadow] Don't let them chalk your door, neighbour. Scrub it before the moon's up.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] Owe a House a penny and they own your boots. Lucky we go barefoot in the fens, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] A clerk in the city smells of smoke. Fen-sure, some fires aren't for warming.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] Don't take the House's coin for your howl, #address#. Mirebridge sold its say once, and look where it got us.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=saltwell] A loan the borrower cannot refuse is not a loan, #address#. It is a leash.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=saltwell] The master of the Counting House has never once been thirsty. That is how you know a dangerous wolf.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=saltwell] Do not pledge your voice for coin, #address#. The well remembers who drew from it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=oakhaven] They chalk doors in the city, mm? We'd mark a tree that way before we felled it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=oakhaven] Bark and branch, a lender who wants your howl wants your whole tree.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=oakhaven] Don't sell your wagon days, old root. You'll want the road back.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=frosthollow] Captain's quiet. Too quiet. Dead rock talk, that note on the mine.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=frosthollow] The Counting House rider comes up the Pass Road. Lamp and pick, somebody wants his letters lost.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=frosthollow] If the mine captain offers you a share in anything, count your claws after.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_seam=crooked] The quota's met, they say, with ore that isn't ours. Black seam. Somebody'll pay for that.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=ridgemere] Somebody's gathering the lists of who pays the Watch. Mind whose name you say aloud in a taproom.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_lists=press] It's printed. The whole list, on every board. Half the Watch can't meet your eye.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_lists=sold] The lists went to the Counting House, they say. The sergeant's on the Harbour Gate now. Funny, that.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_lists=captain] The Watch lists went to the grey captain, they say. Every House on them is paying twice now.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_lists=lost] The Watch lists went into the river, they say. Half the Watch slept easy that night.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=ridgemere] Three Houses on every list, they say. One on none. Ask yourself why it needn't pay.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=ridgemere] The Cinder Gate looks away for a grey paw-mark. Don't trust that gate after dark.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=coldwater] Lamps on the downs, two long and one short. That's no fisher's light, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=coldwater] A captain in grey taking a mark a wagon, eh? Deep and dark, that's a toll with no tollhouse.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=coldwater] The camp above Glasswater comes back in threes. Don't go in alone, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=larkfield] A Watch you can buy is a scale you can lean on. Scales and silver, I'd like to see that list.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=larkfield] Two long and one short. Somebody's selling our wagon days, and the price is a lamp on a hill.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=larkfield] Don't buy a list from the fish hall. It's short-weighed paper.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=southmeadow] The fish-hall wolf sells papers, and they smell of fish oil. Blight take it, don't pay her a penny.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=southmeadow] Somebody in grey keeps the roads now, they say. Wormy sort of keeping.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=southmeadow] If you see two long and one short, don't wait to count again.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] In the fens the Watch never came at all, so nobody paid. Boggy sort of honesty, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] Grey paw-marks on every board now. Fen-sure, he's proud of it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] A lamp you can't see the house behind is a lamp you don't follow.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=saltwell] A Watch that is paid by a House guards that House's well, not yours, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=saltwell] A road kept by no one is kept for someone, #address#. Ask who the grey keeper keeps it for.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_captain=named] Caravans called him the keeper with no face. Now he has a name, they say, and a grey cloak.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=saltwell] Do not buy secrets that smell of fish, #address#. Sweet water does not smell of anything.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=oakhaven] Rot starts under the bark, mm? You don't see it till the tree's down.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=oakhaven] A captain of the roads with no road of his own. Windthrown sort of wolf, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=oakhaven] Don't walk under a lit knoll, old root. They're watching from up there.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=frosthollow] A harness turned up on the Pass Road, old and sooty. Deep strange.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=frosthollow] Somebody's lighting lamps on our ridges and it isn't us. Lamp and pick, I'd like a word with him.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=frosthollow] If you hear two long and one short from a ridge, #address#, you're already seen.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=ridgemere] Eight towns howling at dusk and one silent. The old folk say the ninth was the loudest.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=ridgemere] The Counting House is buying howls, they say. A penny a throat. Ask yourself what a bought Moot sounds like.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_relay=ran|broke] The ridge howled back two long and one short on the relay night. That wasn't ours.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=ridgemere] The Counting House says a bought howl still counts. Buy yours back if you sold it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_cough=tended] The King's daughter climbed the Hundred Steps without stopping. Somebody sat with her.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=coldwater] A gathering howl? We've one for the drowned, one for a catch and one for supper, and I'd not swear which, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=coldwater] Somebody wants the old howls lost, eh? Deep and dark, a Moot with no howl can't sit.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_relay=ran|broke] False howls off the ridge, two long and one short. Deep and dark, he even steals our singing.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=coldwater] Don't howl the burying one at a wedding. It's been done. It was awful, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=larkfield] Larkfield's howl goes up at the end like a price. Scales and silver, it's the best one.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=larkfield] A howl from the ridge, they say, and it wasn't from any town. Somebody's put a price on our song.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=larkfield] If you've sold your howl to the Counting House, buy it back. It's worth more than a note.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=southmeadow] Our gathering howl? Blight take it, I've only ever known the harvest one.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_howl=found] A good harvest of a night! Half the vale came out to howl.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=southmeadow] Somebody chiselled a name off the Sunfields stone. Wormy business, that.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=southmeadow] Don't sing at the stone of a night unless the sky's clear. The cellar hand says so, and she's odd but right.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] Ninth howl's gone under, #address#. Mirebridge got drowned, and the drowned don't howl. Or do they, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] The Houses struck Mirebridge off the rolls. Struck it off so the Moot could never sit, they say.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] Don't sing the drowned howl on the boardwalk of a night. The old ones don't like it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=saltwell] The old one at the salt pans keeps the well's roll, #address#. Every caravan that ever drank is in it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=saltwell] A howl that answers from a ridge with no town under it is a mirage, #address#. Do not follow it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=saltwell] Do not hurry an old wolf's song. Saltwell begins nothing in a hurry.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=oakhaven] Our howl's slow and it climbs, like good bark. Come by the square at dusk, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=oakhaven] Somebody's teaching false howls from the ridges, mm? Rotten at the root, that.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_relay=ran|broke] False howls on the relay night, they say. Somebody's got lamps and a throat.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=oakhaven] The relay night wants a wolf at every post. One gap and it limps, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=frosthollow] In Frosthollow the warning howl goes low, so it carries down the shafts. The gathering one's lower still.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=frosthollow] Deepvein wolves knew a howl too, once. Nobody's heard it since the deep winter.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=frosthollow] Don't go onto Highmere alone, #address#. The ice keeps what it takes.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_silver=greatly] The silver went to the Counting House. Black seam. The mine's charter is a Greatly note now.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=ridgemere] Someone's carrying every letter for the Grayrock lord out to his road at last. Forty of them.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_grayrock=home] The Grayrock lady walked out to the Wharf gate. Didn't even put her hood up.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=ridgemere] Some of those letters are toll receipts, they say, signed with a grey paw. Grayrock pays the roads to stay shut.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_toll=cried] The herald cried a Grayrock toll receipt on the square. The Sump cheered. The Wharf didn't.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=ridgemere] Fell wants the Rainward Hills, and Fell's green is on the wolves driving stakes. Mind the cut.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=coldwater] Bounders in green on the Oakhaven road, eh? Fishers don't drive stakes into the ground.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=coldwater] Green cloaks and grey lamps, together. Deep and dark, who's paying whom?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=coldwater] Black cloaks on the Pass Road, eh? Wardens, they say. Fair winds to whoever they've come for.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=larkfield] Fell wants the hills. Fell wants everything with a price on it, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=larkfield] Grayrock pays one mark a wagon on the High Road. Scales and silver, to whom?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=larkfield] Don't take a Fell errand without reading it. Fellhall has more rooms than doors.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=southmeadow] A lord who's never home is like a vine never pruned. All runners, no grapes, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=southmeadow] Fell's green cloaks are driving stakes in Oakhaven's cut. Blight take them.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=southmeadow] Don't trust a wager in the Fell distillery. The house always drinks first.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] Forty letters and not one answered. In the fens we'd call that a very wet postbag, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] Grey paw-marks on the lord's toll receipts. Boggy coin, that.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] Don't step between Fell and Oakhaven, #address#. Both sides have axes.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=saltwell] The well remembers who drew from it. The lord has drawn for six years and never come back to the well.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=saltwell] A House that pays the roads to stay shut buys a thirst for everyone else.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=saltwell] Black cloaks on the Pass Road, #address#. If you carry a Gift, carry it quietly.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=oakhaven] Walk the bounds with us? Mark every ninth cedar and the old boundary stone, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_hills=oakhaven] Good bark, those wolves. The cut's ours yet. Root well.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_hills=fell] Fell's hills now. Windthrown, the lot of us. Oakhaven howls against Fell at the Moot.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=oakhaven] Wolves in Fell green on the cut, and the Captain's lamps behind them. Same paws, different cloaks, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=oakhaven] Don't argue with a bounder alone, old root. They come in threes.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=frosthollow] Three black cloaks came down the Pass on Stoneday. Didn't take their boots off at the Pass House. Deep strange.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=frosthollow] The Captain's bounders wear Fell green in the west, they say. Grey up here. Same wolves.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=frosthollow] Don't lie to a black cloak, cousin. Don't tell them more than's true, either.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=ridgemere] The Houses are at each other's throats, and a black cloak sits in the Antechamber listening to all of it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_quarrel=fell_timber] The Timberland works burned in the night. Every smith in the Cinders swears it wasn't them.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_quarrel=houses_greatly] There's a run on the Greatly Bank. The masons have walked off the Yard.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_quarrel=greatly_grayrock] Grayrock's closed the Wharf to Greatly stone. The Wharf's idle and the Yard's shouting.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_quarrel=against_crown] The Council wants the lamp-keeper gone before the Moot sits. Petitions on every desk.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=ridgemere] A black cloak at the Antechamber, and every House shouting. Somebody's glad of the noise.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=ridgemere] Cudgels in House colours on the roads out of the city. Walk round them.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=coldwater] Houses at each other in the city and lights in the fens. A good season to mend nets, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=coldwater] Lamp oil in the reeds. Deep and dark, the same lamps as on the ridges.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=coldwater] Don't follow a warm light in the fens, neighbour. Cold ones only, they say.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=larkfield] A black cloak on the Fen Road, and the price of a room on the Long River just doubled.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=larkfield] Plunder up the river by night. Weights and measures, somebody's fencing the Captain's take.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=larkfield] Don't buy cheap wool from a fen boat. You'll be buying it twice.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=southmeadow] Fen boats on the Long River by night, no lamps lit. Blight take them, a Larkholm carter lost a cart of honey.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=southmeadow] The Captain's southern company wades the fens with float lamps. Wormy trick.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=southmeadow] If you walk the fens by night, take a friend and a lamp you won't light.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] Lights in the reeds every night now, no? The old ones say the drowned want their names said.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=mirebridge|fenshore here.weather=fog] Dry feet. Mizzle's up. If you see a light, follow it, but only the cold ones, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_lights=laid] Dark marsh and dry feet. The priest from the city said every name.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_lights=turned] They used the drowned for bait. Dark One's mire, we'll pay for that.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] Float lamps in the reeds, fen-sure. The drowned never needed lamps to walk.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] The potter's post went to a carpenter and the boardwalks whisper. Ask the records before you whisper too.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=saltwell] In the old way, #address#, you bring bread and salt to a House at war. Even a House needs to eat.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=saltwell] Lights in the fens, fire in the city, cudgels on the roads. A mirage of three, and one paw behind it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=saltwell] Do not hide a Gift from the black cloak and then use it in the open, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=oakhaven] The Houses are windthrown in a row this season, mm? One falls and takes the next.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=oakhaven] Cudgels in House colours at the Rainward camps. Proper strange that a House needs a camp.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=oakhaven] Don't take sides in the city's quarrel, old root. Take bread.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=frosthollow] Lights in the fens, fire in the city. Black seam of a season.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=frosthollow] The Captain's company's gone south to the fens. Cold iron, we're glad and we're not.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=frosthollow] One howl from the Pass to the Waste, the black cloak wants. Our post's first. Don't let it be our fault.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=ridgemere] Every wolf who can stand is at the Larkfield ford. The city's quiet as a crypt.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_ford=held] They held the Larkfield ford three nights. Blood and bread, I'd have liked to see it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_ford=burned] The ford burned, and Larkfield's houses with it. The realm will be short of bread before spring.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=ridgemere] The Counting House is buying Longmead grain at siege price. Somebody always profits.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=ridgemere] Wolves carrying sacks from Longmead to the Counting House. Don't be one.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=coldwater] The Captain's at the ford, eh? Then the downs are quiet. Fair catch, for once.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=coldwater] Lamp-black at the ford too, they say. Same lamps as on our ridges.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=coldwater] If the ford burns, the whole realm's short of bread. Help it hold, neighbour.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=larkfield] Every sack in Longmead's gone to the ford walls. Scales and silver, I never thought I'd see grain for a rampart.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_ford=burned] Short-weighed, all of it. The year, the bread, the lot.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=larkfield] The Captain's companies took the Downs Road barns. Weights and measures, he's counted our grain before we have.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_captain=parley] The Captain parleyed at the truce lamp. A wolf with a reason, and a reason's worse than a price.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=larkfield] Don't cross the ford after dark unless you're standing it, #address#. Both banks are watching.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_truce=broken] Somebody struck under the truce lamp. Weights and measures, the whole Downs is talking.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=southmeadow] Every cart in the vale's gone north with something for the ford. Sheaf and sickle, the press house is empty.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_runner=came] The runner came at midnight, howling the new howl. We knew it! Sheaf and sickle, we went.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=southmeadow] The Captain's companies took every barn on the Downs Road. Wormy wolves.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=southmeadow] Don't wait for a runner if you see smoke from the ford. Go.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] The river company comes up through the reeds. Boggy fighting, that.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_sloe=turned] Fen boats bringing grain upriver now, no? Not plunder. That's new.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] The Captain's a Deepvein wolf, they say, from the high valley. Long way to come for a ford, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] Keep off the Long River banks by night. They're all fighting there.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=saltwell] Salt and water for the wolves at the ford, #address#. The well gives to those who stand.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=saltwell] A captain who parleys has a grievance, not a greed. By salt and water, that is harder to buy off.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=saltwell] Do not leave the pool unwatched while the south is fighting.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=oakhaven] Half the cut's gone south to the ford, mm? The cedars can wait. Wheat can't.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_captain=parley] Old Oak, a captain who parleys. That's a wolf with a reason, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=oakhaven] Deepvein, they say. Turned out in the deep winter. Rotten thing to do to a wolf, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=oakhaven] Don't go to the ford without bandages, old root.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=frosthollow] The Captain's a Deepvein wolf. Lamp and pick, I could have told you. Nobody shared oil with Deepvein.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=frosthollow] Deepvein. The deep winter. The mine house door. Black seam, we all knew.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=frosthollow] Don't say Deepvein in the Lamp and Pick unless you mean it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=ridgemere] Everyone's asking what the Chancellor wept over in the Rain Hall. Turns out half the city saw him do it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_writ=read] The old King wrote it down: the Sump's own peace-keeper keeps the lamp until a Moot. So it was no accident.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_oskar=confessed] The Chancellor stood before the Council and said it all. The Counting House's debt, the order, the lot.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_bell=lost] They lost the bell through the ice. The Upper Mere kept it. Some say that's where it belongs.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=ridgemere] The Counting House master told the Chancellor to lose it, they whisper. Lose a King's writ!
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=ridgemere] An old rag-mill hand is selling what she saw. Get there before she gets to the City Office.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=coldwater] Hear that? Under the ice. Bright One's tide, it's ringing.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_bell=rung] Net and line, they raised it! Green as a pike and loud as a gale, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_mere=still] The whole mere's still. I've never seen it so. Calm water to her.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=coldwater] The black cloak watches the mere all day. Deep and dark, what's she looking for?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=coldwater] Don't walk the black lane on the ice, neighbour. It never freezes, and nobody says why.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=larkfield] A writ lost for a debt. That's the dearest paper ever bought in Ridgemere, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=larkfield] The Counting House hid the old King's writ. Weights and measures, there's a cheat's scale for you.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=larkfield] Don't go out on the Upper Mere ice alone, #address#. Weights and measures, ice doesn't bargain.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_ford=burned] Send bread to Larkfield before you send iron to the bell.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=southmeadow] The old King wanted all of us to choose? Sheaf and sickle, I'd best think what I'll say.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=southmeadow] Somebody bought a King's writ with a debt. Wormy, wormy business.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=southmeadow] Don't go out on the Upper Mere ice unless the skipper says it holds.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] Our bell, under all that ice. Mud and eels, I'd walk the whole Long River to hear it, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_oskar=fled] The Chancellor ran down the Fen Road and stopped where Mirebridge used to stand. Even the drowned didn't want him, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] The Houses struck us off the rolls and hid the King's writ. Same paws, fen-sure.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] Don't stamp on the ice when you listen, #address#. The bell's not the only thing under it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_bell=cracked] They rang it cracked. Don't laugh. It's still ours.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=saltwell] A King writes "let the realm choose", and the Houses hide it in the dark. The Houses hid it, #address#, not the King.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=saltwell] A Chancellor weeping over a paper means someone made him hold it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=saltwell] A pup who calls water is a gift and a danger, #address#. Do not hide her carelessly.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=oakhaven] Old Oak. The old King planted something deep before he fell, mm? Now we see the shoot.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=oakhaven] The Counting House paid for a writ to be lost. Rotten at the root, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=oakhaven] Don't trust a sale of secrets on the Sump Stairs. Somebody's paying both ends.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=frosthollow] Our iron's in the bell's yoke. Cold iron for a cold bell. Lamp and pick.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=frosthollow] On the Moot night the Pass is his, the notice says. The Captain writes like he means it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=frosthollow] Nobody goes down alone, and nobody comes up without counting the others.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=ridgemere] Every town's sending its howl to the Moot. Ours goes to whoever kept the peace best.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_moot=midwinter] The Midwinter Moot! Every post on the Line wants a keeper, and every keeper wants a coat.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_moot=nine_howls] The Moot of the Nine Howls, they're calling it. Nine towns, one night, one howl.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_dagfinn=stands] The lamp-keeper will stand at the Moot. A Sump wolf, standing!
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_dagfinn=steps] The lamp-keeper's stepping back, they say, and asking the Moot to choose. A Sump wolf who doesn't want a crown.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=ridgemere] The Counting House master says he's already counted his voices. Make sure he's counted wrong.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=ridgemere] The Captain says the Pass is his on the Moot night. If the north arm fails, the trunk starts short.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_bell=rung|cracked] The big thing's going to the city for the Moot. It rang once on the road, they say. On its own.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_moot=midwinter] A Midwinter Moot, eh? The mere's froze hard, and a howl carries over ice.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=coldwater] The Counting House has bought howls. A bought howl's a muddied one, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=coldwater] If the howl stops at the mere post, it's not over. The next post can take it from two back, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=larkfield] Our voice to the Moot is bought by deeds, not silver. Scales and silver, that's a market I like.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_moot=midwinter] A Midwinter Moot. Weights and measures, the coldest market the realm's ever held.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=larkfield] Bought howls go to the Purse, three at most. Weights and measures, that's three too many.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=larkfield] Don't go to the Moot empty-pawed. Bring oil for a post.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=southmeadow] Southmeadow's voice is ready. A windfall of a Moot, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=southmeadow] The Counting House would crown a debt if it could. Blight take it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=southmeadow] If the pool's silent, we can still take the howl from two back. Don't give up on it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] Mirebridge has a voice again, no? Dry feet to every wolf who carried it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_lights=faded] The Council would cast our voice if we're silent. The Council struck us off. Boggy justice.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=mirebridge|fenshore] The crossing post's out in the open. Don't stand it alone if there are cudgels about.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=saltwell] Stand by the pool when the night falls, #address#. Saltwell starts the south road's howl.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=saltwell] A crown bought with debts is a well with salt in it, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=saltwell] If Saltwell is late, the whole south arm is late. Do not be late, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=oakhaven] A handful of wolves and one voice. That's a lot of shade for a small grove, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=oakhaven] The Counting House would buy every voice in the grove, mm? Rotten at the root.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_hills=fell] Oakhaven howls against whoever Fell backs. The hills went to Fell, and we've long roots.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=oakhaven] If the road post goes quiet, the square can't carry. Fill both, old root.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=frosthollow] Frosthollow starts the howl at the Pass. Lamp and pick, we'll be heard.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=frosthollow] The Captain's band gathers at the Pass the night before. Cold iron, there'll be a fight.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=frosthollow] If the Pass falls silent, the north arm's two posts short. Don't let it, #address#.
say[self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_crown=ottilie] Bright One keep the Queen. And the lamp-keeper beside her, bless his flat feet.
say[self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_crown=lamp] A Sump wolf at the lamp, by the realm's own howl. Blood and bread, I howled for him.
say[self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_crown=regency] No crown at all, and a Moot every year. I'll believe it when it sits twice.
say[self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_crown=regency world.mem.nh_moot=midwinter] No crown at all, and a Moot every Midwinter. I'll believe it when it sits twice.
say[self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_crown=bought] The Counting House has the realm now. They call it a Protectorate. I call it a debt with a crown on.
say[self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_concord=answers] The black cloak tore the Keeping at the Bay Light. The Wardens are going home.
say[self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_concord=bends] Wardens in every silent town by spring. We were too quiet, somewhere.
say[self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_captain=turned] The Grey Captain went back over the Pass with the coin. To fetch the Deepvein families down, they say.
say[self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_captain=beaten] They held the Grey Captain a day in the Keep's cells and judged him at the Moot's end. It's on the Market Square board.
say[self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_howl=ran] We answered, eh? Glasswater answered! A howl over the water.
say[self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_crown=ottilie] A Queen who coughs in the damp. She'll want a lake wolf's soup. Calm water.
say[self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_crown=lamp] The lamp-keeper's a fen wolf. Close enough to the lake. Fair catch.
say[self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_crown=regency] A Moot every year, eh? The city asking the lake what it thinks. Deep and dark, I'll get used to it.
say[self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_crown=bought] Bought, eh? Muddied water all the way up.
say[self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_concord=holds] One black cloak at the Grey Gull till spring. Fair winds to her.
say[self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_howl=ran] Larkfield answered on the dot. Sold, to the realm.
say[self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_crown=ottilie] A Queen who carries her own petitions. That's full weight.
say[self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_crown=lamp] A patrolman king. By the market cross, the Houses are still weighing it.
say[self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_crown=regency] No crown, and a market of voices every year. Fair price.
say[self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_crown=bought] Short-weighed realm. The Counting House kept the scales.
say[self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_captain=beaten] They led the Grey Captain down the Pass Road. Weights and measures, there'll be a judging worth watching.
say[self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_howl=ran] Ripe days. We howled the burying howl by mistake and nobody minded.
say[self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_crown=ottilie] A Queen! Sheaf and sickle, I'll plant her an apple tree.
say[self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_crown=lamp] The lamp-keeper's king. Good harvest to him.
say[self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_crown=regency] A Moot every year. More talk than a harvest dance, and longer.
say[self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_crown=bought] Blight take it. Bought, like a cart of chaff.
say[self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_concord=answers] The Wardens left by the Pass. A good harvest of a night.
say[self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_bell=rung] Our bell rang the Moot in. Fen-sure, the drowned heard it.
say[self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_crown=lamp] A Mirebridge wolf with the Palace lamp. Dry feet, the drowned have a king.
say[self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_crown=ottilie] A Queen, and the lamp-keeper beside her. Fen-sure, he'll keep her feet dry.
say[self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_crown=regency] A Moot every year, and Mirebridge has a voice in every one. Mud and eels!
say[self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_crown=bought] Bought. Boggy. We'll howl louder at the next Moot, no?
say[self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_lights=faded] The Council spoke for us at the Moot. The drowned won't forgive that.
say[self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_howl=ran] The howl came out of the dark to the oasis, #address#, and we sent it on. The well remembers.
say[self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_crown=ottilie] A Queen who answers petitions. Peace on her house.
say[self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_crown=lamp] A keeper of the peace with the lamp. By salt and water, that is what the old King meant.
say[self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_crown=regency] The realm draws from the Moot each year, like a well. Good.
say[self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_crown=bought] A crown bought with debt is a brackish crown, #address#.
say[self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_concord=holds] A black cloak at the Grey Gull, they say. Let her drink, and go in peace.
say[self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_howl=ran] A Moot night to remember, mm? It came through the cedars slow and climbing.
say[self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_crown=ottilie] A Queen, mm? Root well, Majesty.
say[self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_crown=lamp] The lamp-keeper keeps it. Proper.
say[self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_crown=regency] No crown. A council of everyone. Old Oak, that's a big grove.
say[self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_crown=bought] Bought. Rotten at the root. We'll grow round it.
say[self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_concord=answers] The black cloaks went back over the Pass. Shade on the realm.
say[self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_howl=ran] Held the Pass post. Cold iron and warm hearts, the both of it.
say[self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_crown=bought] Bought, then. Black seam. At the next Moot, we howl deeper.
say[self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_captain=turned] Deepvein's coming down in spring, they say. We'll share the oil this time.
say[self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_captain=dead] No quarter at the Pass. Lamp and pick, I'd rather we'd given one.
say[self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_captain=fled] The Captain went over the Pass with his coin. He'll be back. They come back for what they're owed.
say[self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_captain=beaten] They took the Captain down to the city's cells. Lamp and pick, I hope they judged him fair.
say[self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_crown=ottilie|lamp|regency] The realm howled from the Pass to the Bay Light. Deep quiet after. Then the bell.
# The quest packs: "someone did it" lines (quests-*.md, talk).
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_last=bread] The infirmary had its bread warm today. Even the nurse smiled, and she never smiles.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_last=herbs] The House of Mending had a full shelf today. Someone brought the healer an armful.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_last=ships] Somebody walked the old pawnshop wolf's littlest home from the piers. She talked about ships the whole way, I'd wager.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=wharf world.mem.sq_last=smoke] The north wharf smokehouse was going full today. You could smell it from the Fish Hall.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_last=resin] The tar pot at the Ropewalk was full today. The whole Cinders smelled like a pine wood.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=office world.mem.sq_last=records] There was a new paw at the copying desk today. Neat letters, they say.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=heights world.mem.sq_last=letter] A City Office letter came to one of our doors today. The servant took it like it might bite.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_last=candles] There were new candles beside the old King's on Restday. Somebody's kind.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=sump world.mem.sq_last=alms] Somebody gave me bread today and didn't ask a thing. Bright One keep them.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=commons world.mem.sq_last=stock] The provisioner's shelves were full by Marketday. Somebody's been gathering for her.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=sump world.mem.sq_last=greens] The greens stall had mushrooms today, fat ones. Someone knows the woods.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=works world.mem.sq_last=charcoal] The nail-hearths were roaring today. Someone fed them.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_last=stables] The Greatly horses were fed early today. That means the factors are riding.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=sump world.mem.sq_last=stables] Somebody's fattening the factors' horses. I'd sooner they went hungry, and so would every chalked door.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.sq_last=bell] Somebody rang the Clock Tower bell at first light. First time since the old King went up.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=sump world.mem.sq_last=bell] Heard the bell? I was at the Stairs before the fish carts for once.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=wharf world.mem.sq_last=lines] A wolf off the street took a ship's lines today, neat as a sailor.
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.sq_last=crate] A city wolf walked a crate to the stores, mm? The storekeeper counted it three times and found it whole.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=heights world.mem.sq_last=willow] Half the Heights smells of willow tea. Somebody brought the healer bark enough for every stiff knee on the street.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=sump world.mem.sq_last=pheasant] There's pheasant pie at the Cinder butchers. Somebody hunted the Rainward Woods.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=commons world.mem.sq_last=tarns] Soundings has fresh word of the tarns. The new chart's half done.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.sq_last=fox] Somebody saw off the Oakhurst fox. Fair catch, that. The hens are laying again.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.sq_last=landing] The Glasswater crew had warm bread today, eh? Somebody carried it down.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.sq_last=kettle] The Boiling House smoked all day. Somebody fed those kettles, fair winds to them.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.sq_last=apples] The orchard pup was found down the mere shore again. They ought to tie a bell on him, eh?
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.sq_last=pens] The Larkdowns pens have fresh straw. The ewes are settled, eh? Somebody walked the fold with him.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.sq_last=ewe] The Larkdowns ewe's home. Somebody followed her wool all the way up, eh?
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.sq_last=drag] The cedar's moving again, mm? The carter got his rope.
say[self.id=cty_tristram_rainridge world.mem.sq_last=drag self.from=oakhaven] Rope's good, mm? Somebody walked it from the city. Root well, whoever they were.
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.sq_last=venison] The cut ate venison today, mm? Proper food for proper work.
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.sq_last=sleep] The logger slept through the last storm, he says. First time in years, mm?
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.sq_last=passwood] The Pass House stack's high again. Somebody carried wood up, cousin.
say[self.id=cty_ebba_coalgate world.mem.sq_last=passwood self.from=frosthollow] The stack's high and the carters are singing. Deep thanks to whoever carried it, eh.
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.sq_last=clamp] The Upper hearths clamp came through whole. Somebody sat it, stone.
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.sq_last=goats] The quarry path's clear of goats. The limeburner's almost smiling, eh.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.sq_last=badger] Somebody shifted the Plumtree badger. Full weight to them, eh?
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.sq_last=swill] Southwood's pigs ate well today. The swineherd marked somebody down for it.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.sq_last=linen] The vats were full today. The printer's running sheets again, eh?
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.sq_last=race] The Longmead wheel's turning sweet again. Somebody waded in for the miller.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.sq_last=hives] The Larkholm bees were gentle as anything today. Somebody filled the smoker, bless them.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.sq_last=hare] The miller lost his hare wager. He's telling everyone he let them win.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.sq_last=garland] The square's garlanded right round. Good harvest to whoever brought the green.
say[self.id=cty_willa_wheatcombe world.mem.sq_last=garland self.from=southmeadow] The rope's round the square. Ripe, every bunch of it, and not one of them city-bought.
say[here.region=fenshore self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.sq_last=nets] The Dune warren has new nets. Somebody brought the warrener cord, fen-sure.
say[here.region=fenshore self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.sq_last=pans] The Fenside pans came up white today. Somebody hauled her wood, fen-sure.
say[here.region=fenshore self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.sq_last=clay] Fresh clay at the kilns today, the grey Mirebridge kind. You can tell it by the smell.
say[here.region=fenshore self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.sq_last=plank] The boardwalk by the Heron's whole again. Dry feet, for a change.
say[here.region=saltwell self.from=saltwell world.mem.sq_last=salt] Salt came in to the stores today, carried on foot. Blessings on the wolf who walked it.
say[here.region=saltwell self.from=saltwell world.mem.sq_last=rabbits] The Ochre vines are safe a while. The vine-tender is smiling, and she does not smile at the city.
say[here.region=saltwell self.from=saltwell world.mem.sq_last=caravan] Someone met the wagons at the well and broke bread with them. That is the old way, and it is good to see.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=estate world.mem.sq_last=fellhall] The Fellhall kitchen had its eggs in time today. The cook was nearly civil about it.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=estate world.mem.sq_last=grayrock] Every bed in Grayrock Hall had fresh linen today. The chamber keeper hummed, they say.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=estate world.mem.sq_last=bolt] Timberland Court has its new hangings. Greywool's bolt went up the hill on somebody's back.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.st_last=wake] The Soup Kitchen had fresh bread for every mourner today. The Square's baker sent it, and somebody carried it.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.st_last=summons] Hillside has its summons for the Moot. The herder read it twice and was late to the milking.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.st_last=stone] There's new stone at one of the Line posts. The masons' yard sent it, and the steward hasn't noticed.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.st_last=timber] Fresh poles at one of the Line posts. The coppice woodward's, by the cut of them.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.st_last=chorus] The two households are speaking again since the howl. Somebody carried mead and honey and said the right thing.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.st_last=bounds] The wolves on the bounds were fed today. The orchard keeper's bread, carried up into the hills.
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.st_last=stake] Another green stake on the logger's fire. Good bark, whoever pulled it.
say[self.id=cty_ingram_ashleaf world.mem.st_last=stake self.from=oakhaven] That stake burned sweet, mm? Somebody pulled it for the cut. Root well, whoever they were.
say[here.region=fenshore self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.st_last=lamps] The boardwalk lamps were lit in good time. Dry feet and true lights, fen-sure.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.st_last=blankets] The wolves at the ford have blankets now. From the Looms, carried down full weight.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.st_last=feed] The burned houses by the ford had bread today. Longmead grain, carried in.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.st_last=haul] The haulers at the Upper Mere shed had bread today, and fish besides. Somebody carried it up, eh?
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.st_last=benches] There's a new bench on the Square for the Moot. The fen carpenter's work, they say.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.mq_lamps=dark] The Sump lamps go out by midnight now. Somebody's thirsty for oil, and it isn't the lamps.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.mq_lamps=reported] They found who was draining the Sump lamps. One of the lamplighters himself, they say. Forty years he lit that round, and that's how it ends.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.mq_lamps=shared] Two lamplighters on the Sump round again. Lit right down to the Knucklebones steps, and about time.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=works|sump world.mem.mq_tally=open] Wagons out through the Cinder Gate after dark, and not a seal on them. Grey paw on the tally, they say.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.mq_tally=nailed] Somebody nailed a tally board to the Cinder Gate. Grey paw on it. The Grayrock clerks walk round the long way now.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=office world.mem.mq_tally=customs] The customs collector's had a tally brought in. A fine on a House, if the Council lets it stand.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=wharf world.mem.mq_wharf=paid] The Grayrock steward paid a widow's due. First time in living memory. Somebody walked in with the rope order.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.mq_wharf=named] There's a new name at the Chapel of the Tide, twenty winters late. The priest read it between the bells.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.mq_sunken=customs] The Customs House pulled a smugglers' cache out of the Sunken Street. Two pups found it hunting ghosts.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=sump world.mem.mq_sunken=poorbox] The Cathedral's poor box had silver beads in it on Restday. Nobody knows where from, and the priest isn't saying.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=commons world.mem.mq_coal=open] Coal at a farthing a sack, cried up and down the street. Wet as a herring. Two chimneys caught this month.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.mq_coal=reported] The Watch fined a coal crier for wet slack. Northgate chimneys are drawing clean again.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=sump world.mem.mq_coal=dry] The coal crier in the Rag Market sells dry now. Dearer, mind. Somebody made him take his wet sacks back.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.mq_note=proved] A cooper's note, proved paid out of the Counting House's own crossed-out line. They say the clerk had to sign for it.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=sump world.mem.mq_note=paid] Somebody paid a cooper's note at the Counting House for him. Twenty pennies. There's still kindness about, then.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=estate world.mem.mq_larder=open] The Court's hall larder comes up a loaf short every morning. Rats, they say. Tidy rats.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=estate world.mem.mq_larder=barred] They barred the old coal chute at the Court. The larder counts true again, and nobody's saying why.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=sump world.mem.mq_larder=basket] A basket by the Timberland Court chute, Restdays. Somebody up there remembers the Sump.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.mq_nets=open] Nets cut three nights at Glasswater, eh? Somebody's fishing with a knife, and not from a boat.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.mq_nets=returned] The Glasswater catch came home off the road. Fair catch, that wolf. Net and line, I'd buy them a cup.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=ridgemere world.mem.mq_nets=sold] The Glasswater Inn's serving fish the landing families lost. Somebody won it back and sold it on, they say.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.mq_blight=burned] Three rows burned at Meresend. A hard choice, and the right one, eh? The rest of the orchard's clean.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.mq_blight=saved] A city wash saved the Meresend rows. I'd not have believed it. Bright One's tide, there's a first time.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.mq_blight=spread] The black leaf's in ten rows at Meresend now. Somebody trusted a city bottle. Muddied water, that.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.mq_still=open] House Fell wants the Coldwater Still. Sent a factor's letter, eh? Like a pike writing to a minnow.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.mq_still=fell] The Still's brandy goes out with a green seal now. Fell money. Fair catch for somebody.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.mq_still=ours] The Sheaf's pouring Coldwater brandy, full weight, fair price. No Fell seal on it. Scales and silver, good stuff.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=estate world.mem.mq_still=ours] A lake still turned down a Fell price, they say. The steward at Fellhall had to tell the Lady herself.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.mq_bolt=open] A bolt of Wharf linen gone between the Looms and the cart, eh? Somebody's thumb on the count.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.mq_bolt=back] The lost bolt's home at the Looms. Full count on the Wharf cart. By the market cross, that's how it should be.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.mq_bolt=worked] That Southwood lad's minding the Linen Shed door. Working off a bolt, they say. Fair price, I call it.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.mq_axles=casks_lost] Fell casks in the Longmead ditch and our flour in the bakehouse. Fair price, I call it. By the market cross, fair.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.mq_axles=flour_lost] The flour went in the mud to save Fell's casks. Short loaves this week, short-weighed in every way.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.mq_bear=killed] They killed the bee garth bear. Sheaf and sickle, it was a size. The hives are humming again.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.mq_bear=led_off] Somebody led the bee garth bear off with honey, past the clay pits. Not a drop of blood. Ripe days, that.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.mq_casks=told] The cellar hand sold spoiled casks to the road lot, they say. Wormy business. She's scrubbing barrels till harvest.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.mq_casks=spared] The vineyard casks came home from the road camp. Ripe work. The vine hand's handing out pebbles by way of thanks.
say[here.region=fenshore self.from=mirebridge|fenshore here.weather=fog world.mem.mq_lights=open] Lights on Withy Creek in this mizzle. The drowned walking, no? Mud and eels, I'll not go out.
say[here.region=fenshore self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.mq_lights=lamps] Float lamps on Withy Creek. Somebody's lamps, not the drowned. That's a right boggy thought, that is.
say[here.region=fenshore self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.mq_lights=quieted] Somebody went out and said the old words over Withy Creek. Dark as a sack since. Dry feet to them.
say[here.region=fenshore self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.mq_kiln=shared] Two potters on the one wheel at the kilns now. One leans his pots, one doesn't. Fen-sure we'll hear about it.
say[here.region=fenshore self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.mq_kiln=ludo] The kiln hand's teaching the new potter fen clay. Grumbling all the while, no? But teaching.
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.mq_kiln=ludo] One of ours keeps the kilns down at Fenshore now. Proper, that. Learning the bog clay, mm?
say[here.region=saltwell self.from=saltwell world.mem.mq_raker=told] A raker was selling Saltpan salt to the Waste Road wagons, and he confessed it. Brackish, but honest at the end.
say[here.region=saltwell self.from=saltwell world.mem.mq_raker=kept] A raker came in out of the salt wind with a stranger's paw on his shoulder. He has not said a word since. Truly.
say[here.region=saltwell self.from=saltwell world.mem.mq_salt=open] Toll-takers in the dry wash on the Waste Road. Five of them, they say. Mirage-talk, I hope. I fear not.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.mq_salt=fought] Salt came home across the Waste clean, no toll paid. Ripe news. Somebody saw the toll-takers off into the dunes.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.mq_salt=paid] Salt came in, but somebody paid the road lot to let it. Blight take them, it'll be dearer by harvest.
say[here.region=saltwell self.from=saltwell world.mem.mq_names=open] The eel trapper at the pans knows every Mirebridge name. He is looking for someone to carry them home, they say.
say[here.region=fenshore self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.mq_names=fen] Somebody said the Mirebridge names at the crossroads at dusk, then gave them to the old one on Withy Creek. Dry feet to them.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.mq_names=city] The mapmaker at Soundings has a list of Mirebridge names, brought up from the crossroads. A village on the map again, in ink.
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.mq_cedar=honest] The carter got through to the city, every stick delivered. Proper honest, that one. Poorer for it, mind.
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.mq_cedar=kept] The road lot took a load off the carter, they say. Odd. Never seen him look so easy about a robbery.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=commons world.mem.mq_cedar=kept] An Oakhaven carter came in a load short and swore the road wolves had it. His creditor's not best pleased.
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.mq_props=named] Somebody named the rotten props aloud in the Lamp and Pick. The mine house had visitors at first light, eh.
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.mq_props=quiet] Sound beams in the low drift, set before the shift. Nobody's saying whose. Deep thanks, whoever.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=works world.mem.mq_props=named] Frosthollow mine props turning up in a Cinders yard. Bought cheap, they say. Somebody up the pass is fuming.
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.mq_oil=shared] Another name on the lamp-oil list this year, and not a miner. Deep strange. Deep good, mind.
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.mq_oil=sold] Somebody rendered the tallow meant for the list and sold the oil in the city. Cold iron. Some folk don't know what a list is for.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=works world.mem.mq_oil=sold] Frosthollow lamp oil for sale on the Commons, three times the price. Burns clean, I'll say that.
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.mq_logs=open] The cut's raft broke up in the fog, mm? Logs all down the Sound shore. Somebody'll be hauling wet cedar.
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.mq_logs=home] The runaway logs came home to the cut. Somebody hauled them uphill wet. Proper, that.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=wharf world.mem.mq_logs=sold] Oakhaven cedar stacked at Soundside, bought as driftwood. The cut's not best pleased, they say.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=sump|commons world.mem.st_wagon=open] The carters won't take the Coldwater road. A mark a wagon, paid at the ridge, the notices said.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.st_wagon=ahead] The city wagon came in clean. Somebody cleared the road under Alder Mere ahead of it, eh? Fair catch.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.st_wagon=with] The city wagon came in with a wolf riding on the tail. No mark paid. Calm water, that.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.st_cloak=open] Black cloaks at the Pass House, eh? The road below Frosthollow wants looking at before they walk it.
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.st_cloak=cleared] Somebody cleared the road below the Pass. The black cloak walked down it like it was Restday, eh.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.st_relief=open] Larkholm's got flour and Larkfield's got none. Somebody's got to carry it, siege or no siege, eh.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.st_relief=road|downs] Larkholm flour at the Bakehouse, carried in by paw. Full weight, every measure. By the market cross, it's welcome.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.st_ice=open] The Larkdowns ewes stare at the mere all night, eh? Something rings under that ice.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.st_ice=bell] A shepherd took his rope to the Upper Mere shed. Says a wolf sat the ice and heard the bell. Net and line.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.st_bell=open] The bell's going down to the city in our felt, eh? Every ell woven here.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.st_bell=go] The old weaver's walking down to the city with the bell. Thirty years he's said it. Fair catch.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.st_bell=stay] The old weaver's staying for the Moot night. Says somebody has to remember the names.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.lq_salt=board] Salt's back at the old price. A provisioner up Northgate was buying robbed sacks, and the Market Board heard every word of it.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.lq_salt=bought] Salt's short-weighed and dear again. Somebody took coin to keep it so, and the market knows who.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.lq_salt=cart] The Saltwell cart sells off the tail-board now, full sacks at the old price. Ripe days for the pickling, #address#.
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.lq_cedars=contract] Grayrock pays Oakhaven for a mast a season now, proper money, felled by our own axes. Good bark, that bargain.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=wharf self.from=ridgemere world.mem.lq_cedars=returned] Somebody floated a lighter's worth of mast cedars back up the Sound. The shipwrights are spitting nails.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.lq_cedars=contract] They say the Oakhaven fellers stood up to the Wharf over their cedars, eh? Calm water to them.
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.lq_rustlers=grey] Grey cloaks on the Pass Road with Coldwater sheep. Cold iron, the camp up there eats well, cousin.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.lq_brown=slain] The Old Brown's down. A pack took it by Greytarn, they say. Bright One's tide, I'd not have gone near it.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.lq_brown=spared] The Greyteeth flock's on the high fold and the bear kept its rocks. Fair price all round, that.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.lq_silver=clipping world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called|reckoning] Every wagon comes home short-weighed, and the factors want their money by the new moon. Weights and measures, somebody's thumb's on the scale.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=commons self.from=ridgemere world.mem.lq_beam=board] The Market Hall's grain beam was false, they say. A Counting House beam. The warden put it before the Board himself.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=commons self.from=ridgemere world.mem.lq_silver=board] The Market Board broke a coiner's dies. An old jeweler, they say, with a factor's chalk on her door. Sad business, all of it.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.lq_silver=mercy] Somebody paid an old wolf's debt and broke her dies quiet. Light coin's gone and nobody's in the stocks. Fair price, that.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.lq_silver=cut] There's still light coin about, #address#. Weigh it twice. Blight take whoever's shaving it.
say[here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow world.mem.lq_vines=burned] They burned the south rows for the blight. No wine from them this year, but clean ground. Ripe days next year, Bright One willing.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.lq_vines=cured] Southmeadow saved its vines with bark and lime, they say. Fair-priced wine this year, if it's true.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.lq_vines=lost] Southmeadow wine'll be dear this year. The blight got past them, for all they tried.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.lq_runnel=covered] There's a cover over Cistern Court now, stone and timber. Wolves from all over carried for it, and the coughing's eased.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=sump self.from=ridgemere world.mem.lq_runnel=drained] The tanner dug a soakaway and the Runnel runs clean again. It smells of the sea now, not the kiln.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.lq_runnel=fever] They've a cough in the Ridgemere Sump, eh? From bad water. Calm water's a blessing, neighbour.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.lq_wreck=named] The Chapel of the Tide named a lighter crew the Wharf wrote down as cargo. The lamp on the headland's out.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=sump self.from=ridgemere world.mem.lq_wreck=watch] They've the headland wrecker in the cells. An old lamplighter. Half the Sump is sorry for her.
say[here.region=coldwater self.from=coldwater world.mem.lq_wreck=wharf] Grayrock turned out an old lamplighter over the wrecks, eh? Rough water for her.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.lq_post=couriers] The Couriers beat the wagons. Sound to Waste in a day, paw to paw. The Carters' Yard keeper bought the round, fair play to him.
say[here.region=saltwell self.from=saltwell world.mem.lq_post=couriers] The runners came over the Waste like water down a wadi. Peace on their pads, every one.
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.lq_post=wagons] Wagons won the post, cousin. Dead rock luck for the runners. Next season, they say.
say[here.region=fenshore self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.lq_eels=run] The eels are up Withy Creek again, thick as reeds. Mud and eels, it's a fair-dry season after all.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=wharf self.from=ridgemere world.mem.lq_eels=run] Eels are dear at the Fish Hall. Somebody pulled their weir out of the fens.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.lq_eels=shared] Fenshore has a share of the Fish Hall's eels now. Fair price, if you ask me.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=heights self.from=ridgemere world.mem.lq_thief=walking] They say a Quickened wolf walks through the Heights' walls and takes pledges. Lock your strongroom, for all the good it does.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.lq_thief=forgiven] Vance House let the Sump pledges go. A wolf put it to the lender plain, they say, and the lender listened.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.lq_thief=named] Ridgemere caught its wall-walking thief. A pup, they say, no Gift at all. Short-weighed magic, that.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.lq_thief=blinker] The Heights swear it was a Quickened thief. Somebody's writing to the Wardens. Bright One keep us all.
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.lq_hearths=undersold] Upper hearths charcoal at half price in the city. Dead rock luck, or somebody's hand in it. Deep, I'd say the hand.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=commons self.from=ridgemere world.mem.lq_hearths=contract] The charcoal store pays the hill colliers by the sack now. Dearer coal, and no strangers at the yard door.
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.lq_hearths=home] Frosthollow charcoal on the Frosthollow square, Marketday. Deep and plain, the way it should be, stone.
say[here.region=larkfield self.from=larkfield world.mem.lq_hearths=greenholt] Greenholt wagons carry the Upper hearths' charcoal too now. Fair price, if not full weight for the hill folk.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere self.quarter=sump world.mem.st_round=open] Somebody's walking the night round since the patrolman went up the Hundred Steps. Not the Watch. Just somebody.
say[here.region=oakhaven self.from=oakhaven world.mem.st_bounds=walked] Somebody walked all twelve bounds of the hills in a day, mm? Old Oak, the old folk did that.
say[here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere world.mem.st_bounds=walked] Somebody walked every bound of the Rainward Hills in one day. Let the Council argue with that.
say[here.region=frosthollow self.from=frosthollow world.mem.st_posts=probed] Somebody stood the Pass post the whole night through, cousin. Warm hearth to them. Deep quiet, that.
# <<< Ninth Howl talk, part 2: gossip lines
say[here.gossip=yes] They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Folk say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Don't quote me.
say[here.gossip=yes topic.claim_kind=theft|wanted] Keep your purse close. They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
say[here.gossip=yes topic.claim_kind=death] Sad news. #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#.
say[here.gossip=yes topic.claim_kind=violence] They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Steer clear, I would.
free
choice Is something troubling you? -> trouble
choice I was wondering about something else... -> do open talk
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node told
ask game.tell
say Is that so. | I'll bear it in mind. | Hm. So I'd heard, or near enough.
free
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node vouch
ask game.vouch
say Nobody's said a word for you that I've heard. | Not to me.
free
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node letters_said
ask game.letters
say My letter? I've written you none that I recall. | I don't remember writing to you.
free
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node festival_said
ask game.festival
say I didn't see who won. I was busy. | I couldn't tell you. I missed it.
free
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node records
ask game.records
say The records? I wouldn't know. Ask the town office. | I've never read them.
free
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node trouble
ask player.trouble
say #trouble_none#
free
each trouble in here.troubles max 2
choice #trouble.words# -> do trouble trouble.id ; then helped ; refused refused
choice I was wondering about something else... -> do open talk
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node helped
say #trouble_thanks#
mood pleased
free
choice I was wondering about something else... -> do open talk
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node way
say #way_ask#
say[here.places=0 priority=2] I couldn't tell you, I'm afraid.
each place in here.places max 6
choice How do I get to #place.title# (#place.kind#)? -> place
choice Actually, never mind. -> do open talk

node place
say #place.way#
free
choice What about somewhere else? -> way
choice Thank you. -> thanks
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node people
say Who are you after? | Who is it you want?
each person in here.people max 6
choice Where would I find #person.name#? -> whereis
choice Actually, never mind. -> hub

node whereis
ask game.where
say #topic.person_name#? I couldn't tell you where, just now. | I haven't seen #topic.person_name# about today.
free
choice What about someone else? -> people
choice Thank you. -> thanks
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node day
ask player.day
say Another day. Work, mostly. | The same as yesterday, near enough.
free
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node wanted
ask player.wanted
say Not that I've heard. The watch would know, not me. | Ask the watch, not me. I keep out of their business.
free
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node match
ask game.match
say Nobody I'd point you to just now. Try again of an evening, when it's busier. | Not just now. Come back when there's more about.
mood warm
free
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node introduced
say #topic.player#. I'll remember it. | #topic.player#, then. Good to know you. | I'll keep that, #topic.player#.
say[player.met=yes] #topic.player#. I'll remember it. And I'm #self.name#. | #topic.player#. I'm #self.name#. Good to know you.
say[pair.disposition=hostile|wary] Hm. #topic.player#. | If you like.
free
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node name
ask game.name
say I'm #self.name#. | #self.name#. And you are? | Folk call me #self.name#.
free
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node thanks
ask player.thanks
say You're welcome. | Not at all. | Any time.
free
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node refused
say #topic.why# | Hm. #topic.why#
choice I was wondering about something else... -> do open talk
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node unclear
say I'm not sure I follow you, #address#. | Come again? | You've lost me there. | I don't follow. Ask me plainer?
say[temper=short] Speak plainly, will you? | What? Say it so I can understand it.
say[temper=calm] I'm not sure I follow you, #address#. Ask me plainer, and I'll answer plainer.
say[warmth=warm] Sorry, love, you've lost me. Try me again? | I didn't quite catch your meaning. Again?
say[warmth=cold] I don't know what you're on about. | Make sense, or don't waste my time.
say[humour=merry] Ha! I've no idea what you mean. Try again. | You've tied my ears in a knot. Again?
say[humour=dry] Fascinating. I understood none of it. | I'll pretend I followed that.

node bye
ask player.bye
say #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#.
end

# ==================================================================================================================
# The Ninth Howl (Docs/Design/86-quests-and-the-ninth-howl.md section 6; artifacts/quests/design/cast-and-talk.md
# sections 1, 3 and 5). Every line and choice below is gated on talk memory the campaign writes (world.mem.nh_*,
# self.mem.nh_*, pair.mem.nh_*), so none of it shows until a key is set: by C8 talk.remember once engine Phase 1b
# lands, or by the DM by hand before that (the realm and town keys only; self.mem and pair.mem lines stay silent).
# A node whose words a chapter counts is marked "story-heard": the game writes `dialogue node` (actor the wolf,
# target the resident, detail the node id) whenever a wolf's window moves to it, and the chapter's trigger decides.
# Lines name no one: roles only. A line in a regional saying carries self.from, so it is said only in its own voice.
#
# The window map: news -> nh_story (the recap) -> nh_help, nh_who, nh_ask, one cast slot (one choice per cast member,
# disjoint by self.id, at most one a stage each), the Mirebridge scrap, the pledge, the backing, the chorus, the
# wharf names, and the two ways out: nine at most (Library::mostShown).
# ==================================================================================================================

node nh_story
say There's talk of little else. Ask me what you like. | It's all anyone talks of. What would you know?
# >>> Ninth Howl talk, part 2 (gossip and helpful knowledge; generated, doc 86 §6.4): nh_story lines
# By stage and dialect: rumours and thanks to the heroes (cast-and-talk §4; R, H). The recap is above.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=ridgemere priority=2] The old King's gone up to the Bright One. And they say the one keeping the Palace lamp still walks his Sump round.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=ridgemere priority=2] Whoever's carrying the Summons out to the far towns, blood and bread, the whole city owes them a cup.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_alder=cleared priority=2] Whoever broke the Alder Mere camp, the carters drink to them now.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called self.from=ridgemere priority=2] A Moot! Blood and bread, I never thought I'd see one called.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_purse=greatly priority=2] The Counting House paid for the old King's wake. Fine wake. Long account.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_purse=household priority=2] The Queen's household paid for the wake from its own purse, they say. Bright One bless a house that pays its way.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=coldwater priority=2] A patrolman keeping the Palace lamp, eh? Still water runs strange in the city.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=coldwater priority=2] Whoever walks the city's word up to the lake, calm water to them. We're not often asked, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_willa=home priority=2] Our carter's home! A wolf of the road walked her in. Calm water to them.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_willa=alone priority=2] Our carter walked home alone. Nobody came for her. Muddied, that.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called self.from=coldwater priority=2] A Moot, eh? The old folk speak of one. Said it was the only time the city asked the lake anything.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=larkfield priority=2] A Watch guard keeping the Palace lamp? By the market cross, the Houses will have that weighed and short-weighed by Marketday.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=larkfield priority=2] The market beam weighs light, some say. Weights and measures, and the factors still want paying by the new moon.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_alder=cleared priority=2] The Alder Mere camp's broken. Full weight to whoever broke it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called self.from=larkfield priority=2] A Moot! Every town a voice. That's the first fair market the city's ever held.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=southmeadow priority=2] The old King's gone up, they say. Sheaf and sickle, I hope the next one likes apples.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=southmeadow priority=2] Whoever walked the Summons all this way south, they'll have a cup of the new wine from me.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called self.from=southmeadow priority=2] A Moot of every town? Ripe days for talkers, then.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] That lamp-keeper's got fen in his mouth, I hear. Talks like the old ones on the boardwalk, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Mirebridge-born, they say, the wolf with the lamp. Dark One's mire, the drowned get a king at last.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] A Moot called by a fen wolf's lamp. Dry feet to the herald who said it out loud.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=saltwell priority=2] The Summons reached the well, #address#. The well remembers who drew from it. We will see whether the city does.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=saltwell priority=2] A guard keeping the Palace lamp. In the oasis we would say: a well is kept by whoever draws the water.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=saltwell priority=2] Whoever walked the Summons to the pool, may their well never fail.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Slow news, the city. A king gone up a fortnight before the Sound Road hears it, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Shade on whoever carries the city's word down the Sound Road, mm? Slow news, but welcome.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_logger=cleared priority=2] The logger's cleared. Somebody found the wool smelling of smoke, not sap. Good bark, that wolf.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_logger=believed priority=2] Still a thief, the logger, if you ask the store. I don't ask the store, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Patrolman keeping the Palace lamp. Deep strange. Keep your lamp lit, they say. Well, someone is.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Whoever walked the Summons up the Pass Road, lamp's thanks. The valley's not used to being asked.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called self.from=frosthollow priority=2] A Moot. The city remembered the valley. Lamp and pick, it'll forget again by spring.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_alder=cleared priority=2] The Alder Mere camp's broken, the carters say. Lamp's thanks to whoever went in.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere priority=2] Chalk on the doors in the Sump. The Counting House wants every debtor's howl for the Moot.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_debts=eased priority=2] A wolf of the road worked off a neighbour's note and asked nothing back. That's the Sump I remember.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_debts=eased priority=2] The lamplighter's note is paid. A wolf of the road did it. Blood and bread, the streets are brighter.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_debts=called priority=2] They called in every note at the new moon. Half the Sump's howl belongs to the Counting House now.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_ledger=shown priority=2] A ledger went to the Antechamber, and the Sump's doubled debts are struck. Bright One keep whoever carried it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_ledger=ash priority=2] Somebody burned a Counting House ledger, they say. Ash doesn't testify, but it doesn't lie either.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_loan=taken priority=2] The Crown took the Counting House's loan. Every small note paid, and the Crown in the book instead.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_loan=refused priority=2] The Queen's household turned down the Counting House's loan. The notes stand, but the Crown's its own.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere priority=2] Blood and bread to whoever lends a debtor a paw at her work and won't take a penny for it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=coldwater priority=2] Factors chalking doors in the city, eh? Out here we'd call that marking a net that isn't yours.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_debts=eased priority=2] A wolf of the road paid off a city note with work. Calm water, there's hope in the city yet.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=larkfield priority=2] Short-weighed, the lot of it. Fair price to you, they say, and the scale's got a thumb on it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_handbill=up priority=2] The handbill's on every board. A debt is not a voice. Sold, to whoever wrote it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=southmeadow priority=2] Notes due at the new moon? Chaff and promises, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_debts=eased priority=2] The new moon came up on paid doors, they say. Ripe days.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Owe a House a penny and they own your boots. Lucky we go barefoot in the fens, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Whoever works the city's lamplighter free of his note, dry feet to that one.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=saltwell priority=2] A loan the borrower cannot refuse is not a loan, #address#. It is a leash.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=saltwell priority=2] May the well never fail whoever frees the city's herald from her note.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=oakhaven priority=2] They chalk doors in the city, mm? We'd mark a tree that way before we felled it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=oakhaven priority=2] A wolf who frees a debtor and asks nothing back, mm? Good bark, that one.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Captain's quiet. Too quiet. Dead rock talk, that note on the mine.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Lamp's thanks to the road wolves hauling ore with us. The note's lighter for every load.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_seam=honest priority=2] The quota's met. A road wolf hauled ore with us. Lamp's thanks.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_seam=crooked priority=2] The quota's met, they say, with ore that isn't ours. Black seam. Somebody'll pay for that.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=ridgemere priority=2] Somebody's gathering the lists of who pays the Watch. Mind whose name you say aloud in a taproom.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_lists=press priority=2] It's printed. The whole list, on every board. Half the Watch can't meet your eye.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_lists=sold priority=2] The lists went to the Counting House, they say. The sergeant's on the Harbour Gate now. Funny, that.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_lists=captain priority=2] The Watch lists went to the grey captain, they say. Every House on them is paying twice now.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_lists=lost priority=2] The Watch lists went into the river, they say. Half the Watch slept easy that night.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_lists=bettany priority=2] The sergeant took the list to the magistrate. Door open, at noon. Blood and bread.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_dark=1 priority=2] No lamps on the ridges last night, the carters say. Blood and bread to whoever sat up there.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=coldwater priority=2] Lamps on the downs, two long and one short. That's no fisher's light, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_dark=1 priority=2] No lamps on the downs last night. Calm water to whoever sat on that ridge.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=larkfield priority=2] A Watch you can buy is a scale you can lean on. Scales and silver, I'd like to see that list.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_glasswater=open priority=2] The Glasswater road's open. Wagons in, wagons out. Full weight.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=southmeadow priority=2] The fish-hall wolf sells papers, and they smell of fish oil. Blight take it, don't pay her a penny.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=southmeadow priority=2] A wolf sat on a ridge all night so a wagon of ours came through. Sheaf and sickle, I'll stand them a cup.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] In the fens the Watch never came at all, so nobody paid. Boggy sort of honesty, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_dark=1 priority=2] Somebody put the ridge lamps out. Dry feet to them, wherever they're drying.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] A wolf of the road sat up on the ridges so the wagons could pass. Dry feet to them, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=saltwell priority=2] A Watch that is paid by a House guards that House's well, not yours, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=saltwell priority=2] The road to the well runs clear this week. May the well never fail whoever cleared it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Rot starts under the bark, mm? You don't see it till the tree's down.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_dark=1 priority=2] The knoll was dark last night. Somebody sat on it. Good bark.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=frosthollow priority=2] A harness turned up on the Pass Road, old and sooty. Deep strange.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=frosthollow priority=2] The Upper Mere post's going up. Cold iron, there's a light on the road that's ours.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=ridgemere priority=2] Eight towns howling at dusk and one silent. The old folk say the ninth was the loudest.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=ridgemere priority=2] Somebody's carrying the old howl from square to square. Blood and bread, it's been years since I heard it right.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_howl=found priority=2] The square came out at dusk and howled the old one right. The Bright One heard that, I'd say.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_cough=tended priority=2] The King's daughter climbed the Hundred Steps without stopping. Somebody sat with her.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=coldwater priority=2] A gathering howl? We've one for the drowned, one for a catch and one for supper, and I'd not swear which, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=coldwater priority=2] Somebody sat with the old ones and caught the howl off them. Calm water, that's patience.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_howl=found priority=2] Coldwater found its howl! Calm water, it went up like a rising fish.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=larkfield priority=2] Larkfield's howl goes up at the end like a price. Scales and silver, it's the best one.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=larkfield priority=2] A road wolf stood in our chorus and didn't miss a turn. Full weight, that.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_howl=found priority=2] Full weight! Larkfield howled the old one right and half the Downs came to hear.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=southmeadow priority=2] Our gathering howl? Blight take it, I've only ever known the harvest one.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_howl=found priority=2] A good harvest of a night! Half the vale came out to howl.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_stone=read priority=2] The stone's read, nine names, one chiselled out. Somebody went up four nights for it. Ripe days.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Ninth howl's gone under, #address#. Mirebridge got drowned, and the drowned don't howl. Or do they, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Somebody's carrying the old howl from town to town. Dry feet to them. The drowned would thank them.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=saltwell priority=2] The old one at the salt pans keeps the well's roll, #address#. Every caravan that ever drank is in it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=saltwell priority=2] A wolf of the road sat three Restdays with the old one at the pans. The well remembers patience, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_howl=found priority=2] The pool heard its own howl again. May the well never fail whoever sat still for it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Our howl's slow and it climbs, like good bark. Come by the square at dusk, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=oakhaven priority=2] A road wolf asked three old roots for the howl, slow and twice. Good bark, that one.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_relay=ran priority=2] Oakhaven answered on the relay night. Proper, it did.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=frosthollow priority=2] In Frosthollow the warning howl goes low, so it carries down the shafts. The gathering one's lower still.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_silver=crown priority=2] The silver came down the Pass Road and the Crown has it. Cold iron, the mine's got its charter.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_silver=greatly priority=2] The silver went to the Counting House. Black seam. The mine's charter is a Greatly note now.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=ridgemere priority=2] Someone's carrying every letter for the Grayrock lord out to his road at last. Forty of them.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_grayrock=home priority=2] The Grayrock lady walked out to the Wharf gate. Didn't even put her hood up.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_grayrock=home priority=2] The Grayrock lord's in the Antechamber, and the Council's whole. Blood and bread, the letters did that.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_wharf=heard priority=2] The wharf drowned were read out at the Chapel of the Tide, with the Grayrock lord standing. About time.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=coldwater priority=2] Bounders in green on the Oakhaven road, eh? Fishers don't drive stakes into the ground.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_hills=oakhaven priority=2] The cut's still Oakhaven's, I hear. Calm water.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=coldwater priority=2] Somebody walked the Grayrock lord's letters out to him, eh? Calm water, the wharf can sleep.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=larkfield priority=2] Fell wants the hills. Fell wants everything with a price on it, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=larkfield priority=2] The Grayrock lady smiled at the gate, they say. Full weight, that wolf who brought the thyme.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=southmeadow priority=2] A lord who's never home is like a vine never pruned. All runners, no grapes, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_hills=oakhaven|split priority=2] The hills are settled and nobody's dead. Ripe days, that's a fair end.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=southmeadow priority=2] Somebody's walking the twelve bounds for Oakhaven. Sheaf and sickle, I'd stand them a cup.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Forty letters and not one answered. In the fens we'd call that a very wet postbag, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_grayrock=home priority=2] The Grayrock lord came home. Dry feet to whoever dragged him.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Somebody carried the drowned's names to the Chapel of the Tide. Dry feet to them, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=saltwell priority=2] The well remembers who drew from it. The lord has drawn for six years and never come back to the well.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_wharf=heard priority=2] The names of the wharf drowned were read before the Grayrock lord. May every well remember them.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=saltwell priority=2] Somebody carried forty letters to a lord who never drinks at home. May their well never fail.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Walk the bounds with us? Mark every ninth cedar and the old boundary stone, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_hills=oakhaven priority=2] Good bark, those wolves. The cut's ours yet. Root well.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_hills=fell priority=2] Fell's hills now. Windthrown, the lot of us. Oakhaven howls against Fell at the Moot.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Shade on every wolf who walks the bounds with us. The cut remembers who stood on it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=oakhaven here.region=oakhaven world.mem.nh_cut=ours priority=2] The cut's ours for good. Good bark to every wolf who walked the bounds with us, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Three black cloaks came down the Pass on Stoneday. Didn't take their boots off at the Pass House. Deep strange.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Lamp's thanks to whoever walks the black cloaks' road with them. The Pass is long and the Captain's watching.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_envoy=walked priority=2] The black cloak walked down with an escort. Lamp's thanks to whoever kept her road.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=ridgemere priority=2] The Houses are at each other's throats, and a black cloak sits in the Antechamber listening to all of it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_quarrel=fell_timber priority=2] The Timberland works burned in the night. Every smith in the Cinders swears it wasn't them.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_quarrel=houses_greatly priority=2] There's a run on the Greatly Bank. The masons have walked off the Yard.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_quarrel=greatly_grayrock priority=2] Grayrock's closed the Wharf to Greatly stone. The Wharf's idle and the Yard's shouting.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_quarrel=against_crown priority=2] The Council wants the lamp-keeper gone before the Moot sits. Petitions on every desk.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=ridgemere priority=2] Somebody carried bread and salt to a House steward and the door stayed open. Blood and bread, the old ways.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_quarrel=peace priority=2] A wedding at the Greatly salon and every House at one table. Blood and bread, somebody kept the peace.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=coldwater priority=2] Houses at each other in the city and lights in the fens. A good season to mend nets, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_lights=laid priority=2] The fen lights stopped. They say the priest said every name. Calm water.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_cache=home priority=2] Our stillmaster got her wine back from the drowned causeway. A road wolf carried it. Fair catch.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=larkfield priority=2] A black cloak on the Fen Road, and the price of a room on the Long River just doubled.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_cache=home priority=2] A wolf brought the cache from the drowned causeway home, piece by piece. Full weight, that.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=southmeadow priority=2] Fen boats on the Long River by night, no lamps lit. Blight take them, a Larkholm carter lost a cart of honey.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_cache=home priority=2] The bee-keeper got her honey back! Some road wolf found it at the drowned causeway. Ripe days.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Lights in the reeds every night now, no? The old ones say the drowned want their names said.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=mirebridge|fenshore here.weather=fog priority=2] Dry feet. Mizzle's up. If you see a light, follow it, but only the cold ones, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_lights=laid priority=2] Dark marsh and dry feet. The priest from the city said every name.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_lights=turned priority=2] They used the drowned for bait. Dark One's mire, we'll pay for that.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_potter=cleared priority=2] The carpenter's cleared. The records say what they say, and he carves birds for the pups. Dry feet.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=saltwell priority=2] In the old way, #address#, you bring bread and salt to a House at war. Even a House needs to eat.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_quarrel=peace priority=2] Bread and salt reached every House. By bread and salt, the old way still works.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=oakhaven priority=2] The Houses are windthrown in a row this season, mm? One falls and takes the next.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_potter=cleared priority=2] The carpenter at Fenshore's cleared, they say. He carved a bird for whoever did it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Lights in the fens, fire in the city. Black seam of a season.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_lights=laid priority=2] The fen lights are laid, they say. Lamp's thanks to whoever walked the path.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=ridgemere priority=2] Every wolf who can stand is at the Larkfield ford. The city's quiet as a crypt.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_ford=held priority=2] They held the Larkfield ford three nights. Blood and bread, I'd have liked to see it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_ford=burned priority=2] The ford burned, and Larkfield's houses with it. The realm will be short of bread before spring.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=ridgemere priority=2] Every wolf who went down to the Larkfield ford, blood and bread, the city's proud of you.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_desmond=mercy priority=2] The dismissed guard stood the granary door all the third night. Mercy paid, for once.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=coldwater priority=2] The Captain's at the ford, eh? Then the downs are quiet. Fair catch, for once.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_ford=held priority=2] The ford held. Calm water to every wolf who stood in it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=larkfield priority=2] Every sack in Longmead's gone to the ford walls. Scales and silver, I never thought I'd see grain for a rampart.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_ford=burned priority=2] Short-weighed, all of it. The year, the bread, the lot.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_ford=held priority=2] Three nights held! Full weight, every wolf who stood.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=southmeadow priority=2] Every cart in the vale's gone north with something for the ford. Sheaf and sickle, the press house is empty.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_runner=came priority=2] The runner came at midnight, howling the new howl. We knew it! Sheaf and sickle, we went.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_ford=held priority=2] Southmeadow went to the ford. Ripe days, we'll tell it at every harvest.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] The river company comes up through the reeds. Boggy fighting, that.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_sloe=turned priority=2] Fen boats bringing grain upriver now, no? Not plunder. That's new.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Somebody walked the river company into the shallows. Dry feet to them.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=saltwell priority=2] Salt and water for the wolves at the ford, #address#. The well gives to those who stand.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=saltwell priority=2] Salt and water went north on every caravan this week. May the well never fail those who carried it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_runner=came priority=2] The runner reached the pool before midnight. May the well never fail that wolf.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Half the cut's gone south to the ford, mm? The cedars can wait. Wheat can't.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_captain=parley priority=2] Old Oak, a captain who parleys. That's a wolf with a reason, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Shade on every wolf at the ford. Oakhaven's sending what it can.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_ford=held priority=2] Larkfield held. Good bark, every one of them.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=frosthollow priority=2] The Captain's a Deepvein wolf. Lamp and pick, I could have told you. Nobody shared oil with Deepvein.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Lamp's thanks to the wolves at the ford. The valley sent rope and lamps, what we had.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_ford=held priority=2] They held the ford in Larkfield. Cold iron, the valley's proud.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=ridgemere priority=2] Everyone's asking what the Chancellor wept over in the Rain Hall. Turns out half the city saw him do it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_writ=read priority=2] The old King wrote it down: the Sump's own peace-keeper keeps the lamp until a Moot. So it was no accident.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_oskar=confessed priority=2] The Chancellor stood before the Council and said it all. The Counting House's debt, the order, the lot.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_bell=lost priority=2] They lost the bell through the ice. The Upper Mere kept it. Some say that's where it belongs.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=ridgemere priority=2] Every wolf hauling on the Upper Mere ropes, blood and bread, the city's waiting to hear that bell.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_writ=read priority=2] A wolf of the road found the writ. The herald read it at noon. Blood and bread, I wept too.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=coldwater priority=2] Hear that? Under the ice. Bright One's tide, it's ringing.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_bell=rung priority=2] Net and line, they raised it! Green as a pike and loud as a gale, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_mere=still priority=2] The whole mere's still. I've never seen it so. Calm water to her.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_bell=rung priority=2] The bell's up and the haulers are home. Calm water to every wolf on the ropes, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=larkfield priority=2] A writ lost for a debt. That's the dearest paper ever bought in Ridgemere, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_bell=rung priority=2] The bell came up out of the Upper Mere. Full weight of a bell!
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=southmeadow priority=2] The old King wanted all of us to choose? Sheaf and sickle, I'd best think what I'll say.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_writ=read priority=2] The writ's found and read. Ripe days for the whole realm.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Our bell, under all that ice. Mud and eels, I'd walk the whole Long River to hear it, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_oskar=fled priority=2] The Chancellor ran down the Fen Road and stopped where Mirebridge used to stand. Even the drowned didn't want him, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_bell=rung priority=2] Our bell's out of the ice. Dry feet to every wolf on the ropes.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=saltwell priority=2] A King writes "let the realm choose", and the Houses hide it in the dark. The Houses hid it, #address#, not the King.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_fenwick=confessed priority=2] The mine captain said it aloud at last. By salt and water, the well remembers, and now so does the valley.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Old Oak. The old King planted something deep before he fell, mm? Now we see the shoot.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_writ=read priority=2] The writ's read. Shade on whoever found it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Our iron's in the bell's yoke. Cold iron for a cold bell. Lamp and pick.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Lamp's thanks to every wolf who went down the mine and was counted up again.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=frosthollow world.mem.nh_fenwick=confessed priority=2] He said it, at the Lamp and Pick. Deep quiet after. Then we drank to Deepvein.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=ridgemere priority=2] Every town's sending its howl to the Moot. Ours goes to whoever kept the peace best.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_moot=midwinter priority=2] The Midwinter Moot! Every post on the Line wants a keeper, and every keeper wants a coat.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_moot=nine_howls priority=2] The Moot of the Nine Howls, they're calling it. Nine towns, one night, one howl.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_dagfinn=stands priority=2] The lamp-keeper will stand at the Moot. A Sump wolf, standing!
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_dagfinn=steps priority=2] The lamp-keeper's stepping back, they say, and asking the Moot to choose. A Sump wolf who doesn't want a crown.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=ridgemere priority=2] Every post on the Line has a keeper now. Blood and bread, I never thought the realm could agree on a howl.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_bell=rung|cracked priority=2] The big thing's going to the city for the Moot. It rang once on the road, they say. On its own.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_moot=midwinter priority=2] A Midwinter Moot, eh? The mere's froze hard, and a howl carries over ice.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=coldwater priority=2] Every wolf standing a post on the Line, calm water to you, eh? We'll hear you from the mere.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_voice=raised priority=2] Coldwater's voice is raised. We'll answer even if no wolf of the road is here. Calm water.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=larkfield priority=2] Our voice to the Moot is bought by deeds, not silver. Scales and silver, that's a market I like.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_moot=midwinter priority=2] A Midwinter Moot. Weights and measures, the coldest market the realm's ever held.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=larkfield priority=2] Every wolf who held the ford, Larkfield howls for you on the Moot night.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=southmeadow priority=2] Southmeadow's voice is ready. A windfall of a Moot, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=southmeadow priority=2] Every wolf who carried a howl south, Southmeadow sings for you. Sheaf and sickle.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=southmeadow world.mem.nh_stone=read priority=2] Whoever read the stone, Southmeadow howls with Mirebridge's name back in it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Mirebridge has a voice again, no? Dry feet to every wolf who carried it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] The drowned heard their names this season. Now they'll hear their howl. Dry feet to you.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=saltwell priority=2] Stand by the pool when the night falls, #address#. Saltwell starts the south road's howl.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=saltwell priority=2] The well's roll has your names in it now, every wolf who sat still. Peace on you.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=oakhaven priority=2] A handful of wolves and one voice. That's a lot of shade for a small grove, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Shade on every wolf who walked the bounds. Oakhaven remembers.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Frosthollow starts the howl at the Pass. Lamp and pick, we'll be heard.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Every wolf who stands at the Pass, Frosthollow keeps your lamp lit.
# <<< Ninth Howl talk, part 2: nh_story lines
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king priority=1] The old King's gone up to the Bright One, and a Sump patrolman keeps the Palace lamp. The herald's sending word to every hearth.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called priority=1] You're new on the roads? The old King's gone up, a Sump patrolman keeps the Palace lamp, and the herald's called a Moot of the nine voices.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning priority=1] You've missed a moon of it. The herald called a Moot, and now the Counting House wants every debtor's howl for their note.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals priority=1] Lamps on the ridges, a captain in grey taking his toll off every wagon, and the Watch's own lists going round. That's the news.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls priority=1] The herald says a Moot needs nine howls, and half the towns sang the burying one at the feast. They're finding the old ones now.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters priority=1] A Moot called, debts fought, lamps put out, the old howls found, and now forty letters chasing a lord who's never home.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights priority=1] Now the Houses are at each other, the fens are full of lights, and a black cloak wants one howl from the Pass to the Waste.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest priority=1] Now the Captain's at the Larkfield ford with every wolf he has, and the harvest with him.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell priority=1] The Chancellor's tears, a writ the Houses buried, and a bell under the Upper Mere ice. The Moot's coming.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot priority=1] The Moot's nearly on us. Every post on the Line wants a keeper, and the Moot sits at midnight on Market Square.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot world.mem.nh_moot=midwinter priority=1] The Midwinter Moot's nearly on us. Every post on the Line wants a keeper, and it sits at midnight on Market Square.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot world.mem.nh_moot=nine_howls priority=1] The Moot of the Nine Howls is nearly on us. Every post on the Line wants a keeper, and it sits at midnight on Market Square.
free
choice Where could a wolf lend a paw? -> nh_help
choice Who's behind it all, do you think? [world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning|signals|howls|letters|lights|harvest|bell|moot] -> nh_who
choice Who ought I to ask about it? -> nh_ask
