# ---- Helpful knowledge, the villain and who to ask (section 4 of cast-and-talk fills these by stage and dialect;
# these plain lines are the floor: they point at real content only, by role)
node nh_help
say Ask at the square. The herald's notices go up on every board. | Look at the board on the square. There's always something wants doing.
# >>> Ninth Howl talk, part 2 (gossip and helpful knowledge; generated, doc 86 §6.4): nh_help lines
# By stage and dialect: where to lend a paw (cast-and-talk §4; W), each town its own (@town lines).
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere priority=2] The Palace wants its word carried to every hearth. The herald hands out the Summons at the Antechamber.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere priority=2] The baker on Market Square is sending bread to the Soup Kitchen for the wake. Carry a basket if your paws are free.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere priority=2] The City Office has more Summonses than clerks. A clerk there wants one walked out to a Rainward farmstead.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=coldwater priority=2] The carter's cart went out on the Oakhaven road and hasn't floated home. Net and line, somebody look below Alder Mere.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=larkfield priority=2] The Summons came on the cart. Carry one on to the looms if you're going: Larkfield wants its own reading, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=southmeadow priority=2] We've had no city word in a long while. Blight take the roads. Bring the Summons south and you'll be stood a cup.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Fen-sure, the city boards are slow. Walk the Summons down the Fen Road yourself and you'll be the first.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=saltwell priority=2] If you carry the city's word, #address#, the far towns want it most. Saltwell has heard nothing since the last caravan.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Camp's on the Alder Mere side, under the windthrown oaks. You'll smell it before you see it, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Carters down from the Pass say there are lamps on the High Road that aren't ours. Cold iron. I'd walk in a pair.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere priority=2] Want the notes? The Pawn and Ledger buys and sells them. Smell the ink: Counting House ink smells of lamp oil.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere priority=2] The City Office still has Summonses to walk out to the Rainward farmsteads. Ask a clerk there; they're short of feet.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=coldwater priority=2] The carters' yard in the city is buying wagon days by night. Somebody's paying to know where our carts go, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=larkfield here.region=larkfield priority=2] Weigh a sack at Longmead and weigh it again at the press. The printer wants the difference in ink, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=southmeadow priority=2] Help a debtor with a day's work and the city counts it paid. A good harvest from a little sweat.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] The Fenshore boats won't carry Counting House chests. Boggy coin, that.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=saltwell priority=2] Bring bread and salt to a debtor's door, #address#. In the old way, a guest's gift cannot be called in.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=oakhaven priority=2] A debt's lighter carried by two. Lend a paw at a debtor's work and see, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=frosthollow here.region=frosthollow priority=2] The mine's short of ore and the note's due. Bring a load down to the mine house and it's one less hold on us.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=ridgemere priority=2] The fish-hall papers smell of fish oil. A real Watch list smells of a Watch House: wet cloaks and old ink.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere priority=2] The Masons' Yard wants stone carried out to the Line posts. The Yard's keeper calls it a gift to the realm.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=coldwater priority=2] Stand on the ridge where they burn and they won't light it. They don't like being seen, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=larkfield priority=2] The camp above Glasswater comes back in threes. Take a friend, and then another, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=southmeadow priority=2] Two long and one short means a wagon going out. Get to it before they do, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Lamps on a ridge want oil. Follow the smell of it uphill, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=saltwell priority=2] Four ridges, four lamps. One wolf on each and the company is blind, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=oakhaven priority=2] There's a lamp-stone on the Alder Mere knoll now. Sit by it of a night and see who comes, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=oakhaven here.region=oakhaven priority=2] The Line post by Alder Mere wants stone and timber, mm? Carry them out and gift them at the post.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Lamps burn on the Upper Mere ridge after the second bell. Go up with your own lamp out.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=frosthollow here.region=frosthollow priority=2] Our Line post wants stone and timber, #address#. Gift them at the post; the city yards send some, never enough.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere priority=2] The herald stands on the square at dusk. Howl with her and the city's howl comes back.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere priority=2] The guard holding the north gate wants the road kept safe for the fair-goers in the feast days. Ask him at the gate.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=coldwater priority=2] The mine captain at Frosthollow wants rope for Highmere. Something under that ice besides the big thing, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=larkfield here.region=larkfield priority=2] The linen master starts the chorus at dusk. Stand by her and it counts.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=southmeadow priority=2] The bee-keeper's honey's what the cellar hand wants. Don't ask why. Nobody ever knows why.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=southmeadow here.region=southmeadow priority=2] The Larkholm farmer starts our chorus at dusk on the square. Stand by her and lift it round and warm, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] The creek at dusk. The eel-trapper sings the first turn there, twice round the reeds.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=mirebridge|fenshore here.region=fenshore priority=2] The stores keeper howls on the boardwalk at dusk. Bring him the scraps you've gathered, no? Ours went thin when Mirebridge went under.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=saltwell here.region=saltwell priority=2] The keeper of our stores starts the howl at the pool when the water is still.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=oakhaven here.region=oakhaven priority=2] Three old roots in town know a piece each. Ask slow, and twice.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Highmere's iced at the edges even now. Haul together or don't haul.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=frosthollow here.region=frosthollow priority=2] The miner who watches the road starts our howl low on the square at dusk. Ask three old ones for the pieces first, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=ridgemere priority=2] Every wharf wolf has a letter for him. Do them a kindness and they'll give it you gladly.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere priority=2] The bounds-walkers in the Rainward Hills want water and bread carried up. The orchard keeper out there sends for it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=coldwater priority=2] If you're walking the bounds, mark the alders too. The old line runs along the water, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=coldwater here.region=coldwater priority=2] A Coldwater carter wants wolves to scout the Pass Road stage before the black cloak walks it. Ask at the carts by the square, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=larkfield priority=2] The Grayrock lady's a Larkfield wolf, did you know? Bring her something from the downs and see her face.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=southmeadow priority=2] Thyme grows on the Larkdowns swells where the sheep don't crop. A windfall, if you know where.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=southmeadow here.region=southmeadow priority=2] Thyme for the Grayrock lady grows on the Larkdowns, not here. Take the Downs Road north, #address#, where the sheep don't crop.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Black cloaks on the Pass Road, they say. Fen-sure they'll want walking down.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=mirebridge|fenshore here.region=fenshore priority=2] A deckhand on the boardwalk wants lamp oil for the fog lamps, no? Honest lamps, these. Not the warm ones in the reeds.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=saltwell priority=2] A letter carried is a debt paid, #address#. Do the carrier a kindness first, and they will give it gladly.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=oakhaven here.region=oakhaven priority=2] Pull the green stakes and bring them to the square. Old Oak, they burn well enough.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=frosthollow priority=2] The cloaks want walking down to the city. Go in a pair, #address#. The Captain's men watch the High Road.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=ridgemere priority=2] A House at odds still eats. Bring its steward bread and salt. It's an old custom and nobody refuses it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=coldwater priority=2] The fen lights smell of lamp oil, they say. No drowned wolf ever carried a lamp, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=larkfield priority=2] The fen boats come up past the ford with no lamps lit. Sold goods, #address#, and not theirs to sell.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=larkfield here.region=larkfield priority=2] Fen boats tie up below the ford after dark. Watch the bank from the mill, #address#, and count what comes off.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=southmeadow priority=2] The stone's names are nine, and one chiselled out. Take that to the fen priest, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] The path with no note, #address#: start at Withy Creek, keep the reeds on your left, and never step where it shines warm.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=saltwell priority=2] The healer at the Sump Infirmary writes to the black cloaks. If a friend carries a Gift, speak for them there, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=saltwell here.region=saltwell priority=2] Bread and salt for a House at odds? Saltwell's stores have the salt, #address#. Carry a measure to the city's stewards.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=oakhaven priority=2] The quarrel's carts go by the East Road. Ride with one and nobody touches it, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=oakhaven here.region=oakhaven priority=2] The board on our square still asks for green stakes pulled from the cut, mm? Read it, then pull one.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=frosthollow priority=2] The black cloak's healer asks after the Gifted. Say what's true and no more, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=frosthollow here.region=frosthollow priority=2] Our Line post still wants stone and timber before the Moot, #address#. Gift them at the post.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=ridgemere priority=2] The ford wants every paw. Take the Downs Road south, and take bread; they're short at the walls.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_toll=bargained priority=2] The Wharf says two Grayrock ships are loading bread for the ford. Somebody bargained well.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=coldwater priority=2] Bring blankets to the ford. Wolves who stand all night want warm backs, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=coldwater here.region=coldwater priority=2] The Glasswater camp creeps back while every paw's at the ford, eh? The Watch in the city pays for it broken again.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=larkfield here.region=larkfield priority=2] They come up the shallows below the mill. The current's slack there after dark, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=larkfield here.region=larkfield priority=2] The looms are sending blankets down to the ford. A loom hand wants them carried, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=southmeadow priority=2] If the Downs Road's held, go round by the vine lanes. Blight take the Captain, he doesn't know them.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=southmeadow here.region=southmeadow priority=2] A relief wagon goes from Larkholm to Larkfield in the siege nights. Walk beside it, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] The Larkfield smith knows a path across any bog. Ask her before the river company does, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=mirebridge|fenshore here.region=fenshore priority=2] The ford's up the Long River from us. Take the river road north from the boardwalk, no? You'll smell the smoke first.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=saltwell priority=2] A runner from the ford wants the caravan arc, #address#. It is the shortest way to the pool.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=oakhaven priority=2] A truce lamp's a truce lamp. Strike under one and the whole of Cedar Sound will know by morning, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=frosthollow priority=2] If he names the mine house, ask the mine captain what he barred, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere priority=2] The Records Office rolls, the cathedral crypt and the Greatly Bank flat. One of them hides it, they say.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=coldwater priority=2] Take a tug rope and oil your coat, eh? And lie flat on the ice. It carries the sound.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=coldwater here.region=coldwater priority=2] The Bakehouse wants bread and smoked fish carried out to the haulers at the Upper Mere shed, eh? Cold paws want feeding.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=coldwater here.region=coldwater priority=2] A Coldwater shepherd wants a wolf to sit a night on the Upper Mere ice and listen, eh? Something rings under there.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=larkfield priority=2] The bell'll want a yoke of good iron. Frosthollow's the only seam deep enough. Scales and silver.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=larkfield here.region=larkfield priority=2] The looms still send blankets down to the ford houses. Ask a loom hand what wants carrying, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=southmeadow priority=2] If you're hauling on the mere, take something hot. A windfall for whoever's next to you.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=southmeadow here.region=southmeadow priority=2] A Larkholm wagon still carries relief north to Larkfield. Walk beside it, #address#; the roads aren't safe yet.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Bring the scattered something from the bell, #address#. A keepsake off the old ferry-raft, and they'll give you a name.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=saltwell priority=2] The keeper of our stores lost a brother at a mine. She has asked which one for years, #address#. Ask Frosthollow.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=oakhaven priority=2] A bell under ice wants a slow pull. Rush it and it cracks, like green wood, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=oakhaven here.region=oakhaven priority=2] The road post by Alder Mere wants stone and timber before the Moot, mm? Gift them there. The printer counts who comes.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=frosthollow here.region=frosthollow priority=2] The mine captain drinks at the Lamp and Pick on Restday. Bring him there if he's got something to say.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=ridgemere priority=2] On the Moot night, listen for the Bay Light bell, then count a hundred breaths. That's when the far howls come in.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere priority=2] The carpenter in the Market Hall wants planks and benches for the Moot on the square. Carry some; the Houses won't.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=coldwater priority=2] The relay's at the old Glasswater camp. Both arms meet there. Bring oil, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=coldwater here.region=coldwater priority=2] The Looms want wolves to walk the bell a stage on its road to the city, eh? Ask a loom hand.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=larkfield here.region=larkfield priority=2] The ford post is ours. Stand with the linen master and lift it at the end like a bid.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=southmeadow here.region=southmeadow priority=2] Our post is the square, second on the south arm. After the pool answers, it's us.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Lamp oil to the crossing three nights running. The true lights answer, fen-sure.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=mirebridge|fenshore here.region=fenshore priority=2] The boardwalk post's ours on the Moot night. Stand it with the stores keeper, oil and a horn, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=saltwell here.region=saltwell priority=2] Our post is the pool. Oil, a horn, and a still heart.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=oakhaven here.region=oakhaven priority=2] Our square's on the trunk, after the road post. Slow and climbing when it comes.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=frosthollow here.region=frosthollow priority=2] The Pass post's by the Pass House. Stand it with the miner who watches the road.
# <<< Ninth Howl talk, part 2: nh_help lines
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king priority=1] The herald wants a Summons carried to every town's Keeper. Ask her at the Great Palace.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called priority=1] Every town has a Keeper taking pledges now. Howl for a town, and every deed of yours carries its voice.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning priority=1] There's chalk on half the doors in the Sump. A wolf who works off a note and asks nothing back is worth ten heralds.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals priority=1] The lamps on the ridges want dousing, and the posts on the Line want stone and timber carried to them.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls priority=1] Every Keeper's hunting their town's old gathering howl. Ask yours. The old ones hold the pieces.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters priority=1] Forty letters for the Grayrock lord, and he's somewhere out on the coast road. The Hall gives them out to carry.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights priority=1] The chapel's priest is gathering names for the drowned, and the fens want wolves who'll walk them carefully.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest priority=1] The Larkfield ford wants every wolf who can stand, and the relief wagons want walkers beside them.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell priority=1] There's a bell under the Upper Mere ice, and a skipper on the shore there who'll want rope hands.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot priority=1] Every post on the Line wants a keeper on the Moot night. Bring oil and a horn.
free
choice Who's behind it all, do you think? [world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning|signals|howls|letters|lights|harvest|bell|moot] -> nh_who
choice Who ought I to ask about it? -> nh_ask
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node nh_who
say Who knows? Somebody with deep pockets, I'd guess. | I keep my nose out of that. You should too.
# >>> Ninth Howl talk, part 2 (gossip and helpful knowledge; generated, doc 86 §6.4): nh_who lines
# By stage and dialect: who is behind it, and warnings (cast-and-talk §4; V, !).
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=ridgemere priority=2] There's a camp on the Oakhaven road that won't starve out. Somebody's feeding it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=ridgemere priority=2] The notice on the Oakhaven board was signed with a grey paw-mark. Nobody signs like that who means well.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=coldwater priority=2] Wet ash on the wind from the Alder Mere side. That's no fisher's fire, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=coldwater priority=2] Don't take the Oakhaven road alone. Something's camped under the oaks, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=larkfield priority=2] Somebody's buying the Oakhaven road off the carters. Fair price? Not to the carters.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=larkfield priority=2] Wagons to the Sound Road go in pairs now. Scales and silver, I'd not send one alone.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=southmeadow priority=2] Carters say the Oakhaven road's got a toll on it now, and no tollhouse.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=southmeadow priority=2] Don't send a cart north alone, neighbour. They wait for the lone ones.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Grey paw-marks on the Oakhaven board, no? Boggy business, signing with a paw.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Keep off the Oakhaven road alone, #address#. Something's sitting on it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=saltwell priority=2] Caravans say the north road has a keeper who is not the Watch. By salt and water, I mistrust a keeper with no face.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=saltwell priority=2] Caravans that walk the north road alone come in short, #address#. Walk in company, or wait for one.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Grey paw-mark on our board. Proper strange. Wolves who sign with a paw don't sign with a name.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Don't walk the Oakhaven road alone. Bark and branch, we've lost a wagon already.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Somebody's paying carters for their days. In Frosthollow we call that buying a road.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Don't take the Pass Road alone, #address#. Lamps where there's no house.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere priority=2] The Counting House master gives every debtor a moon's grace. Grace, he calls it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere priority=2] Don't sign anything the clerks bring round. Chalk washes off. Ink doesn't.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=coldwater priority=2] Counting House pennies at the carters' yard. Deep and dark, those coins swim upstream.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=coldwater priority=2] Don't lend your wagon days to a guard with his badge cut off, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=larkfield priority=2] The Counting House lends with one paw and weighs with the other. Weights and measures, I know a cheat's scale.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=larkfield priority=2] If a clerk asks you to sign for a neighbour, read it twice and sign nothing.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=southmeadow priority=2] The Counting House master wants every howl in the realm. Blight take him, he can't carry a tune.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=southmeadow priority=2] Don't let them chalk your door, neighbour. Scrub it before the moon's up.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] A clerk in the city smells of smoke. Fen-sure, some fires aren't for warming.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Don't take the House's coin for your howl, #address#. Mirebridge sold its say once, and look where it got us.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=saltwell priority=2] The master of the Counting House has never once been thirsty. That is how you know a dangerous wolf.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=saltwell priority=2] Do not pledge your voice for coin, #address#. The well remembers who drew from it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Bark and branch, a lender who wants your howl wants your whole tree.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Don't sell your wagon days, old root. You'll want the road back.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=frosthollow priority=2] The Counting House rider comes up the Pass Road. Lamp and pick, somebody wants his letters lost.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=frosthollow priority=2] If the mine captain offers you a share in anything, count your claws after.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=ridgemere priority=2] Three Houses on every list, they say. One on none. Ask yourself why it needn't pay.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=ridgemere priority=2] The Cinder Gate looks away for a grey paw-mark. Don't trust that gate after dark.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=coldwater priority=2] A captain in grey taking a mark a wagon, eh? Deep and dark, that's a toll with no tollhouse.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=coldwater priority=2] The camp above Glasswater comes back in threes. Don't go in alone, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=larkfield priority=2] Two long and one short. Somebody's selling our wagon days, and the price is a lamp on a hill.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=larkfield priority=2] Don't buy a list from the fish hall. It's short-weighed paper.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=southmeadow priority=2] Somebody in grey keeps the roads now, they say. Wormy sort of keeping.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=southmeadow priority=2] If you see two long and one short, don't wait to count again.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Grey paw-marks on every board now. Fen-sure, he's proud of it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] A lamp you can't see the house behind is a lamp you don't follow.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=saltwell priority=2] A road kept by no one is kept for someone, #address#. Ask who the grey keeper keeps it for.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=saltwell world.mem.nh_captain=named priority=2] Caravans called him the keeper with no face. Now he has a name, they say, and a grey cloak.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=saltwell priority=2] Do not buy secrets that smell of fish, #address#. Sweet water does not smell of anything.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=oakhaven priority=2] A captain of the roads with no road of his own. Windthrown sort of wolf, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Don't walk under a lit knoll, old root. They're watching from up there.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Somebody's lighting lamps on our ridges and it isn't us. Lamp and pick, I'd like a word with him.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=frosthollow priority=2] If you hear two long and one short from a ridge, #address#, you're already seen.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=ridgemere priority=2] The Counting House is buying howls, they say. A penny a throat. Ask yourself what a bought Moot sounds like.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_relay=ran|broke priority=2] The ridge howled back two long and one short on the relay night. That wasn't ours.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=ridgemere priority=2] The Counting House says a bought howl still counts. Buy yours back if you sold it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=coldwater priority=2] Somebody wants the old howls lost, eh? Deep and dark, a Moot with no howl can't sit.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=coldwater world.mem.nh_relay=ran|broke priority=2] False howls off the ridge, two long and one short. Deep and dark, he even steals our singing.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=coldwater priority=2] Don't howl the burying one at a wedding. It's been done. It was awful, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=larkfield priority=2] A howl from the ridge, they say, and it wasn't from any town. Somebody's put a price on our song.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=larkfield priority=2] If you've sold your howl to the Counting House, buy it back. It's worth more than a note.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=southmeadow priority=2] Somebody chiselled a name off the Sunfields stone. Wormy business, that.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=southmeadow priority=2] Don't sing at the stone of a night unless the sky's clear. The cellar hand says so, and she's odd but right.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] The Houses struck Mirebridge off the rolls. Struck it off so the Moot could never sit, they say.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Don't sing the drowned howl on the boardwalk of a night. The old ones don't like it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=saltwell priority=2] A howl that answers from a ridge with no town under it is a mirage, #address#. Do not follow it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=saltwell priority=2] Do not hurry an old wolf's song. Saltwell begins nothing in a hurry.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Somebody's teaching false howls from the ridges, mm? Rotten at the root, that.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_relay=ran|broke priority=2] False howls on the relay night, they say. Somebody's got lamps and a throat.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=oakhaven priority=2] The relay night wants a wolf at every post. One gap and it limps, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Deepvein wolves knew a howl too, once. Nobody's heard it since the deep winter.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Don't go onto Highmere alone, #address#. The ice keeps what it takes.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=ridgemere priority=2] Some of those letters are toll receipts, they say, signed with a grey paw. Grayrock pays the roads to stay shut.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_toll=cried priority=2] The herald cried a Grayrock toll receipt on the square. The Sump cheered. The Wharf didn't.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=ridgemere priority=2] Fell wants the Rainward Hills, and Fell's green is on the wolves driving stakes. Mind the cut.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=coldwater priority=2] Green cloaks and grey lamps, together. Deep and dark, who's paying whom?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=coldwater priority=2] Black cloaks on the Pass Road, eh? Wardens, they say. Fair winds to whoever they've come for.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=larkfield priority=2] Grayrock pays one mark a wagon on the High Road. Scales and silver, to whom?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=larkfield priority=2] Don't take a Fell errand without reading it. Fellhall has more rooms than doors.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=southmeadow priority=2] Fell's green cloaks are driving stakes in Oakhaven's cut. Blight take them.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=southmeadow priority=2] Don't trust a wager in the Fell distillery. The house always drinks first.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Grey paw-marks on the lord's toll receipts. Boggy coin, that.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Don't step between Fell and Oakhaven, #address#. Both sides have axes.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=saltwell priority=2] A House that pays the roads to stay shut buys a thirst for everyone else.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=saltwell priority=2] Black cloaks on the Pass Road, #address#. If you carry a Gift, carry it quietly.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Wolves in Fell green on the cut, and the Captain's lamps behind them. Same paws, different cloaks, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Don't argue with a bounder alone, old root. They come in threes.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=frosthollow priority=2] The Captain's bounders wear Fell green in the west, they say. Grey up here. Same wolves.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Don't lie to a black cloak, cousin. Don't tell them more than's true, either.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=ridgemere priority=2] A black cloak at the Antechamber, and every House shouting. Somebody's glad of the noise.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=ridgemere priority=2] Cudgels in House colours on the roads out of the city. Walk round them.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=coldwater priority=2] Lamp oil in the reeds. Deep and dark, the same lamps as on the ridges.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=coldwater priority=2] Don't follow a warm light in the fens, neighbour. Cold ones only, they say.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=larkfield priority=2] Plunder up the river by night. Weights and measures, somebody's fencing the Captain's take.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=larkfield priority=2] Don't buy cheap wool from a fen boat. You'll be buying it twice.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=southmeadow priority=2] The Captain's southern company wades the fens with float lamps. Wormy trick.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=southmeadow priority=2] If you walk the fens by night, take a friend and a lamp you won't light.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Float lamps in the reeds, fen-sure. The drowned never needed lamps to walk.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] The potter's post went to a carpenter and the boardwalks whisper. Ask the records before you whisper too.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=saltwell priority=2] Lights in the fens, fire in the city, cudgels on the roads. A mirage of three, and one paw behind it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=saltwell priority=2] Do not hide a Gift from the black cloak and then use it in the open, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Cudgels in House colours at the Rainward camps. Proper strange that a House needs a camp.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Don't take sides in the city's quarrel, old root. Take bread.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=frosthollow priority=2] The Captain's company's gone south to the fens. Cold iron, we're glad and we're not.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=frosthollow priority=2] One howl from the Pass to the Waste, the black cloak wants. Our post's first. Don't let it be our fault.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=ridgemere priority=2] The Counting House is buying Longmead grain at siege price. Somebody always profits.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=ridgemere priority=2] Wolves carrying sacks from Longmead to the Counting House. Don't be one.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=coldwater priority=2] Lamp-black at the ford too, they say. Same lamps as on our ridges.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=coldwater priority=2] If the ford burns, the whole realm's short of bread. Help it hold, neighbour.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=larkfield priority=2] The Captain's companies took the Downs Road barns. Weights and measures, he's counted our grain before we have.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_captain=parley priority=2] The Captain parleyed at the truce lamp. A wolf with a reason, and a reason's worse than a price.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=larkfield priority=2] Don't cross the ford after dark unless you're standing it, #address#. Both banks are watching.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_truce=broken priority=2] Somebody struck under the truce lamp. Weights and measures, the whole Downs is talking.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=southmeadow priority=2] The Captain's companies took every barn on the Downs Road. Wormy wolves.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=southmeadow priority=2] Don't wait for a runner if you see smoke from the ford. Go.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] The Captain's a Deepvein wolf, they say, from the high valley. Long way to come for a ford, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Keep off the Long River banks by night. They're all fighting there.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=saltwell priority=2] A captain who parleys has a grievance, not a greed. By salt and water, that is harder to buy off.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=saltwell priority=2] Do not leave the pool unwatched while the south is fighting.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Deepvein, they say. Turned out in the deep winter. Rotten thing to do to a wolf, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Don't go to the ford without bandages, old root.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Deepvein. The deep winter. The mine house door. Black seam, we all knew.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Don't say Deepvein in the Lamp and Pick unless you mean it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=ridgemere priority=2] The Counting House master told the Chancellor to lose it, they whisper. Lose a King's writ!
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=ridgemere priority=2] An old rag-mill hand is selling what she saw. Get there before she gets to the City Office.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=coldwater priority=2] The black cloak watches the mere all day. Deep and dark, what's she looking for?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=coldwater priority=2] Don't walk the black lane on the ice, neighbour. It never freezes, and nobody says why.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=larkfield priority=2] The Counting House hid the old King's writ. Weights and measures, there's a cheat's scale for you.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=larkfield priority=2] Don't go out on the Upper Mere ice alone, #address#. Weights and measures, ice doesn't bargain.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=larkfield world.mem.nh_ford=burned priority=2] Send bread to Larkfield before you send iron to the bell.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=southmeadow priority=2] Somebody bought a King's writ with a debt. Wormy, wormy business.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=southmeadow priority=2] Don't go out on the Upper Mere ice unless the skipper says it holds.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] The Houses struck us off the rolls and hid the King's writ. Same paws, fen-sure.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Don't stamp on the ice when you listen, #address#. The bell's not the only thing under it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_bell=cracked priority=2] They rang it cracked. Don't laugh. It's still ours.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=saltwell priority=2] A Chancellor weeping over a paper means someone made him hold it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=saltwell priority=2] A pup who calls water is a gift and a danger, #address#. Do not hide her carelessly.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=oakhaven priority=2] The Counting House paid for a writ to be lost. Rotten at the root, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Don't trust a sale of secrets on the Sump Stairs. Somebody's paying both ends.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=frosthollow priority=2] On the Moot night the Pass is his, the notice says. The Captain writes like he means it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=frosthollow priority=2] Nobody goes down alone, and nobody comes up without counting the others.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=ridgemere priority=2] The Counting House master says he's already counted his voices. Make sure he's counted wrong.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=ridgemere priority=2] The Captain says the Pass is his on the Moot night. If the north arm fails, the trunk starts short.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=coldwater priority=2] The Counting House has bought howls. A bought howl's a muddied one, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=coldwater priority=2] If the howl stops at the mere post, it's not over. The next post can take it from two back, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=larkfield priority=2] Bought howls go to the Purse, three at most. Weights and measures, that's three too many.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=larkfield priority=2] Don't go to the Moot empty-pawed. Bring oil for a post.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=southmeadow priority=2] The Counting House would crown a debt if it could. Blight take it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=southmeadow priority=2] If the pool's silent, we can still take the howl from two back. Don't give up on it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_lights=faded priority=2] The Council would cast our voice if we're silent. The Council struck us off. Boggy justice.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] The crossing post's out in the open. Don't stand it alone if there are cudgels about.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=saltwell priority=2] A crown bought with debts is a well with salt in it, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=saltwell priority=2] If Saltwell is late, the whole south arm is late. Do not be late, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=oakhaven priority=2] The Counting House would buy every voice in the grove, mm? Rotten at the root.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=oakhaven world.mem.nh_hills=fell priority=2] Oakhaven howls against whoever Fell backs. The hills went to Fell, and we've long roots.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=oakhaven priority=2] If the road post goes quiet, the square can't carry. Fill both, old root.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=frosthollow priority=2] The Captain's band gathers at the Pass the night before. Cold iron, there'll be a fight.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=frosthollow priority=2] If the Pass falls silent, the north arm's two posts short. Don't let it, #address#.
# <<< Ninth Howl talk, part 2: nh_who lines
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning priority=1] Somebody's buying every small note in the Sump. Ask yourself who has that much coin to spare.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals priority=1] A captain in grey, they say. Nobody's seen his face, only his paw-mark on the notices.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls priority=1] Somebody would rather the towns sang the burying howl. A Moot with no voices is a Moot that never sits.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters priority=1] Black cloaks on the Pass, and Grayrock wagons that never get robbed. Make of that what you like.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights priority=1] Every House says another House set the lights in the fens. One of them's telling the truth.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest priority=1] The grey captain wants the ford. Ask who pays for the grain once he has it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell priority=1] The Chancellor wept over a paper, they say. Somebody made him.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot priority=1] Whoever's been buying voices all year will try to buy the Moot. Mind your own.
free
choice Where could a wolf lend a paw? -> nh_help
choice Who ought I to ask about it? -> nh_ask
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node nh_ask
say Ask the herald. She reads what's to be read. | The herald at the Great Palace knows more than she says.
# >>> Ninth Howl talk, part 2 (gossip and helpful knowledge; generated, doc 86 §6.4): nh_ask lines
# By stage and dialect: who to ask (cast-and-talk §4; A), each town its own (@town lines).
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere priority=2] Looking for the wolf with the lamp? Ask on the Sump Stairs. The porters always know who's passed.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere priority=2] A Watch guard means to walk the Sump round the lamp-keeper left. Ask at the Watch Office if he wants company.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere priority=2] The herald takes pledges at the Palace door. Pledge to a town and your deeds carry its howl.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=coldwater here.region=coldwater priority=2] The loom master takes the city's word for the town. If you carry a Summons, it's hers to hear, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=larkfield here.region=larkfield priority=2] The linen master's the one to hear the city's word. She'll weigh it fair.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=southmeadow here.region=southmeadow priority=2] The Larkholm farmer walked to the city once. She'll take the Summons for the town.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=mirebridge|fenshore here.region=fenshore priority=2] The stores keeper takes the city's word for the boardwalks. Mind, he'll argue with it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=saltwell here.region=saltwell priority=2] The keeper of our stores hears the city's word for us. Bring it to her shade.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=oakhaven here.region=oakhaven priority=2] The logger's not the thief they say. Ask her about the wool, and smell her paws, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called self.from=frosthollow here.region=frosthollow priority=2] The miner who watches the road takes the city's word for us. Short with it, but he hears.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=ridgemere priority=2] The Greatly daughter reads in the gardens. They say she's found a sum that won't sit still.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=coldwater priority=2] Ask a debtor what work wants doing. A day's work for a neighbour pays a note in the old way, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=coldwater here.region=coldwater priority=2] The loom master takes Coldwater's pledges for the Moot. Howl for the lake and she'll keep your name, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=larkfield here.region=larkfield priority=2] The printer's making handbills: a debt is not a voice. Ask him for a stack to carry.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=larkfield here.region=larkfield priority=2] The stores keeper weighed his own sack on the market beam and it came up short. Ask him, #address#. He's quiet, but he's counting.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=southmeadow priority=2] The city's herald owes a note herself. Free hers and the whole Moot owes you a cup.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=southmeadow here.region=southmeadow priority=2] The Larkholm farmer takes Southmeadow's pledges for the Moot, #address#. Pledge to us and your good deeds carry our howl.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Want to know who sold whose note? The cells in the city. The keeper there remembers everything.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=mirebridge|fenshore here.region=fenshore priority=2] The stores keeper takes Fenshore's pledges, no? Pledge to the boardwalks and every deed you do howls for us.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=saltwell priority=2] The pawnbroker in the city knows every note, #address#. Bring her a gift; trust is bought slowly there.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=saltwell here.region=saltwell priority=2] The keeper of our stores takes Saltwell's pledges, #address#. Pledge in her shade and your deeds carry the well's voice.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=oakhaven priority=2] The Grayrock wharf office knows which wagons go out by night. The harbourmaster says little, slowly.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=oakhaven here.region=oakhaven priority=2] Ask at the store counter about pledging for the Moot, mm? Somebody there will point you right.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=oakhaven here.region=oakhaven world.mem.nh_logger=cleared priority=2] The logger takes Oakhaven's pledges now, mm? Sap on her paws, not smoke. Howl for us there.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=oakhaven here.region=oakhaven world.mem.nh_logger=believed priority=2] The store takes Oakhaven's pledges while the logger's name stays muddy, mm? Ask at the counter.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning self.from=frosthollow here.region=frosthollow priority=2] The miner who watches the road knows the quota. Ask him, short as he is.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere priority=2] They say the abbot keeps a list too, and shares it only after the Restday service.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere priority=2] The Carters' Yard wants a wolf to walk beside a wagon to Coldwater, past the lit ridges. Ask in the yard.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere priority=2] A Watch guard walks the Sump round the lamp-keeper left, and wants company of a night. Ask at the Watch Office.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=coldwater priority=2] The shepherd at Greyteeth counts lamps from his barn. Ask him why he counts, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=coldwater here.region=coldwater priority=2] The Greenholt carters bring their wagons in by the square. Ask them which nights they saw the lamps, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=larkfield priority=2] The Glasswater road's half ours. Ask the carters which nights the lamps burned.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=larkfield here.region=larkfield priority=2] The Longmead farmer knows which nights the wagons didn't come. He counts sacks, and he counts carts, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=southmeadow priority=2] Ask a carter who's lost a wagon lately. Every one of them saw the lamps first.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=southmeadow here.region=southmeadow priority=2] Our carters wait by the press house. Ask one which ridge lit up when they went north, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] The old ones in Frosthollow say there's a list of who shared lamp oil one bad winter. Ask the city's records.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=mirebridge|fenshore here.region=fenshore priority=2] The Fenshore carter takes the north road twice a week, no? Ask him which ridge he'd not pass these days.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=saltwell priority=2] By salt and water, the shepherd on the Greyteeth counts every lamp. Ask him why he counts.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=saltwell here.region=saltwell priority=2] The keeper of our stores counts every caravan in off the north road, #address#. Ask her which ones came in short.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=oakhaven here.region=oakhaven priority=2] The printer counts every stake and every lamp. Ask her the tally, slow.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=signals self.from=frosthollow here.region=frosthollow priority=2] Ask the miner who watches the road about lamp-black. He knows the smell of it better than he'd like.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=ridgemere priority=2] Want the old howl? Ask the oldest wolf in town, then ask her again. She'll give you half the first time.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=coldwater here.region=coldwater priority=2] The loom master knows the old howl. Catch her on the square at dusk and she'll start it if you'll carry it, eh?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=larkfield here.region=larkfield priority=2] The pot hand at the Sheaf sings the old Mirebridge turn when he's had two. Buy him the second, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=southmeadow priority=2] The cellar hand says the old stone on the Sunfields remembers. She says a lot of things, #address#. Some are true.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=southmeadow here.region=southmeadow priority=2] A young Larkholm farmhand sang the burying howl at a wedding. Now he wants mead and honey for the families. Ask him, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Ask the eel-trappers who came out of Mirebridge. Every one of them has a scrap of the old howl, fen-sure.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=saltwell priority=2] Sit with her on Restday, #address#, three times. The well remembers who drew from it, and the howl remembers who sat still.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=oakhaven here.region=oakhaven priority=2] The keeper starts it low. Don't rush in. A sapling that rushes falls, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=howls self.from=frosthollow priority=2] If the mine captain asks for rope, he's after the old King's silver under Highmere. Lamp and pick, go in a pair.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere priority=2] Want the Grayrock lord? Ask at the Wharf Office which road he took. He's always on one.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=coldwater priority=2] The harbourmaster at the city's Wharf Office grew up on the lake. Ask her kindly and she'll say which road the lord took.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=larkfield here.region=larkfield priority=2] Thyme grows on the downs where the sheep don't crop. The linen master will know the swell.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=southmeadow priority=2] The younger Timberland son's a Southmeadow wolf at heart. He rides out our way. Ask him what Timberland wants.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] The Chapel of the Tide's priest wants names of the wharf drowned. Ask the wharf; it's all wet grief there.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=saltwell priority=2] The healer at the Sump Infirmary grew up at our well. They say he wrote to the black cloaks. Ask him why.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=saltwell here.region=saltwell priority=2] Our stores keeper still takes Saltwell's pledges, #address#. A wolf pledged to the well carries its voice on every road.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=oakhaven priority=2] The quarrymaster's saving for the common right. Ask her what she's short, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters self.from=frosthollow here.region=frosthollow priority=2] The Pass House keeps the cloaks a room. Ask there when they move.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere priority=2] The Records Office rolls have Mirebridge's names, they say, under the Houses' own. Ask the roll keeper.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=coldwater priority=2] The city's Chapel of the Tide priest says names over water. Bring her one and she'll say it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=coldwater here.region=coldwater priority=2] Our stillmaster lost her wine to the fen boats. Ask at the Still what went missing, eh? She'll know it by the smell.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=larkfield priority=2] The Rivermouth skipper's always a little late. Ask her where she's been, and watch her paws.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=southmeadow priority=2] The bee-keeper lost her honey to the fen boats. Ask her what it smelled of.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=southmeadow here.region=southmeadow priority=2] The cellar hand at the press house read the Sunfields stone. Ask her for the chiselled name; the fen priest will want it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] The old one at Withy Creek knows which lights are which. Don't sit with your back to the reeds when you ask.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=mirebridge|fenshore here.region=fenshore priority=2] The Rivermouth skipper ties up at our boardwalk at dawn, late as ever. Ask her what she carried, no? Watch her paws.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=saltwell priority=2] The black cloak speaks only through the healer. Ask him what she asks.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=oakhaven priority=2] The carpenter at the Fenshore pottery's an Oakhaven root. Ask him about the potter's post, slow.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=lights self.from=frosthollow priority=2] If you want the black cloak's question, ask the healer in the city. She won't say it herself.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=ridgemere world.mem.nh_desmond=held priority=2] The magistrate's court hears the dismissed guard's case. Sit in if you've an opinion.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere priority=2] The sergeant at the Watch Office rides with the ford escorts. Ask her when they leave, and bring a lamp you're willing to lose.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=coldwater priority=2] The Larkfield looms are sending blankets to the ford. Ask a loom hand there; they're quiet, but fair.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=larkfield here.region=larkfield priority=2] The smith knows a path across any bog. Ask her for the flank path before the river company finds it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=larkfield here.region=larkfield world.mem.nh_ford=burned priority=2] A Longmead farmhand is sharing grain with the burned-out houses. Ask at Longmead what wants carrying, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=southmeadow here.region=southmeadow priority=2] The Vine and Sickle keeper knows who the Longmead farmer's word is for. Ask her quietly.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Ask the Rivermouth skipper what moves on the river by night. She'll answer, late.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=saltwell here.region=saltwell priority=2] Ask the keeper of our stores when the runner came. She keeps the hour.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=oakhaven here.region=oakhaven priority=2] The Felled Cedar keeper hears the carters. Ask her which roads are open.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest self.from=frosthollow here.region=frosthollow priority=2] The miner who watches the road went quiet when he heard. Ask him why, and wait.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere priority=2] Want the Chancellor's story? Ask the porters on the Sump Stairs. One of them saw the seal on the paper.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=coldwater here.region=coldwater priority=2] The Upper Mere skipper takes bearings. Fish with him first; he doesn't trust city paws.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=larkfield priority=2] Ask the mine at Frosthollow for ore. They count everyone down and up, so go as a party.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=larkfield here.region=larkfield world.mem.nh_ford=burned priority=2] A Longmead farmhand is still sharing grain with the burned-out houses. Ask at Longmead, #address#.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=southmeadow priority=2] The cellar hand says the stone remembers the last Moot. Now there's a writ that remembers it too.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] The eel-trapper at Withy Creek knows the bell's old note. Ask her to hum it.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=mirebridge|fenshore here.region=fenshore priority=2] The stores keeper was a pup when the bell last rang, no? Ask him how it went. He'll hum it, badly.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=saltwell priority=2] The mine captain drinks at the Lamp and Pick on Restday. Bring a friend if you mean to ask him things.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=saltwell here.region=saltwell priority=2] Our stores keeper has waited years to hear which mine, #address#. When the mine captain speaks, carry it to her shade.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=oakhaven priority=2] Ask the Glasswater Inn's cook about the ice. He's seen the big thing move too.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell self.from=frosthollow here.region=frosthollow priority=2] The miner who watches the road wants the lamp-oil list read out. Ask him what it says.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere priority=2] The herald's posted how the voices are counted. It's on the board, plain as bread.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere priority=2] A Watch guard means to stand a Line post all night before the Moot night. Ask at the Watch Office if she wants company.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=coldwater here.region=coldwater priority=2] The skipper keeps the Upper Mere post. Ask him where to stand.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=larkfield here.region=larkfield priority=2] The board says how Larkfield howls and why. Read it before you back anyone.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=southmeadow here.region=southmeadow priority=2] The Larkholm farmer keeps our post. Ask her for a horn.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=mirebridge|fenshore priority=2] Ask on the boardwalk who keeps the crossing post. Somebody always does, no?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=mirebridge|fenshore world.mem.nh_lights=laid priority=2] The eel-trapper at Withy Creek is our Keeper now. Ask her where the crossing post stands.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=saltwell here.region=saltwell priority=2] The keeper of our stores starts it. Stand where she points.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=oakhaven here.region=oakhaven priority=2] The printer keeps the road post. She counts every wolf who comes. Be counted, mm?
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot self.from=frosthollow here.region=frosthollow priority=2] Ask the miner who watches the road what the Captain means to do. He knows the wolves.
# <<< Ninth Howl talk, part 2: nh_ask lines
say[world.mem.nh_stage=king priority=1] Ask the lamp-keeper's patrol partner. She walks the Sump round, and she'll know where he's got to.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called|reckoning|signals|howls priority=1] Ask your town's Keeper. They take the pledges, and they hear everything.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=letters|lights priority=1] Ask the chapel's priest, down by the water. She listens to the wharf, and the wharf talks.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=harvest priority=1] Ask at the Larkfield ford. Anyone there will tell you what they need, and quickly.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=bell priority=1] Ask the skipper on the Upper Mere. He's out on the ice more than anyone.
say[world.mem.nh_stage=moot priority=1] Ask the Speaker. He keeps the Moot's roll, and he'll tell you where a voice is still wanted.
free
choice Where could a wolf lend a paw? -> nh_help
choice Who's behind it all, do you think? [world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning|signals|howls|letters|lights|harvest|bell|moot] -> nh_who
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

# ==================================================================================================================
# The cast's talking paths (cast-and-talk section 3)
# ==================================================================================================================

# ---- Dagfinn Thornham, the lamp-keeper (mirebridge speech)
node nh_df
say Ask, then. I've a round to walk later. | Ask. I'll answer slow.
say[self.from=fenshore] Ask, then. I've a round to walk later, no? | Ask. I'll answer slow, no?
say[self.from=fenshore world.mem.nh_stage=lights] Ask. The fens have ears, no?
free
choice Why aren't you up at the Palace? -> nh_df_why
choice What's the letter you carry? [world.mem.nh_stage=king|moot_called|reckoning|signals|howls|letters] -> nh_df_letter
choice What was Mirebridge like? [world.mem.nh_stage=lights|harvest|bell|moot] -> nh_df_mire
choice Do you think you should stand at the Moot? [world.mem.nh_stage=reckoning|signals|howls|letters|lights|harvest|bell] -> nh_dq
choice If you stand, I'll back you. [world.mem.nh_stage=moot_called|reckoning|signals|howls|letters|lights|harvest|bell|moot] -> nh_back
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
