# ---- The Scattered (Ch 4): a scrap of Mirebridge's howl from each (story-heard: one scrap a resident a wolf)
node nh_scrap
say Mirebridge? I've a little of it. Here. It goes like this.
say[self.id=tn_mb_aspen_marshholm self.from=larkfield] Mirebridge? Scales and silver, I left it at six. Here's what my mother hummed.
say[self.id=tn_mb_thorn_marshditch self.from=larkfield] That's my second cup, so you're in luck. Here it is, once. I'll not sing it twice.
say[self.id=tn_mb_tansy_eelbridge self.from=larkfield] I can find a path across any bog, and a tune across any reed bed. Here's the turn the trappers used.
say[self.id=tn_mb_roan_pikewater self.from=fenshore] Dry feet. A scrap? Here's the whole of the second turn, no?
say[self.id=tn_mb_tamsin_eelbank self.from=fenshore] Don't sing it near the reeds. Here. Quietly.
say[self.id=tn_mb_oriel_marshditch self.from=saltwell] Peace on you. I left as a pup. I have only the last note. It is the loudest.
say[self.id=tn_mb_bramble_bogditch self.from=saltwell] The old turn? Sit first. Sit still. There. It goes like this, slow as the well fills.
say[self.id=tn_mb_fell_miremore] I remember the words, not the tune. Here are the words.
mood calm
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

# ---- Pledges and backings (cast-and-talk 3.20), story-heard: the chapter reads the target for the town or the backing;
# a second pledge or backing in a chapter is refused by the story, so the reply is said either way
node nh_pledge
say #thanks#. Carry our howl far.
say[self.id=rmx_brenna_abbot] Then Ridgemere's howl is yours to carry as well as mine. #thanks#. Walk it far.
say[self.id=tn_cw_fallow_lakewick self.from=coldwater] Still water. You'll howl for the lake? Good. The city never asks the lake anything, eh?
say[self.id=tn_mb_aspen_marshholm self.from=larkfield] Sold, to Larkfield! Fair price to you. Carry our voice and I'll weigh it in gold.
say[self.id=tn_sm_iris_meadowfield self.from=southmeadow] Good harvest! A wolf howling for Southmeadow. I walked to the city once. Now the city walks to us.
say[self.id=tn_mb_roan_pikewater self.from=fenshore] Dry feet. Fenshore's howl's a wet one. Fen-sure you'll carry it?
say[self.id=tn_fh_thistle_stonepick self.from=saltwell] Peace on you, #address#. Saltwell's voice is yours to carry. The well remembers who drew from it.
say[self.id=cty_ulla_rusthand self.from=oakhaven] Shade on you. Howl for Oakhaven, then. Slow and climbing, mm?
say[self.id=cty_ulric_stonevein self.from=frosthollow] Warm hearth. Frosthollow's voice goes low. Carry it low, cousin.
say[self.id=rm_imogen_nailridge] A pledge for a village that isn't on the rolls. I'll write you in the margin of my survey, where it still is.
say[self.id=tn_mb_skye_eelbank self.from=fenshore] Dry feet! Mirebridge's voice, carried by a wolf who isn't drowned. That's two of us, no?
say[self.id=tn_cw_myrtle_stillford self.from=coldwater] Calm water. For Coldwater? I'll keep your name with the loom master's.
say[self.id=tn_sm_dun_harvestley] For Larkfield? I'll print your name in the margin, small. Larkfield likes it small.
say[self.id=tn_sm_rusk_plummeadow self.from=southmeadow] Ripe days! Southmeadow takes your howl and gives you a cup for it.
say[self.id=cty_jory_corncroft self.from=fenshore] Dry feet. Fenshore's howl, kept by a carter till the Keeper's back. Fen-sure I'll carry it on the cart with the rest, no?
say[self.id=cty_lavinia_mudworth self.from=saltwell] Water and shade to you. Saltwell has a new voice, and a loud one, I hope.
say[self.id=tn_oh_cairn_oakhaven] Oakhaven, then. We're few. Howl for ten.
say[self.id=tn_fh_aster_coldfell self.from=frosthollow] Hearth to you. Frosthollow's, then. Don't let them hear you in the city.
say[self.id=rmx_corra_coldridge] For Ridgemere, while the herald can't? Bright One, yes. I'll write your name in the usher's book, nice and big.
say[self.id=tn_mb_tamsin_eelbank self.from=fenshore] Dry feet. For Mirebridge. The drowned will hear you. Don't sit with your back to the reeds.
mood pleased
choice I was wondering about something else... -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node nh_back
say #thanks#. I'll remember who stood with me.
say[self.id=rmx_dagfinn_thornham self.from=fenshore] Then you'd be backing a patrolman. Fen-sure, I'll try not to make you sorry.
say[self.id=rm_ottilie_harrowgate] Then back the petitions, not me. I'll carry them either way.
say[self.id=rm_gerrit_mudhand] The Moot itself? By the forge and the sea, the roll is glad of you. A Moot that sits every year, and no crown to fight over.
say[self.id=rm_edric_kelpham] The House thanks you, and so does its steward. The steward rather more quietly.
mood pleased
